R {  670} {0} {<178>} {The Dining Area} {<278>###<088>} {  This dining area is very quaint. There are dozens of small, round tables, and over each table has been draped a crisp, white tablecloth. Every table is  surrounded by six chairs. At the center of each table sits a small white  vase, filled with roses of varying colors. The eastern and southern walls  contain evenly-spaced picture windows that occur approximately every four  feet. Chunky, square pillars hold up the ceiling at widely spaced intervals,  and the style of the ceiling here is wood planked and open beam. The floor is covered with an ornate carpet that must be horrible to have to clean. The  windows have been dressed-up with bright red curtains that complement the  carpet nicely, since it does have some elements of a similar red hue in its  design. } {nursing} {} {castle} {} {1.000} {}
