R {  672} {0} {<178>} {The Kitchen} {<178>[ ]<088>} {  Several large cauldrons are suspended over a hearth in the middle of the room here; hot and bubbling with soups and stews. Since the cooking is done over  an open fire, the walls and floor have been made of stone, in order to reduce the risk of a fire, and the smoke is vented out through a large chimney. There are a few wooden tables, built high, so that anyone standing at them  can prepare ingredients for a meal. Many ingredients sit out on these tables  at the moment, so it appears as if a meal is in the midst of being prepared. The rest of the food must be stored within the various pantries, barrels, and cupboards that line the walls. } {nursing} {} {chesswhite} {} {1.000} {}
E {  671} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  673} {0} {<278>} {Jack's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Jack's room is an interesting place. It's certainly not decorated the way  most people would decorate a room. There are oval-shaped mirrors that run  along the walls, in intervals. Between the mirrors, face-masks of various  animals have been hung. Perhaps he took a recent visit to Masquerade Island. The floor is covered in an exotic-looking rug that contains a myriad of  designs in a rainbow splash of color. A potted palm plant sits in one corner  of the room, and two yellow leather-upholstered club chairs have parked  themselves across from the bed. Every resident gets a basic room that comes  with a bed supplied by the nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the  room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an inch thick, installed vertically for the walls,  and thicker boards for the floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {  664} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  674} {0} {<278>} {Glaadys' Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Glaadys' room is simple and neat. She has a table and chairs off to one side  of the room, and on top of the table is a crystal dish that is filled with  freshly baked cookies. The furthest wall from the door has a firm beige couch that is topped with many plush beige cushions. On the walls hang quaint  paintings and drawings of horses and cottages. Beside the bed there is also a tall wooden wardrobe where Glaadys stores her clothing. Every resident gets a  basic room that comes with a bed supplied by the nursing home. They are  encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal  touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an inch thick,  installed vertically for the walls, and thicker boards for the floor and  roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {31988} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  675} {0} {<278>} {Phil's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Wow, this room is a busy place! Dozens of gadgets that somehow run on their  own are humming and buzzing about in here. There are little machines that  look like bugs which are rummaging through a pile of small, scrap bits, and  sorting them into separate baskets. Several shelves are filled with rolled-up scrolls that make an individual wonder what sort of plans for machines are  written-out upon them. The most complete looking invention in here is a  marble machine that sends a marble on an interesting journey if it is placed  upon it. There are several other large objects that look about halfway to  completion. This causes one to ponder, does Phil ever actually finish his  creations, or does he move on to a new one every time he gets bored or  frustrated? Every resident gets a basic room that comes with a bed supplied  by the nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove  boards an inch thick, installed vertically for the walls, and thicker boards  for the floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {31984} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  676} {0} {<228>} {A Dusty Wagon Trail} {<228>, `<088>} {  The broken cobblestones of the Blessed Aylorian Highway give way to something a little bit softer; the rocky road disappears, the stones either buried or long ago torn up, leaving a wide trail of black dirt.  A little puff of dust rises with every footstep.  Ruts have sunk into the road, as far apart as the length of an average wagon axle, and thick, impassable forestry lines either side of the trail.   } {childsplay} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
