R {  679} {0} {<228>} {A Bridge on the Wagon Trail} {<228>, `<088>} {  The drought theory is dispersed upon arrival at this arched bridge of weatherworn wood.  It allows travelers following the trail to cross over a wide, if shallow, brook without getting wet, and the stream, as sparkling and clear as crystal, babbles along merrily with no signs of a water deficiency.  Footprints formed of both dirt and mud trail across the boards of the bridge, and there are even some on the protective railings.  Most of the footprints seem rather small, even child-sized.   } {childsplay} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {  680} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
