R {  684} {0} {<278>} {The Entrance to the Mines} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The trail widens into a large dirt clearing within the forest, several wagons parked along its grassy border.  The horses and mules attached to them are exhausted, with their ribs poking outward sharply at their sides.  Opposite the trail is a large, rocky hill, the first of many.  However, this particular hill has a gaping black hole in its side, and a hinged wooden door attached to it.   } {childsplay} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
