R {  692} {0} {<228>} {The Entrance to a Village} {<228>, `<088>} {  The trees gently part to either side of the immaculate laid stone path underfoot.  Just before the village is a high arch that curves over the path, carved from polished, golden hardwood.  The detail is exquisite, with vines and four-petal flowers carved all along the structure's sides.  The arch itself is broken; a few stray pieces left on it indicate that the wood used to form letters.   } {childsplay} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
