R {  702} {0} {<278>} {A Cluttered Shoppe} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Young Harriet took over this shop when Lord Peter conquered the village, and she maintains it with a wisdom beyond her youthful years.  Still, she's just a kid, and what kid likes to clean?  Not young Harriet, that's for sure.  The wares she offers are tossed onto the white (now greying) board shelves every which way, the floor hasn't been swept in ages, and cobwebs are thick over the ceiling corners.   } {childsplay} {} {inside} {shop} {1.000} {}
E {  694} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  703} {0} {<178>} {The Village Smithy} {<178>~ ~<088>} {  Despite a lack of walls, the air in the vicinity of this smithy washes over folks in waves of heat.  The forge roars with the crackling blaze it contains, and the sharp odor of red hot metal invades one's nostrils to the point that it can almost be tasted.  Hammers, anvils, and iron shapers are hung neatly on a rack of hooks near a chestnut tree.   } {childsplay} {} {ice} {} {1.000} {}
E {  695} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  704} {0} {<278>} {The Village Doctor's Office} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Soft beige paint on the walls creates a soothing atmosphere in what can understandably be a nerve-wracking experience.  Going to the doctor is rarely an enjoyable event, after all.  Still, the anatomical charts and metal instruments hanging on the walls aren't exactly comforting either.  A high cot in the center of the office includes restraints in case a patient needs help in keeping still during medical procedures.   } {childsplay} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {  696} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  705} {0} {<278>} {A Cluttered House} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Dust and cobwebs predominate here, for certainly the children who occupy this house aren't going to clean voluntarily.  Cupboard doors hang open, or on broken hinges, a carpet of toys almost hides the floor, and dirty dishes covered in fuzzy green mold are piled high in the kitchen sink.  There isn't anything left clean in the entire house.   } {childsplay} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {  698} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  706} {0} {<228>} {A Meadow Path} {<228>, `<088>} {  Although grass attempts to grow here now and then, the steady tromping of feet going between the village and the meadow keeps the path fairly clear and firm.  It passes between a series of houses before the village gives way to thick aromatic forest on each side of the trail.  The sounds of a babbling brook become louder, and the aromatic scent of a flowering lea becomes stronger, as one proceeds north.   } {childsplay} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
