R {  722} {0} {<278>} {The Dais} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  On this high dais is where Lord Peter and his 'court' reside over their minions.  A shorter table than those in the rest of the hall is here, with just three available seats.  Oddly, the grandest of those chairs is the one reserved for the little lord's second-in-command, Vachese, rather than for Peter himself.   } {childsplay} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {  719} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  723} {0} {<278>} {The Kitchen} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This kitchen is very large, built in anticipation of cooking entire feasts to feed dozens, if not hundreds, of people.  The kitchen staff are kept busy at almost all hours; they rest only in the very wee hours of the night before arising once more to prepare breakfast.  From the looks and smell of things, it seems that Lord Peter has acquired an adequate cook.  Certainly, his minions are not lacking for decent food.  Pity the staff don't keep the kitchen clean though; the place is a salmonella outbreak waiting to happen.   } {childsplay} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {  721} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {  724} {0} {<228>} {A Brookside Cranny} {<228>, `<088>} {  The water in the deep brook that runs from east to west through the meadow is as clear as crystal, and the reddish-brown sand and rocks that form the streambed can easily be seen.  The water moves along quite rapidly, the current strong enough that swimming could very well be dangerous.  The brook seems to sing as it burbles along merrily, providing drinking water essential for the survival of the village.  Here we have a tiny inlet surrounded by elm trees as wide as a man, where the water calms enough to create a tranquil pool just north of the brook itself rushing by.   } {childsplay} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {  710} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

