R {  889} {0} {<278>} {Gateway to the horse pasture} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You are at a gateway of sorts. The Alehouse extends over the land you occupy  and comes down once again on the eastern side of this little path, supported  by what must be a small collection booth. Before you is a simple fence. The  only purpose this fence serves is to keep the horses of the Alehouse patrons  from wandering off or being stolen with absolutely no effort. Here, the  section of fence immediately before you is replaced with a wooden gate on a  pair of rusty iron hinges. Clearly, this is the entrance to the horse  pasture. The smell of horses, to no big surprise, grows stronger. The booth  features an open window facing you, and a small door in the back, visible  through the window. A sign hangs under the window reading "Horse storage - 20 gold" The only exits worth noting are to the pasture to the north, and back  to the south, towards the entrance of the Alehouse. } {alehouse} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
