R {  926} {0} {<148>} {In the stockroom} {<148>. .<088>} {  You are in the basement of the Wayward Alehouse. It is a big, open room,  serving as the establishment's wine cellar and stockroom. The floor here is  dirt, not wood like it is upstairs, and makes virtually no sound when one  takes a step. A large pillar in each corner of this vast, square cavern,  holds up the Alehouse above, as well as four similar pillars closer to the  middle of the cavern. All along the four walls of the stockroom barrel upon  barrel of wine and ale sits, waiting for somebody to come retrieve it. The  floor is littered with boxes stacked on top of boxes, all filled with bottles of booze. You can see clearly from one side of the cavern to the other. Rats  scurry back and forth across the ground as they look for food and cover. The  only obvious exit from this giant cavern is back up through the trapdoor, to  the Alehouse proper. } {alehouse} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
