R { 1126} {0} {<238>} {The Bridge Over Kettermoor Crick} {<238>===<088>} {    The rushing waters of Kettermoor Crick flow far below this sturdy stone bridge. In the miserable old days, the people that first settled this godsforsaken scar of land built the bridge to access Fellchantry-- the squat, sprawling island that sits astride the river like the biggest bully in the schoolyard. Or so they say anyway... Really, it'd make just as much sense if they built the bridge to give themselves something high enough to jump from. Fellchantry isn't what you'd call a vacation spot. The water is colder and darker than a witch's heart. The fog-- like a mourner's veil-- stretches perpetually over the land, as if the sun just can't eat a big enough breakfast to ever cook it off. This is where dreams go to die.    To the west the Crickbridge Road leads away from town. To the east the city of Fellchantry looms, looking like the saddest verse of the most dismal dirge you've ever heard. If the word on the street is true, then the murdered smith is somewhere inside, his body giving off the putrescent stench of a mystery. } {chantry} {} {bridge} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1127} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 1125} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1127} {0} {<278>} {Fellchantry Square} {<278>. .<088>} {  Here, filled with all manner of sights and smells, is Fellchantry Square. In the constant hell of the Barony, this is where the honest (and you have to be flexible on your definition here) citizens come to gossip, barter, and conduct their necessary business. The square is a microcosm of the city\; all cramped buildings, bustling crowds, and narrow side streets. A guy could get lost with the slightest wandering from the beaten path, and he probably wouldn't like where he ended up. The only thing less welcoming than Fellchantry's main streets are its back alleys.     The spikes of the raised Kettermoor gate loom to the west like a dragon waiting for a snack. From all other directions the cramped chaos of the square presses in. } {chantry} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1132} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
