R { 1128} {0} {<278>} {Fellchantry Square} {<278>. .<088>} {  The presence of the barony's courthouse to the north does nothing to curb the traffic of the usual ne'er-do-wells and cutthroats here. For the majority of the Justiciars-- Fellchantry's city guards-- the pay just isn't good enough to really make an effort. The occasional drunk gets roughed up, and a murderer may even be arrested if he's a little too indiscrete, but in the end it's just keeping up appearances. Who cares about a murder when no one misses the deceased? Besides, everyone in Fellchantry is guilty of something.    Justice waits to the north, longing for someone to avenge the slander done to her name. The square looms predatorily to the east and south. } {chantry} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
