R { 1134} {0} {<278>} {Fellchantry Square} {<278>. .<088>} {  Most of the traffic at this intersection of the square is either coming from or going toward the south. The third most corrupt organization in the city (after its government, and its law enforcement) has its guild hall in that direction, and with the recent trade talks announced by the Baron there are plenty of foreigners and citizens alike who feel the need to visit the Merchant's Guild. Hatred and bigotry wash from Fellchantry's citizens in a palpable wave toward the outlanders with their strange features, strange clothing, and strange ways. Likewise in a southerly direction are the homes of some of Fellchantry's more affluent, non-royal citizens, as well as several other guild halls. There is even said to be an assassin's guild, but who can afford to believe everything they hear?       Affluence is to the south, along with all the dark deeds it can buy. The press of stinking bodies in the square is all around. } {chantry} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
