R { 1148} {0} {<278>} {La Rochelle Row} {<278>. .<088>} {  A welcome break from the square, buildings of stone and layered over with  plaster cascade in varying shapes and forms towards the south. Beddings and  pots provide a surprisingly lush fauna in reflection to the denizens which  march these cobblestone ways - lords and ladies by any given right, all  marred with some deformation or another which tells of their past during (or  perhaps prior to) their stay within Fellchantry. Surely the Barony had seen  no opulence like this since Valkur himself had fallen.   To one's north they would find their gaze fixated upon the many bodies which  traffic Fellchantry Square, while southwards the opulence continues. Many  structures present the grace and presence of emulated royalty, though some  find themselves distinguished from others via eye-catching entrances and bold gatherings before their respective halls. } {chantry} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
