R { 1417} {0} {<278>} {Trial of Light} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The third trial, the Trial of Light, takes place inside a small crystalline chamber.  A clear glass chandelier hangs from the center of the chamber's ceiling.  The blinding light in this room is provided solely by the light spirit, Lucindra.  The walls of the edifice reflect and deflect Lucindra's effervescent power, as the entity is made of pure light.  The air in the chamber is remarkably clear: there is no scent, no wind to take away from the splendor of Lucindra and her chamber.  Your hand passes over one of the flawless glass walls, and you feel as if somewhere through this glass lies an escape or a path to freedom.   } {amazon} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1418} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1418} {0} {<278>} {Trial of Energy} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Although the crystalline chambers of Lucindra's chamber have left you hard of seeing, you move on to the fourth trial: the trial of energy.  Upon the death of the light spirit, you passed through the crystal walls hoping to find an exit, but instead find yourself in a swirling mass of energy.  You feel the synaptic forces tearing at your mind and soul, threatening to rip you asunder.  Slowly you are able focus your thoughts on the task before you, and bit by bit you regain control of yourself.  The energy is as thick as honey, and only by 'swimming' are you able to move about.  Flashes of purple and green are occasionally seen, and you attempt to move yourself in that direction.  After what seems to be years of travel, you arrive at the source of the power: a medium sized man who waits to challenge you.   } {amazon} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1419} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1419} {0} {<278>} {Trial of Death} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  An endless void surrounds you in all directions\; nothing but endless blackness everywhere you look.  The only sound is your own heart, which begins pumping faster and faster as you come to the realization that there are no landmarks to guide you.  This place has no ceiling, no floor, no walls.  You can only float aimlessly, hoping to somehow find the final guardian.  After hours upon hours of wandering, you see two tiny points of grey in the blackness.  As you approach the source of the odd color, you are met by the force of death itself.  This is the final, most terrible trial, and if you survive, you will truly be among the strongest adventurers in the world.   } {amazon} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
