R { 1420} {0} {<278>} {The Castle Kitchen} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The Annex to the Great Hall is better remembered for its smell than its looks.  The grey stone walls seem to be rotting, and in places the rocks have shifted and fallen.  Yet the castle chefs are too busy cooking and baking goodies to care.  Three dirty brick kilns flare in three corners of the dusty kitchen, while a well and basin are situated in the fourth.  The rooms center contains a huge fire-blackened pit for general cooking: right now 3 kettles of soup are simmering, giving off an aroma of onions, cheeses, and various spices.  Six roast pheasants lie on several silver platters on a nearby table.  Everyone seems busy bustling around, getting ready to serve Queen Melosa's guests.   } {amazon} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
