R { 1720} {0} {<148>} {The Bottom of the Mine Shaft} {<148>. .<088>} {  The rock is gravelly here, a thin layer of dirt covering the hard rocky ledge.  The hard consolidated rock here is the sole clue that the tunneling has descended to the bedrock layer of the volcano.  There are no gems here, no gleam off the wall - the faceless walls give away nothing, and yet the dwarves chip tirelessly away at them.  The temperature is oppressive here, the heat lending another aspect of menace to the already dismal trip down the volcano's tunnels.  A slim exit has been carved out of the forbidding walls to the east and another to the south.   } {hoard} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
