R { 1721} {0} {<148>} {A Narrow Tunnel} {<148>. .<088>} {  The walls converge on each other, but visibility is obscured by the dimness of the light and the dust-mist created by speckles of rock and gravel.  The stony surroundings resemble nothing on earth so much as an avalanche.  No craggy cliffs or romantic figures here - the abrasive stone has eroded away all sign of humanity.  An ominous groan from the depth of the maze-like tunnels threatens to release more fragments of wall and ceiling to further narrow the almost-invisible path.  There is but a faint outline of the tunnel widening to the east, while all around the dwarves continue eroding the walls of the mine, some already flagging in energy.   } {hoard} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1722} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 1720} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1722} {0} {<148>} {A Precarious Ledge} {<148>. .<088>} {  Suddenly, the rock wall to the north and the east fall away into nothing. No dwarves dare pass further than here; the tunnel is barely there, formed by the cascades of rock.  The tunnel becomes a ledge, the edges horrifyingly cracking and bits of rock plummeting into the bubbling pools of lava.  The passageway is narrow; too narrow to pass without a constant fear as to whether the next footstep will prove too treacherous a step to take.  The dull glow of the lava casts damning glows on the uneven walls, eerie shadows leaping and dancing ghostly dances to strike fear into the hearts of all who must pass.  The only way is south - to the last room before the volcano ends and the fire starts.   } {hoard} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1726} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 1726} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
