R { 1723} {0} {<148>} {The Heart of the Volcano} {<148>. .<088>} {  The heat climbs from oppressive to meltdown temperatures here, as the air simmers.  No one can stay in here long without experiencing faintness of body and soul, so intense is the anger of the lava on the walls that contain it.  The polar opposite of the cold outside - the heat so desired by those in the cold threatens to destroy everything in its wake and inflict its wrath on all the poor hapless beings in its path.  Destruction is its name and fire is its weapon, heart, and soul - a terrible firestorm waiting to wreak havoc on earth if any are fool enough to release it from its rocky hell.   } {hoard} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1722} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1724} {0} {<148>} {A Claustrophobic Space} {<148>. .<088>} {  The air has been consumed, or so it seems - not one mouthful of oxygen has been spared for any who would venture farther.  The walls seem to move closer together, inch by inch, as the passage winds down into the depths of the volcano.  Rocks jut out of the wall in yet another attempt to hinder the path, to ensnare the unwary and lure them to inescapable doom.  One misstep could potentially lead to a slide down to the liquid fire pools that beckon the careless.   } {hoard} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1720} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 1725} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1725} {0} {<148>} {Before a Mine Collapse} {<148>. .<088>} {  The fate of the complacent is evident in this room - rocks have sealed off the path they have taken, their uncalculated steps triggering a domino-like collapse of part of the tunnel.  The collapse almost seems to have occurred to spite those who would persevere further, blocking off what seems to be the only way down to the secrets the volcano has hidden.   } {hoard} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
