R { 1727} {0} {<218>} {Inside a Magma Tube} {<218>` <118>,<088>} {  The viscous yellow lava coats the walls of this tunnel, evidence of the volcano's active days.  Now the volcano lies dormant, and no lava spurts out from here, but if the volcano were to wake, the fury of the lava would release itself through the multitude of magma tunnels carved out of the bedrock, channels for erupting the liquid fire lava.  The volcano has lain dormant longer than any dwarf in residence here can recall, and the occasional rumble from the depths is the sole reminder that in the bowels of this volcano, a sleeping dragon lies.   } {hoard} {} {hell1} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1726} {u} {open u;u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 1728} {d} {open d;d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1728} {0} {<218>} {The Burning Core} {<218>[ ]<088>} {  This is the belly of the volcano, the well where lava bubbles.  The lava pools on the upper layers of the volcano pale in comparison to this vast expanse of seething liquid.  The rock seems so fragile, so destroyable in the face of the blazing heat.  This is but the outer core, shielding the inner core - the heart of the volcano.  Who knows what gems lie there, that may satisfy even Tbir's seemingly unquenchable greed?  If the dwarves dared brave the bone-melting heat of the outer core, they would surely try to conquer the last mystery of the volcano.  The molten lava, gem-like in its purity and bright surface, sends an unmistakable message to all who survived thus far - Stay away.   } {hoard} {} {hellinside} {} {1.000} {}
