R { 1961} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mRaider Gathering Place[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You stumble into a domed room. A magical light source hovers above your  head, surely once the belonging of some other clan. In the center of the  room stands a huge table littered with the loot from invaded enemies. Eye  patches, hooks, anchors and bottles of rum lay discarded in a corner.  On the walls hang tapestries, banners and various other items stolen from  some imperial stronghold. To your right you see an entire rack of wizardly  items, decorated with the ears of annoying bards. Side by side like pairs  of pixie wings, richly decorated cultists robes hang. Adjacent these,  the cloak of some unfortunate assassin hangs, like the dead weight from  a hangmans noose. In a tidy pile of Viking helms to your left, stands  a table upon which fine cloaks of dragon skin lay. Their iridescent scales  shimmer with the reflected light. You suddenly freeze where you stand as  you feel someone breathing down your neck. You turn to see a huge drow with red eyes staring at you. You can almost feel his cold gaze starring deep  into your heart, awakening the fear within!  } {retri} {} {inside} {bank,safe,shop} {1.000} {}
E { 1960} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1962} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mStanding Before the Throne of Taboo[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You enter a huge room with walls stained in blood. Fires blaze in the room, and in the center of this chamber you see an enormous throne upon which is seated the deity of this clan. A nimbus of flames flicker around the mighty throne of Taboo. Before the great seat of power, skulls and bones of the weak and pathetic lay shattered, as blood flows from beneath, and the fires of Hell blaze round. The flaming plumes dance like maddened men around the throne of the mighty Taboo, the embodiment of clan Retribution. You stand here, small and pathetic, in his great present, holding your weapon in a white-knuckled grip. Adrenaline courses through your body as the great god himself turns his gaze upon you. He opens his mouth, and his words beat into your brain and being as the sound of a ten thousand men marching, WHO DARES DEFY THE MIGHT OF RETRIBUTION? Your pulse quickens, and your whole being trembles in his presence. Through the skulls, blood, and viscera laying shattered in the room, you notice an armed and armored figure approaching. Now is your time, prove yourself worthy of being within these halls of the Great Clan Retribution! } {retri} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 1960} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1963} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mWalking Down the Memory Lane[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You enter a room chiseled out of the cold stone upon which moisture  condenses and falls from the cold walls like tears from ones eye. You  understand that this is no ordinary place, this is a monument to raiders  past. Engraved in the stone in the chamber are the names of raiders long gone but unforgotten. It is here Clan Retribution honors those who have  served her well. You feel the presence of great raiders who once walked  within the Halls of Retribution, those who once were outcasts and shunned  by kin. They may have forgotten, but Retribution will not! Forever we shall stand proud and remember those who were our friends in arms, our  compatriots, part of the clan! To none shall we bow, and such we have never done! The light on many candles flicker as a cold draft blows through the  room, whispering the names from the past. And you feel a strange energy  approaching, moving about in the room. A spirit of the past moves towards  you, her kind and gentle eyes soothing } {retri} {} {inside} {safe,questor} {1.000} {}
E { 1960} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 1964} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mLazarus Crypt[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A mottle of odors reaches your nostrils as you enter the small crypt.  A large table stands in the middle of the room filled with open bottles, animal corpses, body parts and many strange items.  At then end of the room is a large fireplace with a cauldron suspended above the burning blaze.  As small puffs of smoke now and then arise from the boiling cauldron, each time sending out a foul smell in the room.  You notice a sudden move by the fireplace, and a robed creature turns around, looking up toward you then returning its gaze to the cauldron.  You realize that you have entered the crypt of Lazarus, the Dark Monk.  Along the walls, shelves are ladened with small jars, bottles, vials filled with unknown contents.   } {retri} {} {inside} {safe,shop,healer} {1.000} {}
