R { 4394} {0} {<278>} {The Plaza} {<278>. .<088>} {  Around you great stone walls tower into a deep darkness, rising like the  curved hall of some great stone ship long lost to the land. Around the tower  walls are built wooden shops, homes and workships, clustered in no sane order but rather built haphazardly, like a manmade growth upon the dark stone  walls. Chanting mages walk around the plaza, lost in their books and orbs of  magic. They stir raw magic in their footsteps, changing plants and weeds into fantastic butterflies and then back again. Their mutterings, in no tongue  spoken by an earthly mouth, causes the air to shimmer with visions of other  worlds, other times, other realities. Clearly, to live here is to challenge  yourself to stay both sane and humanoid. To your far north, over the streets  and houses, you can see a great staircase rising against the wall of the  tower. To your south is the great gates of the tower proper. To the west a  small dark passage slinks off into the blackness, and to the east, you can  hear the noises of sleepers, and quiet chatter. } {mistridge} {} {city} {shop} {1.000} {}
