R { 4495} {0} {<148>} {The North Courtyard} {<148>. .<088>} {  The courtyard here is a little bit bigger than the tunnel to the south.  In addition to the spongy lichen upon which to tread, the burrow has been turned into a small, pretty park.  Benches line a curvy gravel-strewn path, and water has been re-routed to form a babbling stream that runs from the northwest wall to the east, undoubtedly draining into the tunnels outside the fort.  A stone bridge over the brook makes a fine spot for lovers to meet.   } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
