R { 4496} {0} {<148>} {The South Courtyard} {<148>. .<088>} {  A large fountain of grey stone dominates this part of the courtyard.  Columns line its circumference, and it resembles a wedding cake with a series of triple tiers.  The stone is inset with rhombuses of ruby and emerald, and surprisingly it seems that no one has attempted to pry them away.  Beyond the fountain is a tasteful statue of a tall, crowned rabbit.  His face is that of a sage, wise and deeply lined, and the label on its round base reads "King Cottontail IV".   } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
