R { 4513} {0} {<148>} {Commander's Office} {<148>. .<088>} {  By far the largest of the military offices in Fort Terramire, this burrow is also one of the most secure chambers of the installation.  Instead of simple wooden planks lining the walls, sheets of iron have been installed and painted a soft blue, the color of the rabbits' flag.  Obsessively neat, Commander Fuzzy keeps her office very tidy, with everything assigned a spot to the nearest centimeter.  Even the depressions in the floor meant for resting visitors are perfectly circular, cut to her demanding specifications.   } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4512} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4514} {0} {<148>} {Cavalry Office} {<148>. .<088>} {  This office has a rather homey touch to it.  The cavalry commander, a grizzled veteran of the rabbit army, has decorated it in his own inimitable fashion.  Normally Commander Fuzzy wouldn't allow such a thing, but Captain Appaloosa is an excellent strategist and leader of rabbits, and she knows that she's lucky to have him on her staff.  Paintings of horses, both famous ones and those for whom the Captain has developed a fondness over his career, line the walls in crowded rows.  An antique set of tack, its oiled leather dark from decades of horse sweat, lends to the unique aroma that lingers here.   } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4512} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4515} {0} {<278>} {Military Liaison Office} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Plants are good for more than just eating, and the military liaison has used them to great effect here.  Things like those decorations and the drawing of his wife and kits that sits prominently on his desk are effective tactical pieces in getting civilians to relax.  After all, such a kindly, older lieutenant would certainly have the best interests of everybody at heart... right?   } {terramire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
