R { 4821} {0} {<278>} {A Dingy Saloon} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The walls and ceiling of this saloon are made of a sturdy canvas-like  material held aloft by a wooden framework that gives the large tent its  shape. The dirt floor is covered with sawdust, and it looks like left-over  food and other things have been tossed down there also. The tables and chairs are made of a crudely cut dark wood that gives the saloon a utilitarian  feeling. Along the west wall is a bar made of the same wood as the chairs and tables, but the surface has been smoothed and polished. Behind the bar are  shelves with bottles of various alcoholic liquids, and a keg of beer sits on  the floor underneath the shelves. Small stacks of semi-clean shot glasses are at both ends of the bar, and cheap pewter mugs for the beer sit on a shelf  above the keg. The only illumination is provided by dirty hanging oil  lanterns that swing lazily from the breeze that blows in from the opening. } {dsr} {} {inside} {shop} {1.000} {}
E {30032} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4822} {0} {<228>} {Corral} {<228>, `<088>} {  About 50 feet x 50 feet, this corral is made of dark-colored wood posts that  have a distance of about 15 feet between each one. They are dug into the  ground and form rough equivalent of a square. The wood that spans the  distance between them has been cut into flat boards, and is nailed to the  posts with iron nails. The only way out of this corral is a gate to the  south. A trough of water sits to one side of the corral, with a bucket lying  on the ground next to it. } {dsr} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {30039} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4823} {0} {<278>} {Revival Tent} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This tent is about 30 feet x 30 feet. It is made of the same canvas as all  the other tents. It is clean, without any sign of rodents. What makes it  different is that in the back of the tent is a raised dais made out of a  strong, but dark kind of wood that elevates it about 3 feet above the ground. In the center of the dais is a polished wood podium made for holding  documents. Crude chairs are organized in rows for those that are willing to  sit and listen to what preacher says, and there are a few people sitting here listening to him. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {30041} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4824} {0} {<278>} {Aquamarine Intersection} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This intersection of two hallways is made from aquamarine just like the rest  of the cathedral. Unlike the lower part of the cathedral, this aquamarine  appears cloudy, and you can see imperfections in the material, as though  someone was more concerned with speed rather than quality when they built  this. Something else noticeably missing from the upper rooms is that there is no almost holy feeling of peace and sanctuary emanating from the walls. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {30057} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4828} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4825} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4825} {0} {<278>} {Tarnished Corridor} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Instead of making the walls, ceiling and floor out of a high-quality  aquamarine, they are made out of what looks like a hastily gathered material  that hasn't been carefully cut or polished. Instead of the pure, translucent  blue-green color that you would expect from something made from aquamarine,  the aquamarine here appears cloudy, and the workmanship is shoddy, with  poorly-fit junctions and rough edges. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4826} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4824} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4826} {0} {<278>} {Careless Construction} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  All pretense of constructing rooms that resemble the lower part of the  cathedral has been abandoned. Instead of aquamarine forming a seamless  joining of walls and floor, it looks more like whoever made this just grabbed pieces of stone from the ground and threw them together, forming this  mish-mash of thrown-together stones that are just barely holding up the  ceiling. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4827} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4825} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4827} {0} {<278>} {End of the Hallway} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This has been built in the same hurried method as the rest of the upper part  of the cathedral. The walls and ceiling are barely standing, and it looks  like a strong breeze would cause it to collapse. On the western wall is an  odd plaque, made out of a dark red stone that gives off a dark aura. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4826} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4828} {0} {<278>} {Aquamarine Corridor} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The corridor is covered in the same sparkling blue-green material as the  lower part of the cathedral. The walls, ceiling, and floors have been  smoothed to a dull finish, instead of the sparkling clarity that you would  expect from an experienced person that works with aquamarine. Also, the  joining between the walls, floor and ceiling lacks the attention to detail  that was seen in the lower part of the cathedral. There also seems to be a  smoke-colored, almost insubstantial quality to aquamarine, and it seems to  move when you aren't looking directly at it. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4829} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4824} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4829} {0} {<278>} {Tainted Intersection} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Like all the other rooms here, this intersection is composed of a lesser  quality of aquamarine than the rest of the cathedral. The walls haven't been  polished, the ceiling has irregularities that make it look like it might come down at any time, and the floor looks like it was composed of asymmetrical  pieces that make it look like someone used leftover pieces and arranged them, so they would fit together. The vaporous substance in the aquamarine has  increased, and it still looks like it is somehow moving through the  aquamarine. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4831} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4830} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4828} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4830} {0} {<278>} {Unfinished Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Like the other rooms, the material that this room is composed of looks like  it was made from surplus fragments of previous construction efforts. What is  different from the other rooms, however, is that the walls haven't been  completed, and the ceiling is being held up partly by a scaffolding that  crosses from one side of the room to the other. Also, the floor looks as  though it has been hastily thrown together, with no sign of the junctions  being smoothed out, or that anyone has polished it. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4829} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4831} {0} {<278>} {Guardian Simulacrum} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  While still assembled more for speed than quality, the structure here is more sound than the other rooms. The aquamarine here has been put together into a  more seamless link, and the floor has had some semblance of polishing done to it, and the ceiling looks like it won't collapse at any time. The smoky vapor in the aquamarine has almost completely permeated the stone, making it appear to be more of a dark grey-blue instead of the clear translucent coloring of  pure aquamarine. In front of a corridor leading upward is a door that is made of a dark red, almost blood-colored stone, with a sturdy-looking lock made of diamond. And there also is a giant man-shaped creature standing in front of  the door. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4829} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4832} {u} {'adramelech} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4832} {128} {<278>} {Corrupted Aquamarine} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Unlike the other areas in the upper part of the cathedral, everything here  has been meticulously constructed. The walls, ceiling, and floor have been  polished to a mirror-like finish, and where the different parts of the  aquamarine are spliced together form a seamless joint that makes it appear to be made from a single piece of aquamarine. The aquamarine, however, is  completely permeated by the smoky substance, to the point where there is  almost no trace of the aquamarine color left. A smoky, foul-smelling miasma  is escaping from a small idol facing an eastern window, and that miasma is  being absorbed by the aquamarine. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4831} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4833} {0} {<278>} {Defective Diamonds} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This entire part of the castle is composed of solid sheets of polished  diamonds, which would be impossible without the use of powerful magic. The  way that light reflects off of the smooth multifaceted surfaces gives them an almost-ethereal appearance, as though the walls weren't solid and you could  reach through them. The near-perfect impression of the walls is only at the  surface, because if you look closely, a few minute cracks that are filled  with a sickly green color in the otherwise flawless surfaces can be seen. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {30084} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4834} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4834} {0} {<278>} {Shining Intersection} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The way that the light reflects off the surfaces of the diamonds contained  within the sheets that create this room form a dazzling display that makes it appear that not only do tiny stars surround you, but that they are moving  with you. The imperfections that are filled with the sickly green substance  are more evident now, and seem to be more concentrated along the stairs that  lead up. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4835} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4833} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4837} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4836} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4835} {0} {<278>} {Polyhedral Prison} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you enter this side room, the image you see before you seems too intense  to be real. A single beam of light coming in through a small window to the  east has made contact with one of the diamond-studded walls. That beam of  light has then split into hundreds of smaller beams, which then reflect onto  other parts of the room. The sight you see now is a large polyhedron formed  from thousands of smaller beams of light that are reflected continuously  around the room, forming an almost opaque field of energy. Even the green  substance that has infested the rest of the upper part of the castle has  stopped coming into here, as though it can tell that there is something here  that it should stay away from. In the center of the north wall is an opening  that looks like it was made to hold a solid object. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4834} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4836} {0} {<278>} {Amazing Shapes} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Everything here is composed of tiles that have diamond dust embedded into it. The light that reflects off the panels creates an illusion that makes it look like there are complex three-dimensional shapes dancing all around you. The  shapes are so mesmerizing that staring at them for too long will cause you to be disoriented as your eyes and brain try to decide if what you are seeing is real or not. That same green substance has infiltrated the cracks in the  diamond is here, spreading out from the entrance towards the western side of  the room. The shapes that seem so solid that you feel like you would be able  to reach out and 'get' them are a hexconal pyramid, a pentagrammic prism, a  torus, and an octahedron. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4834} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4837} {0} {<278>} {Corrupted Stairway} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The diamonds that compose this stairwell are mostly covered by the green  substance that you have seen in the upper part of the castle. Thin tendrils  of this green energy are attached to the facets of the diamond walls, giving  them the appearance of small roots or vines that thicken farther up the  stairs. Unlike what you have seen before, these green tendrils seem to pulse  with an energy that causes your stomach to churn just looking at it. } {dsr} {Key: dw, get pent, ee, put pent op} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4834} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4838} {u} {open u;u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4838} {128} {<278>} {Magnificent View} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The height of this tower, combined with windows in all directions, gives an  unequaled view of Caspia. You can see an unparalleled view of the cathedral  to the west, the library to the north, as well as the rest of the city all  around you! The walls of the tower normally would sparkle like miniature  suns, but that green growth has covered the entire surface of the interior,  and the pulsing energy resembles blood vessels more than simple roots or  branches. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4837} {d} {open d;d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4839} {0} {<278>} {Mine Entrance} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The mine below Caspia has things that are both similar and not similar to  what anyone would expect a mine to be like. Like all mines, there is a  feeling of claustrophobic closeness that comes from knowing that mines comes  from excavation far below the surface, and that there are tons of rock and  dirt pressing down on you from above. A fine layer of dust covers everything, no doubt as a side effect of all the excavation that is going on here. What  is different, however, is that while the surfaces of the mine are made of  dirt and rocks, they are smooth as though they were fused together to help  reinforce the tunnels. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4840} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {30077} {u} {open u;u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4842} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4840} {0} {<278>} {Eastern Intersection} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The walls here are as smooth as the rest of the tunnels. A string of magic  lights along the ceiling barely gives enough illumination to see where you  are walking, but it doesn't light it as well as the sun would, nor does it  relieve the slightly oppressive feeling that you get from being far below the surface. You can see the floor curving downward to the south, and the lights  show you that there are a few different directions you can go at the southern part of this tunnel. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4841} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4839} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4841} {0} {<278>} {Southeastern Turn} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The layout of these tunnels has more of a smooth surface than what you would  expect from a mine. The walls have been smoothed out, and where the walls  join to make a corner has been rounded. There is a string of lights going  north to another corner, west to another room in the tunnel, and there is  string of lights going downward to another level of the mine. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
