R { 4844} {0} {<278>} {The Middle of the Southern Tunnel} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Just like the rest of the tunnels, this has been smoothed to a rough finish. This part of the tunnel is roughly twice the size of the other parts of the  tunnel, and it looks like it has been used as a place to dump unwanted parts  of the gems and unused parts of the wall because there is a large pile of  detritus in one corner. Something else that doesn't look quite right are  smaller piles of detritus that are arranged in a straight line, with a mining hat on each one. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4841} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4843} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4845} {0} {<278>} {Down into the Lower Levels} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Although the tunnel isn't as well-made as the tunnels that are farther up  are, This tunnel is still sturdy. There is a greater level of grime that  covers everything, and the lights don't illuminate as well. There is a ramp  leading downward farther into the mine, a way up to the upper levels, and to  the east is a partial tunnel with a railing set into it. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4848} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4846} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4843} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4846} {0} {<278>} {Middle of the Tunnel} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Although the north side of the tunnel is smooth and solid, the south side is  another story. To the south is an opening as tall as the walls and about 10  feet long. Looking down, you can see that not only would it be a long drop to the ground, but there is also a flurry of activity at the bottom of the mine. Fortunately, a sturdy railing has been installed into the south wall that  prevents someone from accidentally taking the short way to the bottom of the  mine. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4847} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4845} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 4847} {0} {<278>} {Eastern Railing} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The protective railing that prevents someone from falling to the bottom of  the mine extends east from here. The walls are sturdy and smooth, and the  floor is still covered with dirt and grime. Leaning over the railing, and  seeing just how far it is to the bottom help you to realize just how futile  (and painful) jumping would be, and some activity can be seen to the west,  and there is a ramp leading down the bottom of the mine, as well as back up  to the first part of the mine. } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4849} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 4841} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
