R { 6055} {0} {<278>} {The Black Fountain} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  In the middle of the room stands a roughly carved black fountain with dirty,  ashen water gurgling in it. On the side of it you hardly notice a beautiful,  elvish lady sitting on the corpse of a huge shadowcat. Most of the time she  seems to be crying. It's amazing that she has been here unnoticed for all  that time. Perhaps her long, black hair has been a good cover for her. The  room seems to be a relatively safe place in the citadel, probably protected  by the old adventurer's magic. Besides the lady, everything else in this room looks like it should be in an evil fortress: black walls are covered with ash from a distant volcano and the floor is covered with dirt. The black water in the fountain doesn't seem to be drinkable either. Both eastern and western  exits lead back to the hallway. } {raukora} {} {inside} {pk} {1.000} {}
E { 6049} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E { 6044} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 6056} {0} {<278>} {The Obsidian Watchtower} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You are standing near a big statue of Rauko'ra, the Lord of the Citadel. In  the corner there is huge guard eating the leg of some poor creature. He is  glaring at you angrily. To the west you can see a hopeless land in ruin. To  the east and north there is a dark, desolation filled with ugly monsters. There is a locked chest on the ground. The only exit is down the ladder. } {raukora} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E { 6054} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R { 6057} {0} {<278>} {Light Hallway} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You see a hallway with torches on the walls. They have not been lit because  there is plenty of light emanating from the nearby towers. As you hear the  talking and yelling of guards nearby, it becomes evident that caution will be needed to proceed further. The path west leads to the obsidian watchtower. The eastern one takes you to the granite watchtower. } {raukora} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
