R {10349} {0} {<238>} {The Ruins of Turadar} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  Barely a week ago, the great city of Turadar stood here at the edge of the  wastelands of Tinek. Now, no more than a few scattered pieces of rubble and  fallen stonework mark the spot where the city once stood. Looking to the  east, a sea spreads out before you where once farmers toiled to grow food  for the citizens of Turadar. The rebellion of the Nix is nearly complete\; its power grows as the Nixie absorb more territory into their sea. The rebel army covers the land before you, its collective attention frozen by the hordes of  wyvern descending from the churning, multi-colored sky, called forth by the  Horn of Commanding from deep within the mountain caves of Rhodus. Burning  venom cascades onto the rebels, answered by bolts of magical energy as the  battle for the fate of the world rages on! } {rebellion} {} {desert} {safe} {1.000} {}
E {10350} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {10350} {0} {<238>} {Amid the Nixie Rebels} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  Here amidst the army of the Nixie rebels, your senses reel as bursts of light and sound explode around you as discerning between the cacophony of Nixie  devilment and the actual combatants builds steadily upon a vicious headache. Humans, once-Human things, Demons and creatures beyond any sane imagination  surround you, constantly melting and reforming before your eyes as the whims  of Nixie music wash across them. Each and every one seems completely insane,  driven mad by the unceasing impossibilites battering their senses. Nevertheless, the unreality of Nixie devilment seems far weaker on this  battlefield than it did among the Ships of the Nix, probably due to the  presence of the wyverns. The Horn of Commanding has called them to do the  bidding of the Loyalists struggling against the rebels.  Far in the distance, you can make out a lone hill, seemingly untouched by  the Nixies or the battle. } {rebellion} {} {desert} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {10352} {0} {<278>} {Atop the Wyvern Guildhall} {<278>. .<088>} {  Climbing up a back staircase, you find yourself on the roof of the building, standing at the base of the wyvern's neck to your north.  The massive granite wings block off your view to the east and west, and only rooftops stand between your viewpoint and the shoreline to the south.  As with everywhere else in Rhodus, despite the opulence of the architecture, it is the malformed sky that grabs your attention, never for a moment letting you forget the peril threatening this island-- and this world.   } {rebellion} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E {10324} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {10353} {0} {<148>} {A Converted Sewer} {<148>. .<088>} {  The first thing you notice about this place is the smell...  This must've been used for a sewer back when the part of town above it was still inhabitable.  Although the stench still lingers heavily, a small group of escaped slaves has made these tunnels their home.  However they may have managed to escape, they have achieved a temporary shelter only by placing themselves directly in the path of the oncoming Nixies.  They will be the first to die.   } {rebellion} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
