R {10479} {128} {<148>} {Chamber of the cauldron} {<148>. .<088>} {  Finally entering this room, you realize your efforts were not enough to stop  the evil from being released. A huge black cauldron rests over a magical blue fire in the center of a pentagram. Foul sulfurous fumes rise up from the  boiling green liquid, and a shape begins to take form. The green goo begins  to rock from side to side; growing in its actions, it starts to actually rise up from out of the cauldron. Seeming as though it is trying to pull itself  from within the container, it reaches higher and higher towards the ceiling  until suddenly it stops. The liquid suspended in a column continues to flow  up and down in a swirling pattern and features begin to form. In horror you  watch as a skeleton ten feet tall steps from within the goo. Reaching back  into the cauldron it pulls a robe as dark as the darkest night from within  and dons it. Again reaching into the infernal mix it pulls out a huge scythe. Turning to face you, the being speaks, "I am Nerull the god of all evils. Death, pestilence, famine, suffering, and decay are my tools of pleasure, and the ever living undead are my children. Have you come to serve me or fall  beneath the path of my destruction?"  } {damned} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
