R {11027} {0} {<228>} {The edge of a steamy marsh} {<228>( *<088>} {  As you turn off the swampy path, you realize that the loggers back in Aylor  were not as drunk as they should have been from all the Firebreather they had been drinking. Clearly visible, now that the loggers have chopped through the undergrowth and the trees, is the trail you followed to see for yourself if  the wild stories the loggers were telling were spun out of firebreather, or  if a real adventure could be here. You stand at the very edge of the steaming wetland, hearing the small chitterings, buzzings and splashes that are  associated with places such as this; however, there is also a very faint  chanting on the breeze that doesn't belong here. As you look around, you  notice that like any marshland or wetland, this one is full of greenery,  though there is a multitude of colors from flowers, insects, and decay mixed  with the trees. As you continue to look, you notice three paths branching  from this point, going deeper into the marsh, and of course, the way back to  the swampy path. } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
