R {11028} {0} {<228>} {A muddy path} {<228>( *<088>} {  The path you are following is a sign of things to come it would seem.  The trees here are tall, their large roots poking through the brown mud that serves as a path.  The sounds of insects and chittering animals begins to surround you as you move deeper into the marsh, and the heat mixed with water vapor makes the air shimmer.  There is a light breeze, but it is by no means a cooling one.  Through the trees to the left and right you can barely make out dark, shady-looking pools of water.  The sound of frogs and other aquatic animals drift to your ears.  Still the chanting continues, you remember the loggers mentioning the chanting as well, and they also mentioned dangers; fierce tribal lizardmen, and something about large rats and moving trees.  Ahead the path continues deeper into the steamy quagmire, though you can still return to the edge of this untamed land and try another path or simply leave before you find those lizardmen.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11029} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11027} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11029} {0} {<228>} {Through dense vegetation} {<228>( *<088>} {  The vegetation here has grown up over what little path there was in this swamp.  Thick brown tree trunks block both east and west travel, and vines with brightly colored flowers cover the path, along with several other plants.  Moss grows all over everything here, and fungi of all sorts seem to spring out of every crevice and crack in the bark of the trees and vines.  It is extremely dark here, and the air is heavy with humidity and the scents of flourishing undergrowth.  Ahead it looks as if this vegetation will recede again and let in light.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11030} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11028} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11030} {0} {<228>} {Opening in the undergrowth} {<228>( *<088>} {  Here the undergrowth is less than to the south, the path slopes up slightly, and the mud is a little drier than in the surrounding area.  From here you can see a bit farther in all directions.  To the north, and slightly east, you can see the sparkling of sunlight on water, though only brief glimpses of the body of water through the many trees that surround it. There appears to be some form of rock formation directly north, though it is covered in moss and plant life.  To the west, you see some sort of thorny plant with long spines, and it does not look possible to penetrate the undergrowth in that direction, even if you did wish to risk your skin on those spines.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11031} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11029} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11031} {0} {<228>} {On a well used path} {<228>( *<088>} {  As you walk along this path, you notice faint signs of tracks.  Also there are some discarded tools lying in the mud off to one side of the trail.  It strikes you suddenly that this is the first time you can truly call any cleared path in this marsh a trail.  There are still tall, thick trees with vines and flowers growing around them, and the trail is still dotted with shallow dips where water has collected, but it has been cleared of most of the vegetation that thrives in the steamy climate.  To the east, thick undergrowth and vines block any passage, except perhaps by the small animals who call the marshlands home, while west will take you back to the slight rise in the land.  North you can now plainly see the large lake, though it is still a ways off.  The mound you first noticed on your way along the path rises to the west and just to the north.  There is a faint sound of rustling and hissing coming from farther to the north.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11032} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11030} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11032} {0} {<228>} {Close to a lake} {<228>( *<088>} {  From here you can see the lake more clearly than before.  Thick vegetation is all around, but you notice that the trees on the lakeshore are not growing quite so close together.  West from here the mound has an opening, and appears to be a den of some sort.  The hissing and rustling you heard is coming from inside the mound, and there are a lot of tracks leading in and out of the opening.  There are still trees to the east and it appears that one or two are dead, there are a couple of logs on the ground, covered in fungi and moss which glows a soft green.  The scent of mud, decaying vegetation and water fills your nostrils and the sounds of insects and small animals fill your ears as you move along the path.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11034} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11031} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11033} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11033} {0} {<148>} {The den of the Lizardmen} {<148>. .<088>} {  You have entered the den of the Lizardmen, the skins of many animals lie on the floor or hang from the rocky walls.  Even here the moss grows on the rock, and bones are strewn over the uneven floor.  Painted skins on the walls show various states of a hunt, and there is evidence in one corner of someone's work on a new bow.  The smell here is wild and unpleasant, and you sense that you are being watched, though it is impossible to tell what direction the watcher is staring from.  It may be best to leave while you have a chance.  Perhaps you have already stayed too long.   } {agroth} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {11032} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11034} {0} {<228>} {On the lakeshore} {<228>( *<088>} {  Finally, you stand at the shore of a lake.  The water appears clean and clear, and you can see birds out on the lake, diving and coming up with silvery fish in their beaks.  The shore of the lake is covered with cattails and small red and yellow flowers.  The mud here is very thick and you can see prints which have sunk into the mud about five inches.  The air here is very thick and humid, although the slight breeze off the water makes it feel somewhat cooler than back on the path.  There is a large tree here, its branches lower to the water than many you have seen in the marsh.  It appears that the branches extend completely across the lake, overlapping with branches from other trees.  There are splashes out on the water, and you catch fleeting glimpses of bass and other fish leaping out to catch an insect, before disappearing with barely a ripple on the surface of the lake. } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11048} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11038} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
