R {11035} {0} {<228>} {Up a tree} {<228>( *<088>} {  You now stand in the branches that stretch out over the lake.  The sounds of tree frogs and birds intensify as you rustle in the leafy branches, and many small creatures scurry away in the limbs.  From here, you can see out over part of the marshlands.  Back toward the path that led into this steaming swamp, you can see the den of the Lizardmen, and the thick wall of vegetation on the eastern side of the marsh.  To either side, you see mud and plants, and the lake extends to the north, east and west.  You can either return to the lakeshore, in this heat a swim might be nice, that is if the lake isn't filled with hungry things that would love to try something new for a snack, or you can continue on out over the water, using the branches as a bridge.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11034} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11036} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11036} {0} {<228>} {Out on a bridge of limbs} {<228>( *<088>} {  You are now over the lake, the branches are not extremely high above the water, but they are high enough to keep one from leaping up to grab them from the water.  The leaves and flowers on the tree provide you with some cover from any watchers, but the insects are becoming unbearable.  Mosquitoes and gnats swarm around the lake, and they are finding all the exposed skin on your body.  Below you the lake sparkles and a small silver-sided fish leaps from the water and catches some insect.  At the peak of its arc, the fish gives a flick of its tail and disappears back into the lake with a small splash.  A moment later, a large alligator bursts from the waters of the lake carrying some kind of waterfowl in its massive jaws.  Perhaps the bridge was a good idea for crossing the lake after all, even with the mosquitoes and gnats.  You can continue along the bridge either north or south to trees which will give you access to the ground again.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11037} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11035} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11037} {0} {<228>} {In the limbs of a great tree} {<228>( *<088>} {  You sit in the limbs of a great tree.  From here you can move out onto the lake and cross over it using the limbs as a bridge, they are thick and look as if they can support massive amounts of weight.  Below you the lakeshore teams with life, small rodents move quickly, gathering in insects and very small fish for food, a frog leaps on the shore, snatching a fly or mosquito from the air.  The humidity is very great here, but the breezes coming off the lake help to cool things down, though not by much.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {11047} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11036} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11038} {0} {<148>} {Out on the lake} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  The water in the lake is lukewarm.  It probably never drops to any temperature that would be uncomfortable for the average human.  The water is clear, and you can clearly see fish swimming in the waters.  Also birds dive and swim in the water with you.  Looking up, you see the tangle of limbs high above you, making a bridge over the lake.  Algae grows on the rocks near the lakeshore and on the rocks at the bottom of the lake.  There are many aquatic plants in the lake as well, hiding some of the depths from view.   } {agroth} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}
