R {11047} {0} {<228>} {On the lakeshore next to a great tree} {<228>( *<088>} {  The lakeshore is fairly solid here, and the roots of an enormous tree help to provide footing.  As you look around, you notice that the great tree here stands almost alone, and is the tallest in this part of the marsh.  It continues up high above the surrounding treetops, and its branches extend in all directions.  Some of the southern branches extend far out over the lake, and they seem to mingle with branches from another great tree on the other side of the lake, creating a natural bridge across the lake.  You can continue around the lake, or maybe take a swim in the inviting waters, though you get the feeling that predators are always on the lookout for some unwary thing in the deep waters.  You could also go over the bridge, if you wish, or continue deeper into the marshlands to the north.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
