R {11062} {0} {<228>} {Deeper into the marshlands} {<228>( *<088>} {  Here the path opens up a bit, and becomes broader.  The sun hammers down on this spot as well, and you can see fallen trees to either side of the path.  A few saplings reach toward the sky, but they are only a few feet high at the moment.  Large, rotted logs litter the undergrowth, and farther back in the undergrowth, where the larger trees again reclaim the land, you can see glowing green fungus and moss spreading over the decaying vegetation.  The path becomes very muddy here, and a small pool of stagnant water to the east bubbles and steams.  Small reptiles and swarms of insects move around the water and across the path.  A small rodent chitters and scurries across the path, disappearing into the undergrowth.  The air becomes heaver with water, and you can smell the sickeningly sweet smell of decay and the slightly sharp odor of water and mud.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
