R {11069} {0} {<228>} {An odd village among the trees} {<228>( *<088>} {  The fields give way here to a small village.  You can see many more of those furry humanoids, their bodies sleek, with fur that is sometimes coated with a thin layer of mud from the marsh.  The houses are small only about 6 feet high, and that seems to include an attic.  The breezes here bring scents of fresh bread, sweet flowering bushes, and the faintest hint of mud. Another thing of note is how the marshlings react to the primal chanting which is steadily coming closer as you continue to follow the path.  When the chanting begins the marshlings seem to gather around a large clearing on the far edge of the village and begin a capering dance.  Until now, you had thought them a peaceful species, however, during the dance, you can see many spears and small short bows hefted, and here and there a stone axe.  You decide that maybe it would not be a good idea to try to steal any of their food; they look as if they can use those weapons.  Shrugging you continue on through the rustic village.   } {agroth} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
