R {11073} {0} {<278>} {Just under the great willow fronds} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you part the gigantic fronds and walk into the deep shade of the willow, the temperature drops noticeably.  You can smell the sharp odor of damp earth, and the primal chanting is the loudest sound, now.  There are several clumps of mushrooms and other fungi growing on the ground around you.  To the east, you can see a few rays of sunlight, while to the west, the area is pitch black.  The sounds of dripping water from far above just barely registers over the sound of the chanting, and while the air is cooler under the willow fronds, it is no less humid.   } {agroth} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {11072} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11074} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11074} {0} {<278>} {Deeper into the dark branches} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You are now in near pitch blackness, save for the light you have with you.  With some effort, you can just barely make out a faint glow to the east which would be the sunlight, though it does not come close to penetrating this far under the branches of the enormous tree.  To the west, you can barely make out a faint glow.  The air is much cooler here than out in the open, but it is much heavier, and filled with the scent of damp earth and flourishing fungi.  You begin to think of turning back, and just as you turn to do so, the chanting becomes even more powerful, tugging at everything primal and instinctual within your being. } {agroth} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {11073} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {11075} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {11075} {0} {<278>} {Outside a great crack in the willow's trunk} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Finally, you have reached the trunk of the magnificent willow.  As you move closer, the glow becomes stronger, and you find yourself staring in wonder at an enormous crack in the tree trunk.  It appears to be large enough for a giant to walk into, but the vibrant glow makes it impossible to see what is on the inside of the tree.  It seems odd that a tree can survive with a crack this large, but then, it is a magically made crack, and perhaps whoever made it is also keeping the tree alive.  The chanting is very loud here, blocking out all other sounds, but it is finally centralized, and is coming from the glowing crack in the tree trunk.   } {agroth} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
