R {11539} {0} {<228>} {Fields of Patchy Ice} {<228>, `<088>} {  The Ice Mist Peaks loom to the south and east, while the ocean crashes against the shore to the north.  The ground is hard, and here and there patches of ice and slush grip the earth.  The mountains, along with the thick growth of trees which cover them, help keep this place chill and shaded, allowing water to freeze and hold on for much longer periods than normal.  A light mist from the ocean drifts toward the mountains, droplets of water seeming to freeze as they alight on the mountain slopes.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
