R {11601} {0} {<238>} {High Up in the Mountains} {<238>/ \<088>} {  The smell of spruce and pine is strong on the swirling breezes.  Shadows from the thick trunks and interlaced branches of the ancient trees make it difficult to see in any direction for much distance.  The mist which perpetually hangs over the Ice Mist Peaks is torn to tatters among the craggy tops of the mountains; it does not dissipate, however, and it only helps to obscure the landscape further.  Tall granite cliffs rise high above the questionable safety of the passes which adventurers use to traverse these mountains, and large, odd shaped boulders rest in clusters even among the passes.  While muffled, the sounds of wildlife surround you.  At least it isn't too lonely in these peaks, though perhaps it would be better if it was a little more quiet.  The faint dripping of water seems nearly out of place, considering the thin sheen of ice which seems to cover everything.   } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
