R {11663} {0} {<238>} {Mist Covered Mountains} {<238>/ \<088>} {  The craggy slopes of the Ice Mist Peaks are covered in a thick, icy mist. It is very difficult to see very far in any direction, and the shadows created by the large trees which grow thickly on the mountains do not help.  The sounds of wildlife are everywhere; a clattering of hooves announces the presence of mountain goats; a chittering and snuffling might be chipmunks, and a low growling could be some type of bear.  Nothing seems to get that close to you, though, and at the moment, the biggest danger is climbing safely through the mountains.  The sounds of the ocean can be heard to the north, and the smell of salt water drifts on the swirling breezes.  To the east the mountains march down into the Mesolarian grassland, although this close to the ocean, it is more likely to be marshy and populated with water plants, rather than the tall grasses and grains which are the trademark of the open plains.  West from here the mountains give way to a small valley, or is that just a trick of the mists?   } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
