R {11720} {0} {<238>} {Climbing Through the Mountains} {<238>/ \<088>} {  It might've been a better idea to stick to the rough road.  These peaks are treacherous; rough ground makes travel difficult, though not impossible. The thick boughs of the pine and spruce, which grow thickly in the mountains, block out nearly all light, and the air is chill and damp.  An icy mist seems to wreathe the peaks, which must be how this range got its name.  The road lies back to the south, offering an easier passage through the rugged peaks, and north leads to a temple.  In the distance you can just see a monk walking along a path.  Perhaps the temple is here to test those who wish to become initiates.   } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
