R {11722} {0} {<238>} {Climbing Through Frozen Peaks} {<238>/ \<088>} {  Here the Ice Mist Peaks seem to show off their name.  The ice is thick on the tall spruce and pine trees which make up the dense forest that covers the mountains.  While the space between the trees is open, little can grow with the thick roots of the ancient trees blocking out so much light, and the temperature is not inviting to fungi or mosses.  The shadows are still very thick, making it hard to see far in any direction.  To the south a smooth pass seems to run through the mountains, almost as if a chunk of the mountainside was chopped away.  To the north the mountainside opens out a little, but thick mists obstruct the view in that direction.   } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
