R {11733} {0} {<228>} {The Horn of the Dragon} {<228>, `<088>} {  This is the larger of the two islands which make up the Horn of the Dragon, so named because the first surveyors of the continent were in awe of the large dragons and named several features of the land and waters after the flying creatures which were more abundant in those days.  The soft sand and palm trees make this seem almost a paradise, but sea spray and the winds from the northern seas keep these islands on the cool side.  A small stretch of ocean separates this island from the smaller one to the north.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
