R {11780} {0} {<278>} {Meso Hor Nee} {<278>---<088>} {  It is uncertain how this small dirt track gained its name.  Perhaps it means something in an old, lost language of the continent?  It is left up to those who travel its route to come up with their own explanations; most of these come from the dim smoky rooms of taverns where men have drunk perhaps more than is necessary and turn to bawdy stories for entertainment.  This road joins the Blessed Aylorian Highway to the mountain city of Kerofk.  Here in the mountains, the hard packed dirt is broken occasionally by the roots of the great trees which grow along the mountain sides.  The ruts left by centuries worth of travel by wagon trains are deep, and not even the ancient roots of the trees, or the hard stones which make up the mountains' ground can retake the manmade track for their own.  The branches of the evergreens close in over the top of the road, making this part of the journey dim and chill.   } {mesolar} {} {smallroad_ew} {} {1.000} {}
