R {11784} {0} {<228>} {Fog Shrouded Moors} {<228>, `<088>} {  The land gradually gives way to the sea here.  To the south, the Mesolarian grassland looks vibrant and dry, and to the north, the Bay of Mist provides some respite from the unpredictable ocean.  Here, though, the land is mixed.  The mountains to the west reach down into the moors, making this particular stretch a bit more dangerous than one might think.  Small scalable cliffs provide many opportunities for one to plunge deep into the frigid waters of the bay.  Small pools of salt water dot the area, and the stench of mud, rotting wood and seaweed fills the air, mixed with the tang of the salt water carried on breezes blowing in from the ocean.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
