R {11785} {0} {<228>} {Rugged Mesolarian Grassland} {<228>, `<088>} {  Close to the coast the land abruptly changes, gone is the lush green grass of the plains, replaced by short dry ragged patches of grass.  Large weather-beaten rocks regularly break through the otherwise smooth, flat plains.  Clusters of dried grass dot the sea- and wind-ravaged coast.  Small sand dunes surprisingly sprout living, although twisted and stunted, trees.  In the distance to the west icy mountains rise out of the plains.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
