R {11852} {0} {<228>} {Rugged Mesolarian Grassland} {<228>, `<088>} {  Far from the fertile and lush inland, the coastline is rugged and unforgiving.  Patches of fog roll in from the sea, cloaking' areas of the coast in thick shrouded mist.  The cry of gulls offers a haunting counterpoint to the crash of the waves and the howling winds.  Life close to the coast is not as abundant; though life does exist here it is less noticeable than further inland.  Occasionally the sea birds fall silent for a few moments and then begin their cries again.  Something out there in the ocean must be causing the silence.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
