R {12087} {0} {<228>} {On the Banks of the Dragon River} {<228>, `<088>} {  The ground is extremely fertile by the Dragon River.  Centuries of good rain and the river's tendency to rise during the rains have washed a considerable amount of silt onto the grasslands which serve as its banks.  Soft, green grass carpets the river bank, and cattails and rushes grow thickly at the water's edge.  The sounds of frogs croaking and insects buzzing seem to come from every direction.  Out in the sparkling, pristine waters of the river, a large trout leaps into the air to catch a snack.  With hardly a sound, the fish slices back into the clear waters and continues on its way.  Thick vegetation rises to the south, ferns and willows offer shelter, though the air is very humid, and being enclosed in all that vegetation may be uncomfortable.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
