R {12093} {0} {<148>} {Ninyth Bay} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  On the edges of Ninyth Bay the water changes from a crystal clear color to a sapphire blue.  Fish swim lazily through large, almost forest-like amounts of swaying seaweed and slip between clusters of rocks.  To the north the ragged edge of the Mesolarian continent meets the pure waters and although the waters are shallow close to the rocky shore, they drop off suddenly into deeper waters only feet from shore, which makes it dangerous for an unwary swimmer.  The rip tide is much stronger here than closer to shore as it faces directly onto the sea to the east.   } {mesolar} {} {ocean} {} {1.000} {}
