R {12187} {0} {<228>} {A field of wild flowers} {<228>, `<088>} {  Not all of the Mesolarian grassland is strictly grass.  Here, for instance, the grass is nearly hidden by the clusters of brightly colored flowers.  The air is filled with a soft perfume it is almost enough to encourage sleepiness.  This looks like a nice place to relax and set up a picnic.  Several insects can be seen moving among the flowers, their industriousness enabling the colorful vegetation to thrive and spread.  Bees fly from flower to flower ladybugs seem to patrol the field, feasting on more harmful insects, and small ants hide out in the petals of the plants, protecting the delicate structures from those who would feast on the greenery.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
