R {12208} {0} {<228>} {The Edge of a Rainforest} {<228>* *<088>} {  Tall willows and large ferns spread over the land here.  Many small tracks show where rodents and other types of animals have passed through this area, perhaps many call it home.  The ground is muddy, and holds tracks well.  The air is very humid; the moisture probably trapped by the sheer amount of thick vegetation which has grown up to make this rainforest.  Far to the east the sounds of the ocean are very audible, even over the shirll cries of the birds who live in this rainforest.  To the south it appears as if there used to be more rainforest, but it has long since been reclaimed by the grasslands, thanks to the help of man's axes.   } {mesolar} {} {jungle} {} {1.000} {}
