R {12213} {0} {<148>} {Ninyth Bay} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  On the edges of Ninyth Bay the water changes from a crystal clear color to a sapphire blue.  Fish swim lazily through large, almost forest-like amounts of swaying seaweed.  To the south a large beach meets the pure waters, and although the waters are shallow close to the sand, it drops off suddenly into deeper waters only feet from shore, making it dangerous for an unwary swimmer.  The rip tide is much stronger than closer to shore, as it faces directly onto the sea to the east.  Here the chance of running into large predators is much more likely than closer to shore.   } {mesolar} {} {ocean} {} {1.000} {}
