R {12258} {0} {<228>} {On the banks of the Dragon River} {<228>. ^<088>} {  The sounds of mosquitoes and other small insects fill the air.  The river and its banks are full of life, unfortunately, here on the banks, most of that life is in the form of small, stinging or biting insects.  The soft, green grass is springy underfoot, and reeds, rushes and cat tails grow thickly near the water's edge.  The scent of onion carries very well on a soft breeze, and the source of the smell becomes noticeable with a closer look at the vegetation along the river.  West from here the ground rises in a series of hills, while north of here the Mesolarian grassland stretches out for miles.   } {mesolar} {} {hills} {shop} {1.000} {}
