R {12425} {0} {<278>} {The Blessed Aylorian Highway} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Constructed of large, rectangular stones, this wide highway stretches far to the north and south.  Many wagon trains and caravans travel the Blessed Aylorian Highway, carrying trade goods to the many settlements which have grown up along its route over the years.  To the west a small group of tents have been erected, and the sounds of merriment can be heard from them.  A small sign by the highway reads: "ONLY FOR THE YOUNG AND YOUNG AT HEART!  EVERYONE ELSE KEEP OUT!"  There is something in the air, perhaps magic, which seems to make sure the sign's rule is enforced.  The highway also serves as the main route for pilgrims, on their way to the great city of Aylor, to worship in the magnificent temple there.   } {mesolar} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
