R {12443} {0} {<228>} {North of the Flames of Godhood} {<228>, `<088>} {  The Mesolarian grassland stretches out to the east, west and north, but to the south rise the Flames of Godhood; named for their tremendous height and their glowing tops.  The ground here is scorched, and partially covered with a layer of black rock and ash.  The smell of smoke hangs in the air, which is hot and seems to shimmer, and a pall of smoke hangs over the peaks to the south.  The eastern and western peaks seem to be on fire, but the central peak looks safe enough to travel.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
