R {12503} {0} {<238>} {Atop Mount Angir} {<238>/ \<088>} {  The steep slopes of Mount Angir are covered in slow moving lava.  All life has long since been banished from these slopes by the fury of the gods. This small range is named for its towering height, reaching into the very heavens, or so it seemed to the Mesolarian inhabitants who named it long ago.  Clouds swirl here, soft mist mixed with thick, choking smoke and ash.  The red glow of heated rock surrounds the top of this peak.  To the east Mount Olympus climbs even higher into the sky, though it doesn't look nearly as dangerous as standing around on this active volcano.  In all other directions the Mesolarian grasslands spread out, although they are unseen from here, due to the swirling and smokey mist.   } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
