R {12504} {0} {<238>} {Atop Mount Olympus} {<238>/ \<088>} {  Mount Olympus stands in the middle of this small mountain range known as the  Flames of Godhood. It is framed by two great mountains, though Mount Olympus  is the tallest of the three. To the west, lava slides lazily down Mount  Angir's slopes and to the east, Mount Wraath's ever-cascading fountain of  lava has rendered it a mountain of death. Since Mount Olympus does not  contain such a hostile environment it is teeming with life. Climbing  expeditions are often organized by budding young scientists, though a  successful climb to the mountain's highest peak has yet to be accomplished. The area's local inhabitants are firm believers that a city of gods resides  upon this mountain's highest peak. } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
