R {12505} {0} {<238>} {Atop Mount Wraath} {<238>/ \<088>} {  Mount Wraath is the farthest east of the Flames of Godhood.  Its slopes are a slow moving mass of lava, which has swept the mountainsides clean of life.  Here and there small hills of rock show where forests, or possibly villages used to cling to the slopes of the mountain.  A dark mist of heated water mixed with choking smoke and ash swirls around the top of the mountain, but the mist does not quite hide the red glow of the heated fury of the mountaintop.  To the west lies Mount Olympus, which looks much safer than this enormous mound of violent, steaming, smokey rock and ash.   } {mesolar} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
