R {12506} {0} {<228>} {East of the Flames of Godhood} {<228>, `<088>} {  The Mesolarian grassland stretches out to the east, north and south.  To the west lies Mount Wraath, the eastern most peak in the Flames of godhood.  Only the east and west peaks still seem to be active volcanoes, but their eruptions are enough to cover this part of the grasslands with a pall of smoke.  The ground here is nearly barren of life.  What grass does grow here is sparse and surrounded by dead, brown grasses and scorched earth.  Thin fingers of lava crawl out onto the grassland from the mountain, and the air is hot and thick with the smell of smoke, and the taste of ash.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
