R {12742} {0} {<228>} {A boulder-strewn field} {<228>, `<088>} {  The grass is flattened in many places here by a great jumble of boulders. Perhaps this used to be a stone quarry, or maybe a watch tower stood on this spot.  It is impossible to tell, now.  The boulders offer shade to both man and animal alike.  Small worms and insects can be seen, if one looks closely, scuttling or inching their way under and between the enormous rocks.  To the west the Tothmeer trail winds its way through the flat land, and far to the east, a large forest rises out of the open landscape.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
