R {12752} {0} {<228>} {Cradlebrook forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  Tall, thick trunks reach toward the sky.  The grey-brown bark of the trees is fissured and rough with age.  High above, the patchwork of limbs and leaves lets through very little sunlight, and the shadows amidst the trunks are deep and quiet..  Patches of moss and various types of fungi thrive in the dim light, and the occasional chirp of a cricket breaks the peacefulness of the forest.  It would be easy to return to the plains from here, the vast openness a sharp contrast to the closed feeling of the forest.   } {mesolar} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
