R {12805} {0} {<228>} {Silverwind Forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  Down through the centuries this part of the forest has become known in legend.  Perhaps myth?  It is unsure what truly happened here.  Large majestic trees remained scarred to this day.  The forces of evil managed to get a small raiding party to this part of the forest.  Axe and sword were used against these trees.  It is said that the trees cried out the elves in pain.  As trees fell elven clerics and druids heard the screams of their death.  No longer able to stand the horrifying sound of their beloved silvery trees that had sheltered them for centuries, the elven clerics with the aide of druids gave the trees more than the life they had calling upon the earth itself they enlivened the trees to defend themselves.  Their cries turned to rejoicing as the first tree awoke from its passive slumber, its eyes opening.  Soon its limbs became arms, the deep roots and trunks turning into legs to help them walk.  Rejoicing could be heard throughout the forest.  Soon the sounds of death were gone and the terrible snarl of vengeance took its place.  Here the trees walked, taking a terrible revenge on those who would strike their brethren down.  Trees crushed wolfen, vines choked dark clerics and mages alike.  Even giants were not immune to the tree's wrath.  Howling with a need for justice, the trees turned on even the biggest of the dark armies, clubbing them to death.  Crushed and broken bodies littered the floor and new voices sang out.  "We are the Diva!"   } {mesolar} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
