R {12868} {0} {<228>} {East of a beautiful forest} {<228>, `<088>} {  The forest to the west marks the beginning of the Elven homelands.  Barely visible among the trees are Elven archers and warriors, watching over the entrances to their lands.  Surrounding the lands of the elves is an ancient forest of trees, which seem to have a faint silvery sheen to them.  The larger forest was once part of the Elven homeland, and is still considered their land, but is now more open to travellers.  The ground here is flat, and kept clear of all obstructions.  Perhaps after the great war, and the nearly victorious dark armies' strikes on the edges of Silverwind Forest, the Elves have decided to keep a closer eye on the forests which border their lands.  The trail which runs along the forest to the east is traveled by many peoples, and the Elves, still being an untrusting lot of outsiders, must feel more secure with a vantage point from which to watch for signs of an impending attack.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
