R {13091} {0} {<228>} {On the banks of the Greyhare Stream} {<228>, `<088>} {  The ground is extremely fertile by the Greyhare Stream.  Centuries of good rain and the stream's tendency to rise during the rains have washed a considerable amount of silt onto the grasslands which serve as its banks.  Although a considerable amount of silt now lies on its banks, the stream itself is still a murky and silty grey color.  Soft, green grass carpets the river bank, and cat tails and rushes grow thickly at the water's edge.  The sounds of frogs croaking and insects buzzing seem to come from every direction.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
