R {13092} {0} {<228>} {On the banks of the Greyhare Stream} {<228>, `<088>} {  The vegetation along the banks of the Greyhare Stream consists mostly of cattails, reeds and rushes.  Here and there, other unidentifiable greenery makes its presence known.  The smell of mud and fish permeates the air, and the gurgling of the river is a soothing, pleasant sound.  From here, the waters of the Greyhare Stream look silty and murky, but the ground underfoot is damp; thick greenery covers the saturated earth.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
