R {13110} {0} {<228>} {Silverwind Forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  Large silvery streaked leaves rustle in the soft vagrant breezes.  The creak of large limbs moving gently in the winds high above do not seem to make their way down this far, perhaps it is just because the canopy is so thick.  But surely some wind would make it through?  Unlike most forests throughout the land this one is different.  The bark on the ancient trees is more silver than brown.  Although the forest is vast and you may not see another soul on your travels through here you may not feel alone.  There is a presence here, waiting and watching all who enter the forest, maybe it has to do with the legend of the forest from the last war.  Could trees really have walked and taken vengeance?  Only the trees and elves truly know.  To the south the land abruptly changes, instead of fertile grass and open plains, the lands turns into a swamp.  Frogs croak from their hidden places in the saturated muddy ground.  The annoying hum of mosquitos can be heard even from within this forest.   } {mesolar} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
