R {13346} {0} {<228>} {Fields amid the great forest} {<228>, `<088>} {  The trees seem to give way to a small stretch of prairie here.  There is a small meadow to the north, but its peacefulness does not stretch this far south.  Here, the land becomes wet, almost soggy, and the edge of the Greenwart Swamp borders the southern edge of this field.  The grass here is tall and mixed with small clumps of sawgrass and tall reeds.  The sounds of buzzing insects come from the south, and sevreal swarms of mosquitoes whirr through the air here.  Small, green frogs and a few snakes move through the grasses.  It would be very unwise indeed to travel farther south without being prepared.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
