R {13348} {0} {<228>} {By Agroth's marsh} {<228>; ;<088>} {  The land here is as muddy as the rest of the greenwart Swamp, but a nice difference has come over the land.  There is no evidence here of the lethal Greenwart plant.  It seems as if someone, or something has removed all traces of the plant.  The marshland to the south is fabled to be a place of beauty and, if not peace, at least neutrality.  The man for whom it was named was a druid of ages past.  He fought once in the demon wars, against the horde of Valkur, and during that war, the marshland was created.  Since that time, Agroth along with a representative from the evil forces, and a neutral being who befriended the druid who went astray have stood guard over the marsh.  During the great war, which split the lands once more, Agroth once again ventured out to fight, this time, his contributions represented only removing the Greenwart from the borders of his lands, and the means by which he removed the plant must've been drastic, since the plant has not yet grown back in this portion of the swamp.   } {mesolar} {} {swamp} {} {1.000} {}
