R {13464} {0} {<238>} {On a dull forest trail} {<238>. .<088>} {  The narrow trail becomes swampy to the east of here, but at this point, it is still nice and dry.  The Silverwind Forest lies to the north, and to the south a large field with old tree stumps separates you from the Greenwart Swamp.  Large, thick roots cross the trail, and a few weeds grow up in the center of the rutted track.  The track is wide enough for a small cart, but a wagon would find it extremely difficult to pass along this route.   } {mesolar} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
