R {13467} {0} {<228>} {Greenwart Swamp} {<228>; ;<088>} {  Thick vines cross the swamp at this point.  Many also wind around the large, dark trees which seem to dominate the landscape.  There is no evidence of the Greenwart plant, something to be eternally grateful for.  The small bushes with bright flowers and thorns seem to crawl across the muddy ground, and in places, they seem to hide the small pools of quicksand. Small chitterings can be heard from among the undergrowth, and high overhead, the calls of ravens and vultures seem ominous.   } {mesolar} {} {swamp} {} {1.000} {}
