R {13564} {0} {<228>} {Carvwin's Landing} {<228>, `<088>} {  You are standing on the very spot where Marikus Corvwin made his improbable and daring landing.  Trapped in the city by the host of trolls, minotaurs, and other dark creatures, Corvwin boldly sailed the army out of the city and to this spot.  Under the cover of night, the army sped behind the evil horde in a flanking maneuver and pinned it up against the sea.  Although the Thalosian army took staggering losses, the threat on this part of the continent was ended.  Legend states that Corvwin sold his soul to the devil for this improbable victory.  That would certainly explain the dramatic break with the church.   } {mesolar} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
