R {13579} {0} {<228>} {A lush stream-bank} {<228>( *<088>} {  Small and delicate shoots strain to reach for the sky in small patches of sunlight that manage to seep through the thick almost impenetrable canopy high above.  Even after so much death in the continent, life does go on and new growth replaces those who have fallen.  The ancient trees that have fallen give way to the shoots of the new.  Although some of the ancient trees are gone, the new shoots that have taken their place use the fallen trees as both shelter from the winds and as the trees of old decompose, food for the new.   } {mesolar} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
