R {13652} {0} {<228>} {Greenwart Swamp} {<228>; ;<088>} {  The swamp and ocean meet here in a violent mixture of foam and mud.  The frothy surface of the swamp is quite dangerous, as it hides the myriad pools of quicksand which dot the swamp.  The muddy foam also hides much of the low-lying plantlife, such as the lethal Greenwart plant.  Many small sea creatures have been washed into the swamp here, and they serve as food for the smaller carnivores of the land.  Baby crocodiles and alligators snap up these small creatures and are sustained by the ocean as much as by the swamp's own systems.  To the south is a port city which no longer has any overland trade routes.  Only those who come to the city can trade directly.  People in other lands must wait for the ships of Port City to reach nearby ports where overland trade routes are established.   } {mesolar} {} {swamp} {} {1.000} {}
