R {13700} {0} {<138>} {A narrow strip of beach} {<138>, `<088>} {  Close to the sea the inviting, crystal waters washing upon the shore offer a cool relief and somewhere to get rid of all the grains of sand that have lodged themselves all over and in the clothing of unsuspecting visitors.  Further out to sea, some sort of fin rides above the ocean briefly before plunging back under the waves.  To the southeast the Greyhare Stream flows into the sea where erratic tides and under currents change drastically over the span of a day multiple times, making it an unsafe place to swim.   } {mesolar} {} {beach} {} {1.000} {}
