R {13704} {0} {<138>} {Haytlan Beach} {<138>, `<088>} {  Joining the Greenwart Swamp and the southern ocean, the white, pristine sand of Haytlan Beach squeaks under the feet of almost anyone who crosses it.  Little puffs of sand and bits of seaweed are stirred by a vagrant breeze.  Over the centuries small parts of armor and fragments of weapons have washed ashore from the great war.  Apart from this unusual fixture of the beach it is like any other, shells of all sizes have washed up on the shores, ranging in size, shape and color.  Some more smooth than could be imagined, while others have tiny little ridges over them, and yet more that are covered in spikes.  High over head, sea birds cry and dive towards the waters looking for food.   } {mesolar} {} {beach} {} {1.000} {}
