R {13712} {0} {<228>} {Approaching a port city} {<228>; ;<088>} {  The tall, dark trees and thick, green vines and streamers of moss give way here to a sandy beach.  The oozing mud is now mixed with the white sand of Haytlan Beach, and the smell of salt is heavy in the air.  Small animals scurry here and there, mostly trying to stay out of the stomachs of the snakes which seem to infest the swamp.  East of here is a city which has grown up on the coast.  Unfortunately, during the great war, the Trolls and Minotaur worked very hard to make sure the soldiers of the city would stay at home.  To that end, they systemmatically destroyed every road leading out of the city and through the swamp.  Leaving a small contingent of the Minotaur army on Haytlan Beach was also just enough of a threat to keep the soldiers pinned down in the city.  The residents of the city have never rebuilt the road, since the swamp has become more dangerous, and sea trade is now so profitable that all of the city's exports travel by ship to other seaports.  Only the brave adventurers who travel the swamps, or travel over the sea trade on land with the people of Port City.   } {mesolar} {} {swamp} {} {1.000} {}
