R {13762} {0} {<228>} {A hearty mangrove forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  The forest here grows up in circular patterns around large pools of water.  A mix of fresh and salt water adds to the complexity of life.  Small shrimp and crabs mix with fresh water fish, and the seagulls and other birds make good use of the small pools for their food source.  East of here the ground becomes even marshier, if that is possible, because of the Greenwart Swamp in that direction.  Here, though, the wetland is a bit more pure, the Greyhare Stream flows to the west, adding its own source of water to the saturated grove of water-dwelling trees.  The ocean to the south froths white as it comes ashore, washing bits of driftwood and small sea creatures into the pools of water which dominate the ground amid the trees.  The tunnel-like root systems of the mangroves provide shelter for many small mammals and reptiles, and the area is vibrant with exotic life.   } {mesolar} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
