R {13934} {0} {<228>} {The Boughs of the Forest Heart} {<228>* *<088>} {  The branches of the forest heart are woven like tapestries beneath you.  The tree seems mostly untouched by the eternal autumn, the only signs being wilting on a few of the leaves.  The tree stands as a powerful force against the fall. Birds and small animals still make their homes either here, or deep in the trunk of the tree.  The branches have a magical appearance\; in the right light, they look almost silver.  The bitter wind, which followed you for so long, cannot be felt here.  A series of step-sized branches mark the way back down. } {autumn} {} {jungle} {} {1.000} {}
