R {13937} {0} {<278>} {Through the Gate, Into the Market} {<278>. .<088>} {  Stepping out of the tunnel, you are greeted with the sights, sounds, and  smells of a thriving market. The imposing wall to the east provides a small  clear space in which to take in the view. Well-fitted cobblestone roads and  pathways between the stalls and buildings allow commerce to be a neverending  pastime. Throngs of people of every race move between the shops, some  shoppers carrying bundles, others workmen carrying heavy loads on their  backs. There is even a sprinkling of wandering peddlers calling out their  wares as they move through the sea of life. The shouting shopkeepers and the  murmur of thousands of voices make hearing anything difficult, and though the streets and paths are kept clean, visibility is low from the cloud of dust  thrown up in all the movement. There are dark smudges of smoke, both from  blacksmiths and from stalls where food must be sold, to judge by the exotic  and rich smells that drift through the market. } {empyrean} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
