R {13948} {0} {<278>} {Copper Avenue} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Named for its proximity to the market, and the type of coinage usually dealt  with by the more common merchants, Copper Avenue is the section of town where most of the local merchants have their homes. The street is lined with widely spaced houses, each with a small garden out front, and several sporting  stables where their wagons and horses can be kept. There is a strip of land  dividing the avenue down the center where tall Magnolia trees are  interspersed with lavender and rose bushes and the occasional decorative  fountain. While this area of Empyrean is clean, it does show a tendency to be so more by accident than on purpose. The gutters alongside the street are  filled with waste flowing to the sewers. Their stench is offset by the  aromatic plants growing both in the gardens and along the center of the  avenue\; a fact that probably speaks to the purpose of the plants being more  than merely decorative. } {empyrean} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
