R {15068} {0} {<248>} {Up the Tower} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  You are at the base of a large tower.  The stonework here is far beyond the works of any of the stone-mason of today.  Each stone is perfectly shaped, yet retains the strength of its natural state.  There is not a trace of mortar in the seems of any two stones.  It almost seems as if the stone itself is alive, breathing slowly like one asleep.  The stairs themselves are made of stone, a pure, white marble that resonates your every footstep throughout the tower, carrying it upward.  From here you can go down to the main room, or you can follow the winding path of the stairs up further into the tower.   } {darkside} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
