R {15198} {0} {<278>} {Francois' Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Francois' room is a bit of a mess. There are several cheap wooden chairs  scattered about the floor, and heels of bread sit on plates that are stacked  haphazardly upon a side table. Flies buzz around the bread in an annoying  manner and will randomly fly over to whoever is in the room and land upon  them. Several bags of luggage have been set on the ground at the foot of the  bed, and clothes have managed to sneak out of them and sprawl themselves  about on the floor. Every resident gets a basic room that comes with a bed  supplied by the nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and  groove boards an inch thick, installed vertically for the walls, and thicker  boards for the floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {31983} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15199} {0} {<278>} {Garrett's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The first thing an individual sees when they walk into this room is the big  wooden sign suspended from the ceiling that says "Bedroom of Booty". This  room clearly must belong to a pirate, or an aspiring pirate at the very  least. A cabinet that takes up one whole wall is filled with dusty containers that look like they might contain alcohol. Some are empty, and others are  full, but it seems to be quite the extensive collection. A coffee table in  the middle of the room has been painted with a skull and crossbones symbol,  and a dozen large treasure chests are stacked into one corner of the room. The only other object of note in the room is a shelf over the bed that  contains small, detailed models that are most likely depicting pirate ships. Garrett must really miss life at sea. Every resident gets a basic room that  comes with a bed supplied by the nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an inch thick, installed vertically for the  walls, and thicker boards for the floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {  667} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15200} {0} {<278>} {John's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  John spends a lot of time sitting at his desk in this room. When he is not  sitting at his desk, working through mathematical problems, he takes a  sketchbook and goes out to the nursing home's conservatory or outdoor gardens in order to create some artwork. Aside from his desk and accompanying chair,  the only other visible personal belongings in this room include a number of  textbooks that are stacked upon the floor beside his desk, and a pile of  sketchbooks and art supplies that sit on the floor on the desk's other side. Every resident gets a basic room that comes with a bed supplied by the  nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an  inch thick, installed vertically for the walls, and thicker boards for the  floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {31999} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15201} {0} {<278>} {Polly's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Polly likes to collect dinnerware, so she has a whole cabinet in this room  that is dedicated to displaying it. The cabinet has been stained a very dark  brown and is accompanied by a dining table that is stained the same color. The dining table has six chairs, but the question is, does anyone ever come  by for a dinner party? That is pretty doubtful considering the fact that most folks run in the other direction when they see Polly. Someone who could  spontaneously combust at any moment has a very tough time making any friends  at all. Every resident gets a basic room that comes with a bed supplied by  the nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an inch thick, installed vertically for the walls, and thicker boards for the floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {31999} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15202} {0} {<278>} {Sarah's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Sarah has done her best to make this room look like a bedroom in a castle. Golden chandeliers hang from the ceiling, each filled with a dozen slender  white candles. A gigantic oil painting has been hung on the southern wall  that takes up the entire top half of that wall. The bed has been sectioned  off by a partition that is made from curtains that are suspended from a  transportable metal bar. An ornate chair sits to the side of the bed, and is  meant to look like a throne, and beside the chair is an equally ornate  dresser, complete with a mirror and small stool to sit upon. Every resident  gets a basic room that comes with a bed supplied by the nursing home. They  are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an inch thick,  installed vertically for the walls, and thicker boards for the floor and  roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {32000} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15203} {0} {<278>} {Harry's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Harry's room is a terrible mess. Considering the fact that he is someone who  incessantly gets himself into accidents, you would think that he would keep  the place a bit more organized. A couple of posters have been hung up in the  room, urging folks to explore the most uninhabited areas of Andolor, but  aside from this, things have basically been thrown around on the ground and  left wherever they have fallen. The janitor hates this of course. One day,  after a heated verbal argument with Harry, he swore he would never set foot  in here again. And he has been true to his word! It is difficult to take a  step without stumbling over a discarded piece of clothing or a torn up bit of parchment. Every resident gets a basic room that comes with a bed supplied by the nursing home. They are encouraged to furnish the room further in order to add their own personal touch. Each resident room has tongue and groove boards an inch thick, installed vertically for the walls, and thicker boards for the floor and roof. } {nursing} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {32000} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15204} {0} {<178>} {The Public Washroom} {<178>[ ]<088>} {  This washroom has made an attempt at modernization. It is a single stall,  with a wooden toilet, and there is a rudimentary plumbing system in the  building, so the waste does end up in a sort of sewage system that eventually sends everything into a river. Unfortunately, it seems no one has thought too much about where the river leads to. Luckily there have been no complaints  from downriver thus far, so that is promising. There is also a sink that can  deliver running water, and a small mirror to look into in order to powder  your nose or whatnot. The smell in here is a bit intense and for some reason  the floor is all wet. Eww, so is the toilet paper. Hmm, it might not be a  good idea to speculate upon the reason as to why this room is so wet. } {nursing} {} {chesswhite} {} {1.000} {}
