R {15302} {128} {<278>} {In Pain} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Between the two, which do you choose?  Pain overrides your senses, everything hurts.  You take pain from everything around you, there is nothing that would not hurt you.  Using your senses, you decide that everything you see, hear, smell, taste, and touch is bad and painful.  The pain screams at you to do something, anything to allow yourself to be free of the experience.   } {fantasy} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {15301} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15303} {128} {<278>} {In Pleasure} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Between the two, which do you choose?  Pleasure overrides your senses, everything feels good.  You take happiness from everything around you; there is nothing that would not please you.  Using your senses, you decide that everything you see, hear, smell, taste, and touch is good and pleasant.  The pleasure that you take tells you to do something, anything to allow yourself to continue experiencing it.   } {fantasy} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
