R {15330} {128} {<218>} {Altar of the Blood} {<118>(<178>~<118>)<088>} {  This altar is very familiar, holding a book that has words of power scribbled in it. At a quick glance, the words "How to", "power", "slaves" and "failure" are visible. This is, or was, obviously the gathering place for the Blood. Behind the altar is a circle, closed shackles made from iron and dipped in  blood lying in it, which is probably the bonding magic the "fabled"  Meirin'davel used. From the edges of this circle, some black smoke rises,  which probably was made to keep stray hands away. It might not be, but best  not take the risk of losing your main or off-hand. From up here, the rest of  the Chamber of Salvation is visible to the south. The strange mosaic now  creates a picture, though not too visible. It is a tree with a pointy tip,  like a needle, and people at the tree's base, looking as if they are praying. The back of this platform for the altar holds paintings of a man - Crynn -  and demons, groveling at his feet. Another painting of Meirin, angels  groveling at his feet in contrast to the previous one. The floor here is  smooth and paved with more of this strange dark red stone. The only things  standing out are glyphs around the circle with the shackles, probably also  something to help this ancient bonding magic. } {sanctum} {} {hellfountain} {} {1.000} {}
