R {15584} {0} {<278>} {Aethelgyth's Chambers} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Aethelgyth's room is elegant but very simple, like the rest of the fortress. There is a bed against one wall and a bathroom to the side. Gyth is here  waiting for her son, Cenwig to be through with training and lessons, She is  sitting on her bed considering the issues at hand. } {omentor} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {15583} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15585} {0} {<278>} {Cadmon's Chambers} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This room is the chamber of Cadmon, mate to Aethelgyth, Witch Queen of the  Burh. This room is actually two rooms. One part of it is Cadmon's bedchambers and the other part is his office. In his bedchambers is a large bed with  satin sheets, no doubt Aethelgyth's favorite, and it holds a few personal  momentos. For one of the most powerful warriors of Omen Tor, Cadmon prefers  the simple and less cluttered look in his room and in his office. In his  office is a large desk covered with papers and documents. Next to his desk is a balcony overlooking the wild and beautiful ocean that beats upon the cliffs of Omen Tor. } {omentor} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {15583} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15586} {0} {<278>} {Training Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Here is where young Cenwig received most of his training as a warrior and as  a future head of the Fortress Aethelburh. The room is spacious, with plenty  of room for sparring. Surprisingly, books line one of the walls and there is  a table with several books opened upon it. } {omentor} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {15581} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15587} {0} {<278>} {A Guest Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This room is very small compared to the other rooms you have seen in  Aethelburh. An old woman sits across the room from you. She stares at you,  making you start to wish you hadn't come in here. She is sitting there with a scowling look on her face. There is only a bed and a chair, in which the  woman is sitting. Perhaps that old crone is waiting for someone. But as you  start to walk around she starts to talk in an odd tone and you completely  forget where you are. } {omentor} {} {inside} {safe} {1.000} {}
E {15581} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {15588} {0} {<278>} {Cenwig's Bedchambers} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you wander into the elevated foyer to Cenwig's room you can see him  sleeping peacefully. A grand room lies before you. Tapestries around the  walls of the room depict Cadmon's many victories. The Room is made from wood  paneling and the floor is of black marble. On the wall is a statue of a  female staring down at Cenwig's sleeping form. Her eyes are made from the  rarest sapphires and the rest of her body is made from Black Onyx, a rarity  in Omen Tor. This statue likely cost as much as a peasant makes in a whole  lifetime. } {omentor} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
