R {16565} {0} {<228>} {The Hive} {<228>( *<088>} {  Stepping through the overgrowth, you find yourself standing before the biggest hive you have ever seen.  The hornets have cleared away all forms of plant life from around a huge tree and built their nest around it.  The giant pulsing mass of chewed, paper-like material bulges with the weight of the hornets inside as they go about their given jobs.  From the center of this enormous mass a huge bee head protrudes\; most of its body is concealed within the fifteen-foot-tall nest.  It appears to be at least twice as big as any of the other bees here, and your impression is that this must be the queen.  The queen stares back at you, antennae waving wildly, as a group of hornets swarm from the nest and hover in the air before her, ready to defend the hive.   } {fens} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
