R {16873} {0} {<148>} {The Path of the Dead} {<148>. .<088>} {  This rough-hewn hallway is more recent, and much less developed than above.  Dirt packs the walls and floor, and granite lines the ceiling.  Cross-timbers support the hallway (where did they find cross-timbers?)  from collapsing, yet still, threads of dirt trickle from above, loosened by the excavation.  The hall is filled with the dead.  Human slaves and animals alike have lost their light here, either from starvation or dehydration.  Bones are visible in the packed dirt walls, shadows of who used to own them. The dead are buried in these walls, an unheard voice echoes throughout the passage.  The dead are buried in these walls.   } {deadlights} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
