R {16879} {128} {<148>} {The Burial Grounds} {<148>. .<088>} {  More dead have been placed in the walls on either side of this passage.  One of the skeletons has fallen out, from an intruder, or the tests of time, one can only guess.  Its bones lie in the dust now, scattered across the hallway.  The skull is long and sloped, the teeth extending from the mouth horribly.  The hallway turns to the south here, opening into a large chamber that resembles the portal room far to the east.  Several of the niches near the end of this hallway are empty - tombs that were never used, hopefully.   } {deadlights} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {16878} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16880} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16880} {128} {<148>} {The Stone Lith} {<148>. .<088>} {  This room looks very similar to the original portal chamber.  Mostly plain rock, yet pillars are carved into the walls on either side of a large portal set in the center of the room.  The portal is large, its borders carved of stone, and the center flows with a bright blue flourescence.  There appears to be nothing else of interest here.   } {deadlights} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {16879} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16890} {enter lith} {enter lith} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16881} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>. ^<088>} {  The thick vegetation grows denser in this part of the swamp, making passage difficult indeed.  Insects have ravaged the foliage, with dead and dying vines, plants, and trees mixed with the green growth of new life.  The brackish water is mostly still and serene, yet occasionally movement stirs somewhere below the surface, the only sign of living things beneath.  The strange, flying snakes are rarely seen here, but sometimes one will dip lazily over and snatch one of the giant insects that lay perched on the thick green vines that twist upwards from the water.   } {deadlights} {} {hills} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16882} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  The sun burns hot and low over this boggy, tepid swamp.  The scorching heat from above threatens to burn off the heavy drifts of mist that obscure much of the land from view.  The silence is broken every so often by a hesitant bird call, the sudden flapping of wings, or a distant splash of water, as if boys were enjoying their childhood nearby, engaging in a water fight.  But underneath all the sounds of wildlife, beneath the serenity of Nature's touch, lies a malevolant, gripping presence.  A presence of power so universal it is masked around the guise of this begotten swamp.  There's no question that something evil has pervaded this place.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16883} {0} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  The blazing young sun shimmers above the heat waves that slowly waft their way into the upper atmosphere.  Incredible humidity and sizzling temperatures slowly bake and broil.  Creeping vines are strangling many of the exotic trees, while busy insects are quickly rotting and eating the vines.  A black, bristling beetle the size of a fist buzzes loudly from one vine to the other, eating insect after insect and enjoying his day immensely before some hideous reptilian beast suddenly leaps from the water and devours him before slipping again below.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16884} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  Bog water lies still in rivulets across the muddy ground, home to colonies of breeding insects and bugs.  The wind has picked up a little, driving the thick mist farther, deeper into the swamp and creating a delicious breeze that drives some of the heat from the sun's touch.  The sky is a deep, dark blue, with several piles of white, fluffy clouds drifting lazily across.  A faint moon can still be seen - the other must have set.  Guttural cries emanate from the thickets, and insects buzz back and forth through the humid air.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16885} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  The crypts below seem to have exited into a large and desolate magmire.  The heavy, thick fumes of decay reek through the air, along with the scents of life and growth.  Thick, tangled vines slip in and through the muck of mixed water and mud that make up the surface.  Strange calls of alien birds and reptiles fill the air with a cacophony of odd music - gutteral bird calls and lilting replies in return from flying, darting snakes.  The atmosphere is just as crazy, with at least two moons visible, even during the heat of the day.  And it is definitely hot, nearly steaming.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16886} {0} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  The swampwater has grown deeper, and uneasy currents stir beneath, the path of creatures of the dark swimming through their wet world.  Twisted, mangled trees rise up from the murky depths and feed from the fading twilight of the setting orange sun.  The calls of nature are strangely bizarre in this alien world, the cries of birds mixing with the sounds of insects rising from the grimy water that lies mostly still.  Much of the swamp's mist has been seared off by the last of the young sun's heat, but is already preparing to resettle for the long, treacherous night.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16887} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  The bog cuts sharply away here, an almost definable line into a forested green paradise.  The ground slopes steeply upward from the wetness and rotting decay below, and stretches onto a hard, grassy knoll covered in luscious green grass and thick, healthy trees.  Birds flourish in utter abandon here, flitting from every tree and sounding birdcalls happily.  The trees thicken into a small forest on this knoll, an odd Eden in the midst of this alien environment.  Deep within this thicket of trees is a large, crystal clear pool of pure water.  Resting next to the pool is an odd sight. A large half-circle of stone sits upright, almost like a doorway.  The stone is carved with fascinating precision, ancient symbols that used to mean something.  A deep blue hue emanates from within the half-circle itself, the color of the early afternoon sky.  The portal sits, alone and forgotten, within a deep patch of trees.  The thick branches above cut off nearly all sunlight into this small grove, causing everything to take on a deep bluish tinge.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}
E {16898} {enter stone} {enter stone} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16888} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  The fairly deep bog water gives way to a muddy, sodden ground that looks ready to give at any time.  Not many trees are growing around here.  Low, bushy sprouts and small, spiked plants mostly dominate.  Perhaps the most striking are giant, purple flowers with bloated, blazing orange pistils nearly dripping from within the exotic petals.  The wildlife is very active, with fast, furry creatures running amongst the thick foliage and insects by the swarm darting in and around everything.  Thick, clustered rainclouds look like they may be heading this way soon, taking over the fading light.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16889} {128} {<228>} {On the Surface} {<228>( *<088>} {  Life of all kinds is abundant and flourishing throughout this rich, green environment.  Fanciful birds and other flying things dart here and there from treebranch to vine.  The moist, rotting smell of mulch covers the surface of the water here, where many of the trees and plantlife have rotted and died, or are dying.  Bright green shoots are pushing up through the ground everywhere, and newborn trees and brush thrust towards the sky.  The sun is a pulsing red orb against the far horizon, set starkly against the black mountaintops in the distance.  The air is still and very humid, although the heat is less fierce.   } {deadlights} {} {forest} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16890} {128} {<248>} {An Underwater Chamber} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  This chamber is completely filled with water.  No air seems to be available, even to the fish, who don't seem to need it.  Crustaceans of all types populate the flattened, sandy floor amidst the tangles of vegetation floating from their roots in the silty soil.  Almost unnoticeable are the faded, carved pillars that were formed from each corner of the room, once magnificent structures that have now been conquered by the abundant life.  The ceiling is simply bedrock, blocking off all access from above.  Air-breathing creatures shouldn't hang around too long here.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16891} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16894} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16891} {128} {<248>} {An Underwater Chamber} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  The architecture of this large aquatic chamber is very much evident, in spite of the heavy amount of damage much of the work has sustained.  The ceiling has expanded upward, becoming more of a dome, rising up nearly out of sight, obscured by the thick water.  Heavy, thick clumps of algae and seaweed cover much of the once delicate stonework, causing rock to weaken and crumble.  But what can be seen is supreme workmanship, carved from alien hands that have long been forgotten.  A large stone archway has fallen into ruins about a great passageway to the north, blocking it from further access and threatening to collapse further.  Down below, a large passage has been bored deeply into the rock that now makes up much of the chamber floor.  The bottom drops into stark emptiness, leading further into this mysterious world.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16892} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16890} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16892} {128} {<248>} {The Watery Depths} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  The water has thickened with sand and a thick, grimy muck, making it difficult to perceive anything.  The muddy floor isn't solid at all, mostly a combination of loose silt and rock, with some dirt thrown in.  Great chunks of stone have fallen from above, only partway visible above the murky depths that they are inexorably sinking into.  Dark objects occasionally float lazily by, blind creatures built to live without air and searching only for sustenance.  Barely visible through all of this is a great stone portal, covered with green muck.  The portal, once sealed tightly against any intrusion, has been slowly eroded upon from the centuries of water, and now lies open and unguarded.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16893} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16891} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16893} {128} {<248>} {The Holding Chamber} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  This large room, although underwater, has not been ravaged as badly as the outside hallway.  Large green plants grow in abundance through cracks in the rocky ground and out of the walls.  A giant circular crest has been embedded on the far side, dwarfing the vegetation.  The symbol appears to be of a heron crossing the sun, but it's difficult to make out because of the fissures that have thrust themselves deeply through the rock.  A great number of stone blocks are set to either wall, containers of some sort that yield no secrets.  A thick slab formed of some black, crystalline rock lies across the main floor of the chamber, unmarred and undamaged from the outside forces.  Nothing touches the slab, as if some ward was placed around it, or maybe the black stone has some sort of deadly power.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16892} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16894} {128} {<248>} {Deep in the Water} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  Large fish languish in the clean, clear water that has enveloped this chamber.  Thin, sharply cut steps stretch from wall to wall, slowly descending downwards.  This hallway must have been beautiful at one point, but now its appearance has faded and been overgrown by the abundant amounts of life flourishing here.  Thick, blaringly green plant life crawls up the walls on either side and drifts in plumages from the cracked stone floor.  Tiny fish dart around the larger ones, flitting between and around them.  A set of stone pillars are carved from the rock walls, lending the scene feelings of ancient secrets left to decay, and mixing unease with the tranquil serenity of this place.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16895} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16890} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16895} {128} {<248>} {Deep in the Depths} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  As the narrow, intricate steps lead downwards, the water becomes murkier and less defined.  The stone steps are narrow, but stretch from one wide wall to the other.  The stairs elongate as they stretch deeper, with cracks formed on the steps, birthmarks where strange, alien plants forced their way through the thick rock and now float in serenity all along the staircase and in the walls.  The ceiling drops with the steps, and water fills the rooms with no sign that it will ever abate.  An ancient civilization practiced their skillful arts throughout the chambers, leaving scenes of beauty on the walls and delicately carved rock in all places.  As the staircase finally finishes its lengthy descent, it opens into a chamber to the east.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16896} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16894} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16896} {128} {<248>} {The Firing Chamber} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  Again, this chamber has been carved through solid rock, it seems.  Although slime covers much of the walls to each side, fragments are still visible, covered with artfully etched carvings that are undefinable in this aging state.  Curiously, unlike the previous rooms, there are odd blocks that extend from the walls at various points.  There seems to be no sequential order that can be made sense of - they are just there.  But most strange of all is the sloping black pool that lies in the center of the watery chamber.  The black liquid in the pool does not mix with the water, but stays completely level with the stone floor.  The pool seems to lead deeper inside.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16897} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16895} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16897} {128} {<248>} {Deep Within} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  Although this chamber seems to be filled with black ink instead of water, it doesn't bother any of the underwater creatures that dwell here, for light is alien to all of them.  Algae and green growing plants have taken over everything, changing the environment so radically it would be unrecognizable to its creators.  Barely seen, a large crest dominates the far wall, although what the crest symbolizes will never be known.  Like the chamber above, many odd blocks extend from the walls at seemingly random points and with no order whatsoever.  Against the back wall of the room lies a circular portal of some sort.  It is open, and seems to contain some kind of bluish liquid that glows with great light, but barely illuminates the dense ink.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {16896} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16898} {enter stone} {enter stone} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16898} {128} {<268>} {Beyond Centauri} {<268>. .<088>} {  Silence.  Utter cold is all of existence, along with being baked by radioactives.  Deep in the stark blackness of empty space, the vacuum of absolutely nothing stretches on for infinity, broken only by the brilliant thousands upon thousands of hard, shining diamonds.  Solar winds from Alpha Centauri rush outwards from the bright, nearby star in giant bursts without ending.  In the total and complete emptiness, a rock, nothing but a small asteroid, sits alone nearby.  Glints of metal from the rock betray signs of intelligence in this bereft, hellish nothingness.  The harsh vacuum destroys nearly everything living once blood begins to boil, except for an exceptional few.   } {deadlights} {} {air} {} {1.000} {}
E {16899} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16900} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

