R {16901} {128} {<268>} {Near the Asteroid} {<268>. .<088>} {  Growing closer to the small asteroid, it becomes evident that the rock was once a site of geologic activity.  It was blasted apart a long time ago and the parts drifted back together, more or less.  There are gaps.  Rifts.  Lots of empty places for the things to work their way in that are not supposed to be there.  It appears that ice causes the glinting shimmer from far off.  There is a substantial amount of it, or something else frozen, on the surface, and presumably deeper as well.  There are also obvious signs of past-intelligent life on the rock.  Several large, domed buildings can be seen.  It looks like some sort of outpost.   } {deadlights} {} {air} {} {1.000} {}
E {16902} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
