R {16903} {128} {<278>} {Within the Domed Building} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The dome is hollow, so the inside of the building is very large.  What look like big telescopes are mounted on a metal gridwork suspended about halfway to the apex.  There are hundreds of them, all pointing out through a large hole at the top of the dome.  Computerized hardware full of flashing, multicolored lights surround the outside walls.  A raised platform leads to a corner full of digital equipment.  There is only one obvious exit.  In the center of the room, directly beneath the opening, is a formidable bank of computers, rising up to the metal gridwork.  Within all of the switches, buttons, and lights, in the center of all of this technology, is a large, glowing portal.  Diffused, blue light flows steadily from the portal, giving everything an unworldly appearance - which it is.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16904} {enter technology} {enter technology} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16904} {128} {<278>} {Incinerating in Magma} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Thick and searingly hot lava swirls slowly in all directions, eliminating nearly all of the natural senses, except for the glaringly obvious one.  Skin threatens to melt and bones shatter, marrow boiling from the explosive heat.  Sight is impossible with the incredible pressure from the surrounding magma pushing inexorably into all available orifices.  Within the insane temperatures, movement can be felt from small currents flowing through the lava, revealing the unaccountable existence of life where none should exist. There appears to be no restriction on movement, and the lava seems to travel in all directions forever.  Disorientation is very bad, but strong currents seem to be sweeping upwards and further down.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16907} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16905} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16905} {128} {<278>} {Through a Narrow Lava Tube} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Like a capillary, this small vein forcefully pumps the magma with dizzying speed upwards and northwards, where the tube seems to expand.  Although this tunnel seems small in size, the narrowing walls still cannot be reached without an effort, and the breathtaking quickness of the current is easily underestimated.  Frequently, lumps of mass speed by, organisms that have no right to exist here, yet have mutated or adapted to this extreme environment.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16904} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16906} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16906} {128} {<278>} {A Dead End} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The intensity of the lava flow seems to dissipate a bit here, swirling in all directions in a confused state.  Inevitably, the magma is drawn through a series of spiked, jagged vents, much too narrow for a safe passage through.  Although it is hard to discern, the area is shaped like a globe, with the vents near the top.  It appears that there is no other exit from this chamber.  Except.  Yes, except that nearly unnoticable blue glow filtering through from the bottom.  Sheltered by an outcrop of rock, there is a shimmering blue sphere.  The sphere seems to meld and fluctuate with the eddying currents around it.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16905} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16907} {128} {<278>} {Incinerating in Magma} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Searing magma slowly mixes and coagulates as the lower temperatures affect the boiling liquid rock.  Currents slowly pump and push lava in eternal patterns, the bubbling and seething, red and yellow starburst designs being thrust like blood through white-hot veins of cooling magma.  If this is not hell, then it is surely the very center of a strange, alien world, with the brutally intense lifeblood of a planet swirling through the eons.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16908} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16904} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16908} {128} {<278>} {Through a Very Narrow Lava Tube} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The pressure is greatly increased as the passage becomes more and more narrow.  Melted rock oozes through the thinning tube, being forced and driven as the hollow gets smaller and smaller.  Soon the walls can be grasped on either end, and it narrows still.  Finally, the passage widens and the current stiffens as the flow cascades in a momentous rush, swirling about in a large room to the east.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16909} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16907} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16909} {128} {<278>} {The Dome of Brilliance} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The lava has dispersed and widened in its flow, circulating about a tremendous chamber that is almost blinding in its brilliance.  A large, coiled core of phospherous, melted rock and stone brews about the center of the dome-like room.  Waves of unbearably seething masses of plasma and melted metals sweep outwards in rings from the center, eviscerating all in its path.  Currents eddy and flow in large, swirling circles around the inner core, a strikingly beautiful phenomenon.  A large, gaping rift gouges across the bottom of the sphere, freeing entrance downwards, and a cleft in the eastward wall of rock allows passage.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16911} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16910} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16908} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16910} {128} {<278>} {Inside the Broken Cleft} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This short, stubby niche is nothing more than a large crack in the wall.  Besides melting rock and magma, with the incredible heat and pressure involved, there really does not seem to anything much of interest here.  Not counting, of course, the large blue-shaded rip in the rock.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16909} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16891} {enter rift} {enter rift} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16911} {128} {<278>} {Formations of Wonder} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The wonders of this room are not visible from above, and are barely noticeable here.  Through the coagulating magma, sparks of glitter-like jewels can be seen strewn around the chamber.  Upon closer inspection, the bottom and lower sides of this crevice are covered with natural crystal formations.  Not recognizable crystal types, perhaps, but they are very breathtaking, regardless.  Some of the formations have taken eerily sentient shapes, while some merely crowd together in a jumble of meaningless, shining diamonds.  The oddest creation lies in the bottom center, where countless formations have combined into what looks suspiciously like a doorway, lying across the bottom in this desolate place.  A glowing blue aura can barely be discerned through the lava.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16909} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16912} {enter crystal} {enter crystal} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16912} {128} {<278>} {Blinding, Reflecting Beams of Light} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Rays of light duplicate and reflect as they bounce from the countless thousands upon thousands of beautiful, complex crystal formations that have formed everywhere within sight.  This effect is magnificent, if startling, as light is refracted in a thousand directions, spilling torn rainbows in fragments.  The source of the illumination is not clear.  Light seems to emanate vaguely from all around.  A forest of clear shards form amazing arrangements as they crowd along the ceiling, the floor, and the surrounding walls.  It looks like a miracle of nature - if it was formed naturally.  A shaded, barely discernable opening leads the way south, narrowing so closely that some of the formations almost touch.   } {deadlights} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {16913} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16913} {128} {<278>} {The Crystal Cavern} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Tens of thousands, if not hundreds of thousands of ice-like crystal formations cover every foot of the cavern that has been created.  It looks like this is something similar to an amethyst geode, jumbles of sharp crystals everywhere and a violet hue overshadowing everything.  They shatter into dust at the slightest touch of another object, miniscule motes of glitter floating gently to rest.  Exits lead north and south from this gigantic chamber, and to the east lies the first evidence of intelligent beings ever having visited here.  An unimaginably heavy pair of gates have been imbedded to the east.  Of tremendous size, the pair of heavyset doors are slabs of what appear to be nickel iron, copper, or some other similar substance.  Corrosion lies its heavy hand over the gates, and the device inscribed upon the face has been lost to the ravages of time.   } {deadlights} {Key on sea turtle at 16893} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
