R {16924} {0} {<228>} {The Disappearing Firmament} {<228>, `<088>} {  The number of the grains of sand on a beach are miniscule to the amount of stars in this universe.  Yet, without fail, they continue to fade, to disappear, to die with an abrupt sense of finality that borders on a world of the damned.  Finally, and with absolutely no fanfare, the last of the visible suns empty themselves into the thin strands of whatever time is left.  To gaze upon the heavens now is to look upon a Great Void, one that is dead and has no meaning anymore.  There is no Voice of God shouting "It is Finished!"  , and no Odin arrives to greet the last of his children home. There is simply Nothing, except for this world where the known remnants of life destroy each other quickly and permanently.   } {deadlights} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
