R {16929} {128} {<248>} {Drowning in the Styx} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  The Styx of ancient legend is the distant cousin of this formidable waterway.  The liquid that flows and pulsates in giant currents and eddies between the rock walls is about the thickness and consistency of blood, but is a dark purplish, almost black color.  Above, nothing can be seen but the thick and mired tar-stuff that extends everywhere.  The walls that rise up at about a hundred feet on each side are formed of some hard black substance, descending and rising up out of sight.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
