R {16937} {128} {<148>} {Above the Styx} {<148>. .<088>} {  The stark, brooding resemblace of the aged Styx seems to literally go on forever in all directions.  Even as one travels further upward, using the black wall for some form of direction in this thick void, the Styx seems to head upwards forever.  Only by coincidence, sheer luck, or fate, does the sightless hole that drifts within touch allow entrance away from this hellish abode.  Travelling further into the hole leads towards the end of this crusade, or for some reason the Styx dwells with eternal animosity back downwards.   } {deadlights} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {16929} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {16938} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16938} {128} {<148>} {The Path of the Dead} {<148>. .<088>} {  The souls that were so faint as to be nearly undetectable before, now swarm about the living with great force.  Some of the souls are barely visible, almost totally dissipating into the universe.  Others are so terribly powerful they seem like demons in themselves.  Most of the tortured beings simply swirl in many numbers like a whirlwind through the great cavern that has opened up above the Styx.  A slow stream of souls seem to be getting sucked slowly towards the north, as if something is drawing them unwillingly towards it.  Scratched marks cover the northern wooden door.  They scream with the most agony and terrified cries that drown out the other wails.  The screams of the damned echo throughout the cave, madness and abandoned hope lying so thick in the air as to be almost seen by the living. } {deadlights} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
