R {16945} {0} {<248>} {The Sea of Eternal Torment} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  The environment here is very different than the previous parts of the raging sea.  The water seems clean and almost pure, with no contaminants.  The visibility is very good, although there isn't much to see except for the boiling waters that stretch everywhere.  An aura of calm seems to tread the currents around here, as if something was consistently going right.   } {deadlights} {} {underwater} {maze} {1.000} {}

R {16946} {128} {<228>} {At the Center of it All} {<228>, `<088>} {  This is so completely different from the previous environments that it is truly stunning and totally breathtaking to take in the present surroundings. An awe-inspiring bridge of colossal proportions stretches in both directions to the maximum amount of visibility, threatening to touch both distant horizons.  Once details become perceptible far, far below the bridge, the relativity staggers the mind.  Mountain ranges stretch out broken and shattered peaks in the far distance beneath the bridge, and any wildgrowth or civilization is much too small to be visible at this great height.  The bridge itself spans many miles across in width, and is formed of a glittering black material.  A handful of humanoids are perched on the bridge, watching the utter destruction of this universe approach at a frenzied pace from the western horizon.  Great gales of wind sweep across the wide black expanse of the bridge, threatening to sweep all those on it down into the wild blue.   } {deadlights} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {16947} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16947} {128} {<268>} {Within the Storms of Chaos} {<268>. .<088>} {  The wall of "storms" that is approaching the bridge seems to be literally giant cyclones of living things - nasty, black, maggot-like creatures with great rending teeth all over their long, twisting bodies.  Biting, tearing, and consuming everything they touch, it is truly a wave of death, eating this world alive with astonishing rapidity.  Larger creatures dwell within the swarms, but they are nearly impossible to distinguish from the black masses that cloud visibility.  How anything can withstand this sort of awesome power is beyond imagination.  Even dwelling for brief periods in this area is surely signs of insanity.   } {deadlights} {} {air} {} {1.000} {}
E {16937} {enter pool} {enter pool} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {16948} {0} {<228>} {The Coming of the White} {<228>, `<088>} {  At first, one is greeted with utter blackness, as still and void as it was before the universe was created.  This exists for a long while, the emptiness of Nothing buzzing steadily, the silence and loneliness of generations seeming to pass by.  Then, slowly, with nothing to herald it or make one think it was even there before it was, comes a low whisper of voices too low to be heard.  As time passes, or perhaps no time passes at all, the whispers grow steadily louder until they are a tremendous chorus of trumpeting shouts, singing in blinding triumph.  The White!  The White is here, the White, the White, the Coming of the White!  And in such an instant as everything may be created, in one successive flash of a moment, a greatness almost unbearable envelops everything with such awe-inspiring totality that the ego is gone, and all that exists is the White.  Slowly, and with great finality, colors begin to fade into perception.  A garden of infinite scale surrounds everything.  The brilliant colors continue to vividly shine until they eclipse and obscure anything not divine, the beauty of all.   } {deadlights} {} {field} {healer} {1.000} {}

R {16949} {0} {<228>} {Placid Waters} {<228>, `<088>} {  The extraordinary atmosphere that fills and blooms throughout this forest is almost indescribable.  The absolute calm and serenity floating through the air endows all of the living creatures around here with spirits of relaxation and peace.  Nearly a tropical rainforest, exotic and beautiful plants, various vegetation, and many trees spread out underneath a canopy far above.  The sounds of natural wildlife living out their lives echoes and rebounds in the open air.  A light rain drifts down through the canopy, dusting everything with a light touch of moisture.  The only thing unnatural in this wilderness is the existence of four portals, one in each direction, glowing soft blue colors.  Those, and the large sign nailed to a large tree nearby.   } {deadlights} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
