R {19547} {0} {<238>} {On a Narrow Ledge} {<238>/ \<088>} {  A ledge, perhaps three inches wide, provides a relatively safe, if precarious, perch.  A black entrance lies to the east, dug into the cliffside by some unknown force.  Rather large droppings and several bones are scattered at the entrance.  The wind and black emptiness threaten from behind.   } {desolation} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
