R {19690} {0} {<238>} {Deposits of diamonds} {<238>^ ^<088>} {  Diamonds! Or at least something that looks like them. There are huge chunks  of raw diamonds embedded in the wall here, some nearly as large as a fist. Diamonds are known to form only under immense pressure and heat, and require  some carbon source. They are therefore usually only found in mines, deep in  the earth. Strange that they would form in a mountain, which only attests to  unnatural origins of this place. Furthermore, where would the carbon to form  it come from? } {terra} {} {rocks} {} {1.000} {}
E {19691} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
