R {20030} {0} {<278>} {[1;35mThe Pit[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The sharp, acrid smell of printing ink fills the air of this high vaulted  cellar. The brickwork of the walls is slightly damp and crumbling,  suggesting that the basement is older than the office building above,  perhaps a great deal older. Your attention, however, is dominated by the  masses of Heath Robinson styled equipment currently filling the air with  a ominous throbbing and clanking. Workers scurry back and forth between  the presses, tweaking a setting here, loading a fresh bale of paper  there, too busy to notice your presence. The facade of respectability on the floor above is nowhere to be seen here: This is where the hard graft is done, the very nerve centre of the publishing house, the place where  news becomes flesh (if you consider 'cheap recycled paper' to be flesh). } {gaardian} {} {inside} {safe,trainer} {1.000} {}
