R {20031} {0} {<278>} {[1;35mNewsroom Floor[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A stark contrast to the elegance and serenity of the ground floor, the nerve centre of the publishing offices is a place of raw, unbridled chaos. Harried reporters scramble back and forth, clutching handfuls of articles, shouting to make themselves heard over the general background noise of a newsroom in full swing. Desks are clustered around the room, appearing to have been placed at random, and several are creaking ominously, threatening to collapse under the weight of the paperwork on  them. The air is filled with the overwhelming smell of overbrewed coffee and stale tobacco smoke. A door in the glass-panelled wall to the north leads to the offices of the Editors-in-chief, and the corridor to the east is lined with office doors. To the west is a large, stark room which serves a dual purpose as both the cafeteria and the conference room, or you can follow the staircase up or down. } {gaardian} {} {inside} {safe} {1.000} {}
