R {20033} {0} {<138>} {[1;35mThe Archives[0;37m} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  The smell of this long, high-vaulted room is tantalisingly on the tip of your tongue, until you remember your last trip to the local library: the aroma of printed paper, accented heavily by the passage of time. Books, journals, and back issues are stacked here along row upon row of solid oaken shelves, starting at ground level and reaching up almost to the ceiling. It is often said that books of magic are dangerous things to leave lying around, and thus most magical universities and guilds employ heavy security around their libraries; usually not to keep the books from being stolen, but to keep the books from harming any uneducated soul which might try and read them without protecting himself. Here, however, is something even more potentially dangerous, a collection of history and newsworthy stories which goes back decades. They say a little knowledge is a dangerous thing, but you'd be amazed how much damage this much could do if it got into the wrong heads. The room also seems to be a repository for anything the staff feel might be useful at some point, but not right at this moment. Equipment and items donated to the publishing group poke out of shelves and corners, and you can't help but notice the stuffed alligator suspended by wires from the ceiling. If anyone finds a use for that, you don't want to know what. } {gaardian} {} {shop} {safe,shop} {1.000} {}
