R {20480} {0} {<268>} {An undisturbed coastline} {<268>~ ~<088>} {  Unlike the rest of the beach, the coast this far east has not seen any signs of battle.  The sand is pristine and the waters here are clear and balmy.  The gentle waves that lap the shore bring such peace that the phantasmal horrors you have witnessed seems like a distant memory.  You feel the clean sea breeze from the Aphasia cleanse your soul of darkness.  Its salty tang lingers upon your skin like the touch of a lover.  Up north, the last mountain of Lithaeglar towers above you like a majestic guardian to this piece of land.  The entrance to Melchos lies past its peak.   } {minos} {} {shore} {} {1.000} {}
E {20528} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {20481} {0} {<228>} {A narrow land bridge} {<228>, `<088>} {  You have stepped from a land of peace into what seems to be a nightmare.  As soon as you passed from the mainland to this narrow bridge of land, which connects Minos with the rest of Mesolar your senses are assaulted.  Visually, though there is plenty of light, a gloom seems to fall over everything, casting it in a dimmer light.  The smells of death and smoke are thick in the air, and here, next to the rolling sea, the scent of spray mixes unpleasantly with the foul odors.  The sounds of screaming and moaning come to your ears, though the sound is hollow and seems like it should be distant.  The land here is still green, the trees which grow along the sandy beaches on either side of this narrow strip of land are tall and evenly spaced along the coastline.  The mist from the sea spray brushes against your skin, and there is a hint of chill coming from farther east.  Is it really wise to enter into this nightmare?  The rumors told in many inns warn of going to Minos in search of Asterion's treasure, and all the fragments of stories in the libraries tell of how the land rose up to curse those involved in the mindless slaughter.  They also mention that any who seek to profit from that long ago blood bath are in danger themselves of becoming trapped in the curse of the land.  Perhaps they are just rumors, but there could be a lot to gain from just trying.   } {minos} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
