R {20488} {0} {<228>} {On the ancient battle field} {<228>` ^<088>} {  The original use of this land is long lost in the destruction and decay of the land.  All that is left seems to be crimson earth.  The ground appears soaked in blood and gore even though the combatants are long dead.  Their wounds are as ethereal as the spirits themselves.  The howls and cries of the struggling armies are nearly deafening, yet hollow.  This place is playing with your senses.  The noise should be too loud to hear over, yet conversation is possible and might even be preferable to a silent contemplation of the sounds.  The misty forms of the spirits flow around and through you.  Misty bodyparts lie hacked on the ground, resting where they fell.  Though it should be dry, the ground seems muddied by the struggle and the mixture of gore underfoot.  As you gaze around, you catch sight of an elven warrior raising a long sword to strike at a young minotaur, whose face is a mask of fear and desperation.  An Aylorian knight rides across the edge of your vision, leading a group of horsemen toward a village.  As he and his company flicker out of sight, you notice a small knot of minotaur berserkers cutting their way into the flanks of a diminished Reman Legion.  As the battle rages on around you, you notice that several faces turn toward you.  Many of the eyes seem to be beckoning you to join them, to help sway the battle to one side or the other.   } {minos} {} {field4} {} {1.000} {}
