R {23160} {0} {<278>} {Ye Olde Tavern} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Raucous laughter fills the place as half-drunk trolls and golems bellow loudly across the room to each other, sloshing ale onto themselves and  everything within a one-metre radius of them. Oh, the mess - but everyone is  having so much fun and getting so inebriated they can't tell the difference  between rum and water. The inn-keeper, ruddy-faced and clad in a dirty apron, busily pours drinks and keeps a sharp eye on the little house elves  scuttling across the floor carrying drinks to the noisy patrons.  The wooden walls reverberate with the cheer of the house and the oaken floor barely shakes with each thunderous step the giants take. Every now and then  someone whines as a trollish hand slams into their glass and whacks it to  the floor with a tinkle. The door to the latrine slams shut every five  minutes with some creature unable to hold his liquor, sometimes not even  fully shutting before noisome smells creep out around the hinges. This is  wholly a male enclave, with jostling and pushing and generally drunken  behaviour taking over all commonsense. Hidden behind the bar, casually masked by a tapestry, lies a tightly locked  door. Many "DO NOT ENTER" signs are plastered over the edges of the door.  What could be behind that door? } {manor3} {} {inside} {shop} {1.000} {}
