R {23414} {0} {<278>} {A Gloomy Cell} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  It's...  a cell.  There's not really much that can be said for it.  This is the one man-made place in the Guild where the walls are stone instead of wood.  And they didn't even bother painting the stone.  The entire room is grey.  The walls are grey, the floors are grey, even the single blanket on the bare mattress of each bunk is grey.  It does seem rather solid, though, this six by six foot room.  Somebody has scratched a count of hashmarks on the wall near the bunks.   } {bonds} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23413} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23415} {0} {<278>} {The Guildmaster's Office} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This office has a rather friendly nature about it, perhaps as a result of the clutter and utter chaos that has taken over here.  Somehow Leela always knows where everything is, though.  A board nailed to the wall behind her desk can't be seen for all the flowcharts and memos and missives attached to it.  Her desk has pretty much the same problem, stacks of paperwork overflowing it and threatening to spill onto the spotless floor.  A dish of candy takes up a prominent spot, and the Guildmistress cheerfully offers a piece to visitors.  The desk itself takes up almost all the space in the office- it's not that big, but then neither is the room.   } {bonds} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23412} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

