R {23484} {0} {<148>} {Leela and Callyen's Lair} {<148>. .<088>} {  As Guildmistress (and therefore senior Bondedpair), Leela and Callyen are entitled to the largest lair available in the Crag.  Instead, they chose this one, more convenient to the rest of the Guild but still quite roomy.  Everybody knows that Leela is almost always available to her people when they have questions or problems, and the result is almost fanatic loyalty from the Guildmembers for their leader.  Leela hasn't wasted much time or money on decoration, but the lair is cozy and comfortably furnished.   } {bonds} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {23482} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23485} {0} {<148>} {Jaci and Amerien's Lair} {<148>. .<088>} {  Jaci maintains a home here for herself, her offspring, and her partner dragon.  She also tends to be a very busy woman, and rather weary by the time she returns home at the end of a day in which probably not everything got done that she wanted.  That probably explains why, more often than not, the place is a mess.  Four-year-old children are not conducive to maintaining a perfectly clean environment, and every time Jaci's mother shows up for a visit, poor Jaci gets a lecture on how she's keeping the place.   } {bonds} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {23482} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23486} {0} {<148>} {Aliana and Islien's Lair} {<148>. .<088>} {  Aliana and Islien have just recently taken up residence in a lair of their own, and they've been students for so long that they have only a few belongings of their own.  The lair is achingly empty of decoration except for the curtain stretched across the mouth of the cavern.  It's doubtful that Aliana has really taken much notice of that fact, though- the only thing important in her eyes is her beloved partner.  Everything else could disappear and she'd never notice.   } {bonds} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {23483} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23487} {0} {<238>} {Jarik and Julani's Lair} {<238>/ \<088>} {  This lair seems to be in a bit of a jumble- Julani and Jarik only recently married and had to move into a lair meant to house two dragons and their partners.  Although Julani has tried to get the place set up in the few free hours she has, it always seems that something pops up to take her away from that task.  Baby dragons with indigestion and their frantic partners, planning a field trip for the students, making sure the livestock herds don't need replenishing...  Oh yeah, and trying to get Jarik un-arrested yet again.  She's becoming rather practiced in that task.   } {bonds} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
E {23483} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

