R {23496} {0} {<148>} {Arrogance Square} {<148>. .<088>} {  This alley doesn't really have an official name, but Taryl dubbed it Arrogance Square with a smirk after the first time the Chief of Security used it.  When Fitzcairn took over the job, he designated this spot for public punishments- everything from floggings for minor offenses to executions.  It hasn't been the deterrent he hoped, and the stocks and whipping post here are used almost daily.  The guillotine is saved for special occasions, and Fitzcairn acts as executioner himself.  The terminations are great crowd-pleasers, and the Square is always packed with denizens and street vendors at that time.   } {bonds} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {23494} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23497} {0} {<148>} {The Underground} {<148>. .<088>} {  The deeper one goes into the Underground, the worse it gets.  There's a definite squish underfoot now, and people have often been convinced to buy entirely new boots after they get outside and see what's on the old ones.  There's a little bit more light here, shining from a small window in the door to the south, but illumination is still more or less nonexistent.  The odors are stronger here as well, often causing nausea to those not yet acclimated.   } {bonds} {} {underground} {pk} {1.000} {}
