R {23512} {0} {<278>} {A Dusty Crossroads} {<278>-+ <088>} {  The noise here is unbearable. The screaming of stone being hewn by picks and  hammers, the screech of metal carts against rusted rails, and the constant  barking all combine into an intolerable cacophony. Tattered burlap tents open to the south and east, each one emitting more barks. The tent to the east is  quite a bit larger than the one to the south. A sign can be seen above the  tent to the south. To the west leads a path down into the pit. You can also  see the front door to the white building. Unlike the two closest tents, a  third tent stands atop some rubble to the west. This tent is smaller than the other two, but is much less tattered and has been erected strong enough to  keep out any debris that may fly in with the breeze. } {quarry} {} {crossroad_nw} {} {1.000} {}
