R {23513} {0} {<278>} {Entrance to the Quarry} {<278>- -<088>} {  As you get closer to the pit, the rumble of mining carts, hammers, and  chisels overwhelms any other noise from the camp. Although less deafening  than the barking of the gnolls, the sounds coming from the pit also comes  with vibrations. The rubble path turns more solid as you approach the descent into the pit to the west. Looking over the edge of the pit you can see the  narrow path leading downward at a dizzying incline. The door to the stone  building faces south, and has clearly been repaired multiple times. Barking  comes from both north and south of the road. From each direction, the barking sounds drastically different. The staccato barking from the tent to the south is monotonous and abrupt, while the rhythmic barking from the north varies in pitch and tone. } {quarry} {} {road_eastwest} {} {1.000} {}
