R {23519} {0} {<278>} {Ol' Nutzo's Shack} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Considering a hermit lives here, it is amazingly clear of clutter. Papers  have been stacked neatly on the floor, all plates and utensils are free from  any food, the bed is neatly made, and clothes are clean and stacked against a wall. Despite how clean the shack is, there is a noticeable lack of  furniture. In fact, there is no furniture. The wooden shack shows signs of  repairs, and is not as unstable as it appears. Windows are on either side of the door to the south, and offer a surprisingly clear view of the quarry  below and the camp above. } {quarry} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23559} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23520} {0} {<238>} {Downward Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  As you descend into the quarry, the incessant barking from the camp gives way to the sound of work. The occasion crack of a whip dominates chisels and  hammers pounding against the stone and metal tools repairing metal tools. You can see the path winding down hugging the wall of the cliff, undulating  into the deepest parts of the quarry. Hauling bricks up and sending supplies  down have created a smooth surface that could prove dangerous if it got wet. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
E {23521} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
