R {23521} {0} {<238>} {Downward Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  The incline in the section of the trail is not as steep as it once was. A  bench carved out of the rock face looks as if it was once well used. That,  however, is no longer the case. Slavers at one point stationed guards at each end of the bench to restrict its use to regulated break times, of which there were always very few. Guards are no longer regularly stationed here, as the  slaves know better than to sit. Despite the lack of use, the bench is  noticeably void of stray rocks. The trail continues to the south, before a  sharp curve following the quarry wall to the east. Looking over the edge, you can see more road descending to the floor of the quarry. The mass of vines  above the wall have drooped low enough to almost touch the abandoned bench.  The hustle and bustle of quarry life is almost overwhelming. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
