R {23522} {0} {<238>} {A Curve in the Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  The path levels out to almost even as it curves. The incline remains steep on both the northern and eastern sides of this corner. Rocks have been piled up  in the corner, unusable masses of stone that have been scrapped without being shown to anyone of import. Without access to the bench, this is the only  secret respite the dwarves are able to afford, pretending to unload unused  stone while taking a quick break. Somewhere below, the sounds of metal  working cuts through the constant chipping away at rocks. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
