R {23523} {0} {<238>} {A Steep Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  The incline heading down into the quarry is dangerously steep here. Even the  dwarves can be seen using caution ascending and descending through this  section. Past the incline, the path appears to level out briefly. Pebbles  cause miniature avalanches as they tumble down to the end of the slope. The  rock face of the quarry wall is no longer as smooth as above. Small holes  riddle the wall, perfectly round and deeper than can be seen. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
E {23524} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23522} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23524} {0} {<238>} {An Even Surface} {<238>. .<088>} {  Mounds of pebbles have gathered at the bottom of the steep incline above. Looking up, it's a small wonder that anything has been hauled up the slope. This is the busiest intersection in the entire quarry; dwarves rush in and  out of the cave carved into the wall to the south. The cave seems to be  broken up into three separate sections, each with its own specific purpose. Because of the traffic this area sees, it also allows the widest breadth. The path to the east begins to descend as it narrows. More curves and slopes  can be seen before finally reaching the bottom. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
E {23525} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
