E {23523} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23525} {0} {<238>} {Downward Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  The incline of the slope quickly increases from west to east. Compared to how wide the path is to the west, this path is a mere sliver. Although it is  still wide enough to walk, it is barely wide enough for the carts to ascend  and descend safely. Even the gnolls are constantly on the lookout for errant  carts and runaway pieces of stone. A large enough group of gnolls or dwarves  could threaten to push off any unsuspecting traveler, regardless of how  surefooted they may be. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {23526} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23524} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23526} {0} {<238>} {A Steep Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  Half way down the rock face, this slope is just as dangerous as the other  two. The rock face of the quarry wall becomes rougher the deeper into the  quarry you descend. Even the holes look different here, as they are no longer evenly spaced. Pebble avalanches are more prevalent here, as most extraneous  materials being brought up from the bottom of the quarry falls out here. The  path narrows to the west, while the only other way out is down, farther into  the cacophonous cavern. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
E {23530} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23525} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23527} {0} {<238>} {Cavern of Service} {<238>[ ]<088>} {  Sweat-inducing heat blasts from this cavern. Built directly into the wall of  the quarry, this cavern is divided into three sections. Each section seems to generate an immense amount of heat and noise. Gnolls and dwarves crowd this  room of the cavern, both watching the other intently. Hammers, chisels,  carts, sleds, and other various pieces of equipment in disrepair have been  strewn about. The chaos of this room makes the gnolls wary, but the dwarves  appear to be thriving in it. The dwarves magically avoid each other as they  wind through work stations, repairing hardware as they go. } {quarry} {} {hut} {} {1.000} {}
E {23528} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23524} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23529} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23528} {0} {<238>} {Cavern of Supply} {<238>[ ]<088>} {  Although the rest of the cavern is as sweltering as it is loud, this room  offers a welcome quiet corner. The walls are lined with metal racks, each  diligently filled with spare parts, divided into category. Gnolls don't  frequent this part of the cavern, as the dwarves spend very little time here. The dwarves remove and replace the required items from the racks at blinding  speeds. If you need anything from here, you should grab it quickly and get  out lest you get run over by an overworked dwarf! } {quarry} {} {hut} {} {1.000} {}
E {23527} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23529} {0} {<238>} {Cavern of Repair} {<238>[ ]<088>} {  This cavern is much smaller, hotter and louder than the rest of the  carved-out section. In the center of the room is a giant anvil, which clearly gets plenty of use. Along with the anvil are a smelter, a forge, and a giant  trough of water. Although weapons aren't being made here, it is still the most important place in the entire quarry. If the blacksmith isn't working, then  the quarry shuts down. The rhythmic beating of the anvil is deafening, and  the heat from the furnace overwhelming. Without any circulating air or  natural sunlight, this cavern is an unbelievably uncomfortable and  disorienting place. } {quarry} {} {hut} {} {1.000} {}
E {23527} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23530} {0} {<238>} {Downward Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  Further descending into the quarry, a quick look off of the cliff to the east shows the quarry floor. The noise from repairing equipment above to  harvesting stone below creates a cacophonous surrounding and unnerving  feeling. Although the trail through this section is wider than it is above,  the threat of falling is ever present and very real. Even though the amount  of traffic here is less than above, the sheer number of carts and sleds  pulled by dwarves filled with hewn stone cannot be ignored. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
E {23531} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23526} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23531} {0} {<238>} {Downward Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  Pebbles and gravel from above continue to rain down upon this section. The  slope alone would be dangerous enough, yet the debris underfoot and shower  above makes this section as treacherous as it is narrow. Both things and  people fall from the narrowest ledge of the trail onto this section. The  trails to the north and to the south are wider than here, though not by a  lot. Production has clearly surpassed safety through this corridor of the  path downwards. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {23530} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23532} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23532} {0} {<238>} {A Curve in the Slope} {<238>. .<088>} {  This is the final curve downward into the floor of the quarry. Small rocks  and pebbles have made themselves home here, despite the constant traffic. This path is much wider than that to the north, which is great because the  dwarven traffic here is overwhelming. The path to the east curves further  downward, descending into the floor of the quarry. The constant sound of  drills, hammers, and chisels echo from below, while the din of repairs cut  out all of the noise from the camp above. The occasional *CRACK* of a whip  cuts through the discordance. } {quarry} {} {trail_ew} {} {1.000} {}
E {23533} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
