R {23558} {128} {<278>} {Dormitory} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This room within the large tent is noticeably dilapidated. All of the cots  are uneven, sloping, and in a general state of disrepair. Without any  decorations, the walls of the tent have a peculiar look. Dust blows in from  under the walls, where stakes were lazily hammered into the soft ground. Dwarves are strewn about like small snoring corpses. Every few minutes,  another dwarf is dragged out by a gnoll from his "comfortable" slumber to work yet another shift in the quarry. } {quarry} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23518} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23559} {0} {<238>} {Path to the Shack} {<238>^ ^<088>} {  Below is a sheer drop off into the quarry, while to the north all of the  vines, shrubs and trees seem to create a path as well as obscure any views. From this vantage point, almost every corner of both the camp and the quarry  can be seen. Because of the height, dark cover of the trees, and rare  opportunity to look up, anything up here could remain hidden from below quite easily. The northern trail cannot be seen from below and would be difficult  to see through the trees above. What sounds like mumbling can be heard coming down the trail. } {quarry} {} {rocks} {} {1.000} {}
