R {23563} {0} {<228>} {A Strange Clearing} {<228>( *<088>} {  The paths leading to and from this part of the woods are somewhat overgrown  and rutted, as though they get less use than the other paths you've seen. You move forward warily, wondering if you are about to come face to face with some dangerous creature who inhabits this part of the woods. Instead you  emerge into a small clearing, two sides of which are made up of high rock  walls. Your attention is immediately drawn to these walls as they have been  heavily "decorated" with pictures and words. The paint used is an odd rust  colour, which you suspect may be blood and fervently hope is the juice of  some berry. The center of the clearing is dominated by a large stump,  surrounded by wildflowers and mushrooms. Examining it, you notice droplets of the same rust coloured substance dot the surface. The remains of a firepit  are on the far side of the stump, the ashes still glowing slightly. This  place fills you with feelings of sadness and oppression and you make up your  mind to leave, not caring whether it is back the way you came or farther into the woods, so long as it is away from here. } {nynewoods} {} {forest} {pk} {1.000} {}
