R {23566} {0} {<148>} {Pool Of Tranquility} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  Several springs bubble up from the earth here, forming a huge pool of clear,  cool water. There are a number of paths leading off in various directions,  though the way to the south is blocked by closely packed fir trees. As you  approach you startle a deer. It looks at you for a moment, water still  dripping off its muzzle, before bounding off into the woods. The pool itself  is surrounded by reeds, rushes and cattails and you push your way through  these, seeking to get a drink. The ground is muddy here and you can pick out  the tracks of various animals as well as a number of hoof prints. You are  somewhat surprised to note that the perimeter of the pool has been outlined  with rocks; a long and difficult undertaking considering its size. Your  thirst sated, you stare into the pool, watching fish dart in and out among  the water plants, reflecting on how far you have come to reach this place. A  loud splashing causes you to look up quickly and you watch as a young Nyne  pulls himself from the water far to the south and trots off into the woods. Once again you've been reminded that the woods are deceptively peaceful and  you are not alone. } {nynewoods} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}
