R {23567} {0} {<228>} {Signs Of Civilization} {<228>( *<088>} {  As you pass through this part of the woods you begin to notice signs of  cultivation. Crops have been cunningly placed in among the trees to preserve  the wild look of the area. The wild berry bushes which you have seen growing  elsewhere in the woods have a more tended look here and you spy a basket or  two among them. Large clumps of flowering bushes grow against the rock wall  in the distance. You happen to be looking at one when it opens and a Nyne  comes out carrying a sickle and closes it behind him. It is then you realize  that these are tool sheds and that plants have been carefully trained to grow over them and hide them from casual sight. You wonder what other secrets  these woods may hold. More Nyne are visible in the distance now. Some go  about their business, seemingly thinking ignoring you is the greater insult. Others regard you with open hostility. Still more canter off to the south. To your left you can hear water and woodland sounds, to the south the  clattering of hooves and voices raised in anger. You must make your decision. Stick to the woods or enter the realm of the Nyne? } {nynewoods} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
