R {23568} {0} {<238>} {Descending Into The Nyne's Inner Circle} {<238>] [<088>} {  You head down the sloping passageway as it leads you deeper into the ground. Earthen walls give way to ones lined with wood panels and then to walls lined in cut stone. Torches are lit at regular intervals providing ample light. Several Nyne move up or down the passage, giving you a wide berth but  shooting you dirty looks as they pass. The wood panels and stone walls have  been carefully painted with pictures depicting part of the history of the  Nyne. Hunting parties feature prominently in these, including some where  humans seem to have been the intended prey. The pictures are highly detailed  and obviously made by a skilled hand and well maintained. Quite the effort  for what is after all just a passage to get from one place to another. The  passage ends in a large open area, completely lined in grey and black stone  which makes an alternating pattern on floor, walls and ceiling. You get the  sense that this is a very special place that holds many secrets. Even amidst  the bustling activity there is an air of importance and superiority about the Nyne who gather here. In the center of the floor is a large wooden trapdoor  with heavy iron fittings. Through an elaborately carved archway to the south  you see a library of some kind. Back towards the west is the sound of falling water. Nyne canter back and forth, black and white robes swishing around  their flanks as they move. A clanking sound announces the arrival of more  Nyne wearing full armor. It's like a cross between a temple and a military  fortress. } {nynewoods} {} {tunnel} {} {1.000} {}
