R {23569} {0} {<228>} {A Curious Find} {<228>( *<088>} {  You progress on down the path. You have little choice but to keep going  straight as the woods to the west are far too dense to press through and the  high cliff wall prevents passage to the east. You've grown accustomed to the  woodland sounds by now, paying them little mind. Looking around, your  attention is drawn to an oddity in the cliff face and you go over to  investigate, noting that others must have done the same before you as a rough path has been broken through the undergrowth. A stone wall with a door has  been built into a break in the cliff. At first you think it might lead to a  path like the one you travelled to get to these woods, but looking beyond you can see where the cliff closes in once more, preventing further progress. A  sign over the door swings gently in the breeze and proclaims that you are now standing outside "The Watering Hole". The sign itself seems rather weathered, though it looks as though it recently got a new coat of paint. } {nynewoods} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
