R {23570} {0} {<228>} {An Unwelcome Visitor} {<228>( *<088>} {  Various Nyne mill about here as you enter a large grassy clearing. Smaller  paths lead off in a number of directions, some bordered with... You check  yourself thinking of the word stables, mentally changing it to Nyne homes. Clearly the Nyne are already not pleased to see you, no sense in making it  worse. You can see more Nyne galloping in from the south, some of them still  with farm implements in their hands. Your arrival in the village has  certainly caused quite a stir. Still your curiousity gets the best of you and you look around, trying to take everything in. You notice now that the  structures seem a little too flimsy to be permanent residences and are more  likely used for temporary shelter. A great deal of action is going on in the  center of the clearing and you begin to make your way over there. A Nyne  housewife looks at you in disgust as you pass, her hand resting on her flank. From behind her a young Nyne peeks out and waves shyly. When you return the  wave the mother swishes her tail angrily and stamps her hoof and the child  quickly trots away. The clearing's center has a wide sloping passageway  leading deep into the earth. Nyne canter easily up and down this, shouting  orders to each other. At either side of the entrance flags flap in the  breeze. You wonder what could possibly cause a race so much better suited to  live up above to have moved underground. Although some Nyne give you outraged looks, none try to stop you as you begin to head down the sloping passage to  find out. } {nynewoods} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
