R {23571} {0} {<238>} {The Temple Cellar} {<238>] [<088>} {  Beneath the trap door is a platform which can be easily raised or lowered by  means of pulleys. It is big enough to hold several Nyne at once or a Nyne and a lot of cargo. You lower yourself to the floor and look around. You are in a large cellar, perhaps larger even that the entire temple above it. It's been  cut out of the bedrock itself and chisel marks show clearly on the walls and  floor. One wall has floor to ceiling shelves filled to bursting with  preserved foods. The back wall has a makeshift workshop which could be used  to repair weapons and armor as well as a fully stocked first aid station. The third and fourth walls have racks of weapons of all types and set after  set of armor, neatly stacked by size and type, seemingly enough to outfit the entire Nyne population. It looks as though at some point the Nyne had been  expecting a siege of some kind and had prepared accordingly. More recently  they seem to have become a little more complacent as now parts of the cellar  are being used for more normal storage. Broken furniture, wooden crates  filled with dishes, scroll cases and boxes of books cover part of the floor. Bags of clothing lie discarded in corners. Everything is a little dusty as  though it was once meticulously cleaned but hasn't been as regularly as of  late. Close to the center of the room you discover a rune carved into the  floor, its design familiar to you. You get the feeling this room may be of  great importance, though it appears to be nothing more than a place of  storage. } {nynewoods} {} {tunnel} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {23568} {u} {open u;u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23572} {0} {<238>} {Reading Between The Lines} {<238>] [<088>} {  The Nyne's library is large and quiet. The start of the compound stretches  back to the north and continues farther to the west. The floor here has been  covered in a sponge-like matting which muffles the sounds of hooves and  footsteps. Tables have been strategically positioned around the room should  you choose to take out a volume and read. Oil lamps sit upon them, some  already lit, others with tapers beside them. The far wall has a plaque  reading "The words we speak are heard, the words we read are immortal". Tall  bookcases are ranged side by side on three walls of the room. There are  sections for literature and poetry, politics and philosophy, religion and  morals, memoirs and history, agriculture and geography. The books are of all  sizes and colors as well as topics and it is obvious that although cut off  from the world, the Nyne still take an active interest in learning about a  variety of subjects. Nyne stand around reading and speaking in hushed tones. You pull a volume at random from a shelf and look at it. It's titled "Memoirs of a Monster Hunter". Two particular volumes catch your eye however. One is  on a small round rosewood table and is kept under a glass dome on a velvet  cushion. It is titled simply "Andria". The Nyne walk slowly past this table,  almost as though they consider the book to be sacred. The other sits  unattended on a lecturn, its pages deteriorating and yellowed. Titled  "Echoside", it is noticable because Nyne walking past it invariably look away and make a warding gesture, as though to evade a curse. } {nynewoods} {} {tunnel} {} {1.000} {}
E {23568} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
