R {23573} {0} {<238>} {Between A Rock And A Hard Place} {<238>] [<088>} {  This long gallery separates the Nyne museum to the west and the Nyne library  to the east. Set in alcoves all along the gallery are statues and paintings. Some are of famous Nyne; warriors, leaders, priests. Others represent Nyne  gods and goddesses and these have small altars in front of them where the  Nyne can come to pray for courage in battle or a good harvest. Nyne priests  and clerics move up and down the gallery, lighting candles, making sure the  gods remain appeased. The atmosphere here is one of hushed respect. It would  be a completely peaceful place but for the Nyne guardians who patrol here,  keeping a watch on the entrances to the museum and library as well as taking  care that none of the offerings left in front of the altars are disturbed. One has passed you several times, each time his look growing more hostile. This time he takes a firmer grip on his scimitar. Perhaps it is time to move  elsewhere. } {nynewoods} {} {tunnel} {} {1.000} {}
