R {23575} {0} {<238>} {The Throne Is Not A Game} {<238>] [<088>} {  You've entered a large elaborately decorated meeting room, the seat of the  Nyne's power. It's not easy to be leader of the Nyne. Over the years they've  had their peaceful island turned into a high security prison, faced the  derision of the other continents and had to seal their borders and had to  contend with a rising population that was confined to the island. Yet through it all they have ruled fairly and wisely, confident in their own decisions  and power. No guardians patrol here, no clerics rush about, no priests chant  prayers. Just the Nyne Matron and the Nyne Elder confer quietly with each  other, secure in the knowledge that should danger arise they could meet the  challenge. Now they look up at your entry, almost as though they have been  expecting you to seek an audience. You move closer towards the raised dais at the front of the throne room, passing detailed murals on either side. One  shows a fully armored Nyne in mortal combat with a black dragon. The other  shows a Nyne in the garb of a ruler, hands outstretched as magical energy  pours from them and surrounds a piece of land. } {nynewoods} {} {tunnel} {} {1.000} {}
E {23574} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23576} {0} {<238>} {A Strange Museum} {<238>] [<088>} {  You pass through the archway and into the Nyne museum. You've heard various  Nyne muttering about adventurers come to steal treasure from the museum ever  since you first entered their compound so you were expecting something really spectacular. Now that you are here you find it hard to see what all the fuss  was about. The room is sort of small although it is well maintained and the  floors and walls here are of polished wood instead of the rock that makes up  the rest of the temple. It contains only seven items, each with its own  ornately carved marble pedestal. There's no glass or ropes or any other  security that you can see to prevent you from walking right up to the  exhibits. The pedestals have been placed equal distances from each other  around the room in a circle formation so that if you stand in the center you  are surrounded. Although you are all alone as you stand there you begin to  hear noises, a sibilant whispering. You look for the source and see nothing  at first, then you realize it is coming from one of the exhibits. No, from  several of the exhibits. As you edge closer you can almost make out words and a faint sound of music but it's just not quite clear enough to understand. Perhaps there is something more to the Nyne's treasures than you originally  thought and the reason for keeping them guarded underground is a sound one. } {nynewoods} {} {tunnel} {} {1.000} {}
