R {23584} {0} {<238>} {Now Boarding: The Mur-erry Go Round} {<238>, `<088>} {  This part of the festival has a black and white painted carousel. Four teams  of black horses wearing red saddles and bridles with bells on them are yoked  to the central post. The sign says you have reached the Mur-erry Go Round. The U-R have been crudely X'ed out with red paint. You give in to the  pressure of the carnies and allow yourself to be led to one of the horses,  clambering up into the saddle and a carnie straps your feet to the stirrups  moments before they begin to walk in a circle at a word from the ride  operator. As the horses begin trotting a circular wheel with four long spokes descends from the canopy of the carousel. It moves around in the opposite  direction of the horses at around head height. At the end of each spoke is a  long curved blade, something like a scythe. As it spins towards you, you  duck, marvelling at the extra excitement the ride offers. The fake blades are a really nice touch. The horses speed up to a canter and long spears slide  out from the center pole, going in and out in time to the music. Now you have to move forwards and backwards to avoid the spears as well as duck the  blades. The music reaches a fever pitch just as you hear a gurgling scream  and a thud behind you. You can't look back because you must concentrate on  the blades, but you see several carnies move forward towards the carousel and speculate that someone must have gotten knocked off their horse. However when the ride stops a minute later and you dismount, you see no signs of an  injured party. It mustn't have been serious. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23583} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23585} {0} {<238>} {Forced Onto the Funnel of Fright} {<238>, `<088>} {  A fast flowing chute of water leads into the cavernous black maw of this  water ride, appropriately named the Funnel of Fright. You try to peer inside  but can't see much. The ride operator tells you to hop into one of the boats  and take a ride. You start to protest that you've had quite enough of water  lately, having just come off the Uncharted Oceans, but he just grins and  pushes you into a boat, giving it a mighty shove. As you swirl into the  darkness beyond you examine your craft. It would be generous to call it a  boat, more like a large wash tub really, but should it sink mid-ride, you  figure you can always wade out. The tub swirls in concentric circles, torches placed high in the walls provide dim lighting and screams and maniacal  laughter echo throughout the cavern. From narrow walkways on the sides carnie workers stab at you with swords and daggers, grabbing for you as though to  pull you from your craft. Seasoned adventurer that you are, you evade them  easily, giving a cheery wave as your tub is swept onwards, mentally giving  them an A+ for props. A woman is snatched up from the tub ahead of you, the  tub listing onto its side as you come alongside. A masked man has an arm  around her throat and a dagger protrudes from her stomach surrounded by a  growing patch of blood. Nice touch to include a carnie plant in the ride. You flash a thumbs up and yell "Good job! Very realistic!" as you head into  the final stretch of the ride. A dark shadow slides under your tub, bumping  it slightly and the couple in the tub ahead of you scream as a slimy black  tentacle rises from the water, halting their progress. The man hacks wildly  at it as your tub careens on by and you shout "Leave it be, the ride'll shut  off in a minute!" and shake your head at the foolishness of non-adventurers. A moment later you pop out of the tub and back onto the fairway, shaking the  hand of the bewildered looking ride operator. "Fine ride you have there!" you say, looking around for the next one. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23583} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23586} {0} {<238>} {A Strangely Twisted Festival} {<238>, `<088>} {  You can't help but shake the feeling that there's something not quite right  here. The festival workers seem far too interested in you and although you  are sure they are paid to be solicitous of the patrons they look at you a  little too eagerly and keep encouraging you to "Go for a ride." When you tell them that you aren't sure if you have time, perhaps later, they seem unduly  disappointed. Some of them even get aggressive, grabbing at you, yelling that the festival is "Fun, FUN, FUN!!" and you must take part. You shake them off  and walk farther along the fairway towards the many booths you can see in the distance. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23587} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23583} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23587} {0} {<238>} {Tempting Treats} {<238>, `<088>} {  Ah, now this is more like it. A number of colorful booths have been set up  and hawkers stand behind them selling tasty festival food. A variety of  enticing smells mingle here, familiar and yet different. Beyond the booths a  number of tables have been set up where you can sit and eat. The tables look  rather rickety and some of them have deep stains in the wood, but what can  you expect from a low-budget festival? You remark to one of the ever-present  festival workers that you hope the food doesn't cost an arm and a leg like at most festivals. He looks at you for a moment before beginning to cackle  wildly. As he gasps for breath between chuckles he tells you that "He reckons a lot of the food costs exactly that." before he wanders off, still  snickering to himself. Strange people, must be all the travel. You look at  the signs on the booths, wondering what you should have to eat. The names and food offerings are certainly unique and they've gone to a lot of trouble with the menu. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23588} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23586} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23588} {0} {<238>} {It's All Fun and Games Till Someone Loses An Eye} {<238>, `<088>} {  Every festival has games booths and you see that this one is no different. A  number of stalls have been set up and the cries of "Step right up! Win  fabulous prizes!" echo throughout this part of the festival. You know from  previous experience that these games are usually fixed, but here everyone  seems to be a winner. Whether it's a game of Coin Pitch or Bottle Up,  Crossbow Shoot or Ball in the Basket, shouts of "And we have another winner!" resound throughout the booths. You take a closer look at the games and come  to the realization that like at all festivals, these games are rigged, but  unlike any you've seen before, these are being rigged in favor of the  festival goers. You watch as a ball is thrown wide of the basket and a carnie leaps forward, grabs the basket and rushes over, catching the ball neatly as  it falls. The games master cries out "Big Winner! BIG WINNER! Grand prize! A  trip on all the rides for FREE!" You check out the prize lists and realize  that trips on the rides are the only prizes being offered. No wonder  everyone's a winner. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23589} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23587} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23589} {0} {<238>} {A Portent of Things to Come} {<238>, `<088>} {  You've reached the very end of the fairway. To one side is a large ride in  the shape of a wheel. To the other is a wide canvas tent. A rope barrier has  been pulled across the front with a sign saying "Do Not Enter!". Directly in  front of you is a wooden display case with a mechanical fortune teller gazing into a crystal ball. You approach it and look closer. The fortune teller is  exquisitely detailed and swirls of color chase each other in the crystal  ball. Perhaps you should get your fortune told. You put a coin in the slot  and a light comes on in the case, making the gauzy costume of the fortune  teller shimmer. Her eyes blink and her hands begin hovering over the crystal  ball, fingers waving slowly as her head tilts forward and peers into the  depths. There is a DING! And a card shoots out into a slot as the fortune  teller creaks upright and the light goes out. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
