R {23590} {0} {<238>} {Behind the Scenes at the Festival} {<238>, `<088>} {  Putting a rope barrier and a "Do Not Enter!" sign in front of an intrepid  adventurer such as yourself is like waving a red flag at a bull. Glancing  around to make sure no workers are watching you slip behind the rope and  enter the tent in order to see behind the scenes at the festival. You gaze at the scene in horror as the true nature of the festival becomes all too clear. Piled around various work stations are corpses, some of them so fresh that  blood still leaks from them and puddles onto the ground. Carnie workers  bustle about here, covered from head to toe in blood and gore. At one table a worker tosses chunks of flesh into a large grinder, its grisly meat dropping  into a container labelled "fresh manwich meat". You retch. There is a large  dish containing nothing but fingers and a second with all toes. In a corner  grey, jelly-like blobs are being ground into a sludgy liquid. A carnie  struggles to extract teeth from a decapitated head, gripping it between his  knees as he grunts and pulls another tooth free with a pair of pliers,  dropping it into a delicious pot of candy coating. And in the midst of it  all, a madman juggles three severed heads. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23589} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23591} {0} {<238>} {The Fearis Wheel} {<238>, `<088>} {  You've missed your chance to get on this ride as it is already turning when  you arrive. A huge wheel towers into the air, baskets suspended from it at  regular intervals. You imagine that from the highest point you would have an  excellent view of the entire festival and are rather jealous of the couple  approaching the top right then. When they reach the top of the wheel the ride stops, the bottom of the basket drops out and with a scream they are left  hanging, clinging to the bar, their feet windmilling in the air. The ride  operator shouts "Thrills aplenty! Take a ride on the Fearis Wheel!" and  whistles to a team of horses who begin plodding in a circle around a lynch  pin which causes the wheel to begin to descend once more. You turn to make a  comment to one of the other onlookers and find yourself staring into a silver skull mask. } {nynewoods} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {23589} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23592} {0} {<178>} {The Center Ring of a Three Ring... Circus?} {<178>[ ]<088>} {  Ahhh, the circus... Popcorn, cotton candy, death defying feats of great  daring... You look around and realize with some embarrassment that you seem  to have entered into the center of the big top and are in fact standing mere  feet away from the Ringmaster. His attention is focused on the crowd sitting  in the stands in front of him and for a moment you think there is something  odd about him. Before you can figure out what you become aware that what you  first took for "oohs" and "aahs" sound a lot more like "ows" and "arghs". You take a closer look and your heart begins to sink as you scramble to find  cover. There's something very wrong with this circus and that ticket you're  holding doesn't look so good anymore. } {nynewoods} {} {chesswhite} {} {1.000} {}
