R {23593} {0} {<248>} {The Remains of the Third Ring} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  The Third Ring of the circus now consists mainly of splintered bits of  brightly coloured wood and torn up earth. Although you did not witness it  yourself, it's clear the elephants went wild in the ring before taking their  act up into the stands. Near the center of the ring lies the elephant  trainer. Surprisingly he has not been trampled and his face is frozen in an  expression halfway between horror and surprise. As you shake your head and  wonder what caused the elephants to go on a rampage in the first place your  eye falls on a tangled bunch of ropes in the remains of the ring. It looks  like the remnants of a trapeze and there's something grey beneath it. } {nynewoods} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
