R {23595} {0} {<248>} {Looking Out from the Stands} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  The center stands command an excellent view of the main ring of the circus  where the Ringmaster is holding court, gesturing expansively as he extols the wonders of his circus. The stands here are quite packed and you consider  yourself lucky to find a seat. As you focus on the Ringmaster the sounds and  sights of the chaos around you seem to fade. Panicked circus goers,  stampeding elephants and hungry ligers no longer concern you. The terrified  screams and angry animal noises become a pleasant hubbub in the background as the Ringmaster speaks. You begin to be persuaded that this is, as he says,  The Greatest Show on Earth. Then from out of the very top of the tent a  trapeze artist does a kamikaze leap, knocking the man beside you right out of his seat and the spell you seemed to have been under is broken. A little  dazed, you examine your surroundings closely, looking for a place to escape  or somewhere to hide. } {nynewoods} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
