R {23598} {0} {<248>} {A Corner of Relative Calm} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  This corner of the big top seems oddly calm. It is mostly devoid of  spectators and the stands are all still in one piece. Casting a nervous  glance over your shoulder at the still (thankfully) caged ligers, you take a  closer look around, just in case the lack of people here is an indication of  an exit of some kind. Sadly the only thing you find of interest is a  completely inebriated man sitting in the top row of seats, not in the least  concerned with the chaos in the rest of the tent. As though things weren't  bad enough, you've apparently missed the alcohol vendors. Clearly this man is proof they were here at some point, but now there is no sign of them. And you so could have used a stiff drink about now. } {nynewoods} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
E {23599} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23597} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23599} {0} {<248>} {Divebombed in the Stands} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  Turning in a slow circle you look at the destruction taking place all around  you. Whole sections of the stands have been more or less destroyed by out of  control elephants. Some circus goers run to and fro, crying out and  attempting to find an exit while others cower in their seats. Still more sit  and watch the show as though everything is normal. Perhaps they are in shock. Frightful roars emanate from the liger cage. You no longer hear the shouts of the liger tamer, though perhaps that's just because of all the other noise. You're not about to look and see his fate. Not one, not two, but three  trapeze artists hurtle down from the air, yelling what can only be described  as warcries as they slam into you, knocking you nearly senseless before  retreating back to the lofty heights of the big top. That's it, you need to  find a way out of here. There must be some way out of the tent. } {nynewoods} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
E {23598} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23600} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
