R {23600} {0} {<248>} {Beware of Stampeding Pachyderms!} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  This section of the stands has also been virtually destroyed by raging  elephants. Sadly they have left the tent completely unscathed. Suddenly angry at its cheerful red and white stripes you aim a vicious kick at the tent but  succeed only in hurting your foot. While you are jumping up and down and  muttering a string of curses something catches your eye. A tattered piece of  cloth which was once possibly a shirt has been hung up over a crossbeam of  the now shattered stands. What looks to be letters are scrawled across it. Forgetting your aching foot you rush over, hoping it's a clue to escaping  this awful circus. } {nynewoods} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
E {23599} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23593} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23601} {0} {<278>} {The Haunted Ticket Booth} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You find yourself in a large open area dominated by a banner which is  stretched between two poles. The fancy script on it reads "The Fiendishly  Fantastical Frightful Freakshow!". The banner looks like it has seen better  days. It's frayed and torn in places and has what could possibly be a few  sword slashes. As you pass under the sign the biggest ticket booth you have  ever seen catches your eye. This thing must be at least nine or ten feet high and you can't imagine anyone but a giant being tall enough to buy tickets. A  faded sign has been tacked to the front of the booth. To the right of the  booth is a fancy placard on an easel. To the left is a poster depicting some  of the wonders of the freakshow. Boosters are hyping the various attractions, their words echoing throughout the area. Vendors make their way through the  crowd, though no one seems to be buying. Tickets suddenly erupt from the slot in the ticket booth and flutter to the ground. Some of them drift quite a  long way although there is no breeze. You approach the booth and jump,  managing to grab onto the ledge and look inside the cracked smudged glass. Not only is there no one in there, there don't appear to be any tickets  either. It's completely empty. You drop to the ground and turn to make tracks out of here. A new barrage of tickets pelts into your back as you prepare to  go. Someone really wants you to see this freakshow. } {nynewoods} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
