R {23602} {0} {<278>} {Trained Professionals Only} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Clutching a handful of crumpled tickets you are now standing on a walkway  made of boards which stretches away to either side. Along the walkway are  wooden structures resembling large shacks or sheds except that the front  walls are made up of closed black curtains. Outside of each is a placard  detailing what is inside and a box with a slot for the tickets. Barkers line  the walkway encouraging visitors to come to their exhibit. You glance at the  placard and use one of your tickets, pushing your way through the curtain. The room you are now in is dimly lit with torches. A low stage spans the back wall. Several men and women in red velvet costumes with gold trim stand on  the stage. In the middle is a table which holds an assortment of gleaming  butter knives. As you watch one of the men steps forward and announces in a  loud voice "Don't try this at home ladies and gentlemen. Remember, we are all trained professionals!". You look to left and right, wondering who else he is talking to since you are the only one here. From somewhere in the wings a  drumroll sounds and each of the performers selects a butter knife with a  flourish. Tilting their heads backwards, they hold the knives over their open mouths. As the drumroll builds to a crescendo they put the knives in their  mouths, their teeth clenching around the handles. After a moment they  withdraw the knives and bow to the (non-existent) crowd although there is no  applause. } {nynewoods} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23605} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
