R {23607} {0} {<278>} {An Out of the Way Spot} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The ladder shifts alarmingly underneath your weight as you climb it. Your  first attempt at opening the trapdoor results in failure, but you give a  second mighty shove and it creaks inward on rusty hinges. You glance down  below but there's such a ruckus that no one has noticed you and you pull  yourself through the trapdoor. The room is a decent size with a low ceiling  so you have to stoop a little as you look around. It seems to be some kind of a storeroom for broken or rejected exhibits. You pull aside a couple of tarps but see nothing of any interest. Everything is covered in a thick layer of  dust, causing you to sneeze. Walking over to the trapdoor you prepare to  descend back into the chaos below when something new grabs your attention. At one end of the room is a carved marble pedestal. Unlike everything else  here it seems whole and doesn't have a speck of dust on it. Sitting atop the  pedestal is a painted wooden box. It too is dust free and perfect and you  feel drawn to it, your feet moving towards it before you can think of doing  so. } {nynewoods} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23606} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23608} {0} {<278>} {A Creature Unlike Any Other} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Stopping outside the next building you hear some squeaking noises from  inside. You look at the placard, raise your eyebrows and put a ticket in the  box. Stepping inside you are greeted by several large display tanks, each  containing curious little creatures who slither upright around their tanks  playing with their toys. These cute and unique little critters are morks, so  the placard out front told you. You watch them playing in their enclosures  while reading the signs placed beside each tank. There are water morks, fire  morks, the rare cyclops morks and dragon morks. Fascinating. They wave their  little arms about and squeak excitedly at each other and you would almost  swear they were talking. Every now and again they glance anxiously downward  though you can't imagine what's scaring the otherwise cheerful creatures. } {nynewoods} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23609} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23605} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23609} {0} {<278>} {The Final Exhibit} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This building marks the end of the line for the exhibits. There are stomping  and groaning noises coming from behind the curtain but at this point you  aren't that concerned. How bad could it possibly be? There's a loud bang and  the shed sways a little. Hmm, maybe you should take a quick peek at that  placard before you put your ticket in the box and enter. Cautiously you slip  between the curtains and into the room. It's fairly well lit and contains  quite a bit of splintered furniture. You are astonished as several cyclopses  (or is it cyclopsi?) turn their two (gasp!) eyes on you. As they advance upon you looking ready to attack you abandon all thoughts of asking them what the  plural for cyclops is. On top of everything else, with two eyes they can see  you twice as well. } {nynewoods} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23608} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23610} {0} {<118>} {An Unexpected Entrance} {<118>. .<088>} {  Well this is strange. You have always been under the impression that when you rubbed a lamp something would come out of it (preferably a genie who would  grant you a wish to allow you to understand this crazy place). Instead you  seem to have been transported into the lamp itself. Worse than that, you are  surrounded by strange rustling noises and you aren't so sure you want to know what's causing them. Torn and faded velvet tapestries cover the walls of the  lamp, revealing parts of the burnished bronze beneath. There appear to be  some scratches on the walls and the more you look at them, the more they look like they were caused by claws or perhaps teeth. You look around for a way  out and spy a concave area up above you. You can just make out a thin line  which marks it. It must be the lid of the lamp. Perhaps you can push it out  and escape. } {nynewoods} {} {redcarpet} {} {1.000} {}
