R {23614} {0} {<118>} {Exploring the Lamp} {<118>. .<088>} {  The interior of the lamp is cramped and has a musty odor which makes you want to gag as you travel farther down the dimly lit corridor. The impression is  of a place long abandoned and given over to strange magicks. You reach a  curved wall of bronze, the velvet covering nearly all worn away with time. There's a narrow hole leading upwards and for a moment you think you might  see light. Then it is gone and you aren't sure if it was your imagination or  not. Wondering if you will ever breathe fresh air again, ever see the moon in the night sky, you try to decide whether to go up or turn back. } {nynewoods} {} {redcarpet} {} {1.000} {}
E {23617} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
