R {23622} {0} {<138>} {Everything -And- the Kitchen Sink!} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  This section of the store seems to have nothing but kitchen sinks in it. They are of all shapes, sizes and conditions. Some look brand new and at  least one seems to be made of solid silver. Others are rusted and stained and have cut pipes still sticking out of them as though they were forcibly  wrenched from well, kitchens. The whole area has sinks stacked precariously  almost to the ceiling. A large sign reads "Everything -And- The Kitchen  Sink!" despite appearances to the contrary. Perhaps the small print would  explain more. A sales person leads a reluctant looking man over to a display  and yanks a sink from the middle. The entire sink tower sways for a moment  before stabilizing. The man staggers a little as he shoves the sink into his  arms. "Here you go sir! Fine selection if I say it myself. Step over here and we'll ring you up!" The man says plaintively "When I said my wife had  everything..." but is cut off by the sales person. "Everything but the  kitchen sink sir! I heard you! Think how surprised she'll be when you present her with this lovely sink. A perfect anniversary gift from a thoughtful  husband! Now if you'll just step this way..." Grasping the man by the elbow,  he leads him off towards the cash line. The man opens his mouth as though to  say something, thinks better of it and shuts it again. } {nynewoods} {} {shop} {} {1.000} {}
E {23621} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23623} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23623} {0} {<138>} {We Break It, You Bought It!} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  A long counter with counting machines and money boxes runs along this part of the shop. A number of cashiers stand by tallying purchases and relieving  customers of their coins. Other store employees push reluctant buyers to the  counters smiling and assuring them how much they will enjoy their new  possessions. The actual buying process here is incredibly well organized. There's very little waiting time and people and their money are soon parted. A number of rickety tables with fragile glass merchandise are strategically  placed in between the lines. A nudge in the right direction, the crunching of broken glass and another last minute purchase made. All of the staff are  courteous and helpful, always smiling, never leaving the customers alone for  a moment lest they miss out on a chance to help them buy something. A sign  reads "Cash Only, No Credit. We Do Not Provide Change. All Sales Final. Have  A Nice Day!" Some customers try to make a break for it but are quickly herded back. A store employee grunts with effort as he picks up a metal box and  quickly takes it through a door which is in back of the counter. A woman  begins arguing that she is not trying to steal a stuffed bear, it has simply  been biting her on the shin since she walked through the door. You can take  advantage of the distraction to see what's in the back. } {nynewoods} {} {shop} {} {1.000} {}
E {23622} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23626} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
