R {23624} {0} {<138>} {All Sales Final!} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  You've reached the back of the shop and are standing in front of a large  counter marked "Returns and Refunds". A number of people are standing in line attempting to return various items. You can hear muttered complaints about  quality, quantity and durability. One by one they approach the staff member  who greets each one with a bright smile and patiently listens to their  explanation. Then she points behind her to the large red "All Sales Final!"  sign behind the counter and waves over the next customer. An irate man  explains in a very loud voice how one of the shop's staff broke the item,  helped themselves to the price from his coin purse and then presented him  with his unwanted purchase. The girl behind the counter nods and tuts  sympathetically, then smiles and points to the sign, beckoning for the next  customer to approach. The man protests and tries to hang on to the counter  but several other staff appear to wrestle him away, breaking a china vase in  the process. "What a good eye for quality you have there sir! We'll just head to the cash to pay for your latest purchase shall we?" and they hustle away  to the cash line to pay. The man groans and begins to utter a feeble protest, but you can tell they've broken him down, a suspicion which is confirmed when he voluntarily reaches for his coin purse a moment later. } {nynewoods} {} {shop} {} {1.000} {}
E {23623} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23625} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23625} {0} {<138>} {Murder Weapons, Slightly Used} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  Display cases in this part of the shop contain various weapons, from axes and daggers that still have dried blood on the blades to a moth eaten pillow and  a bowl of dessicated food that was once possibly stew. A large sign reads:  "Murder Weapons, Slightly Used". In smaller print is the caveat: "We here at  Crazy Consignments make no guarantees that purchasing one of these fine  weapons will turn you into an effective serial killer. All sales are final or fatal or possibly both." The lines in front of these display cases are  disturbingly large as are the small tags on the items which advertise how  many people were slaughtered with any given weapon. A bidding war is going on between two customers who both want the pillow which smothered five people,  including a distant relative of a royal family member (what royal family  isn't clear). The staff is encouraging the bidding, acting as temporary  auctioneers to drive the price ever higher. The pillow, while it may look  like any other, is after all a one-of-a-kind, uniquely rare item which would  look quite lovely as a couch cushion. } {nynewoods} {} {shop} {} {1.000} {}
E {23620} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23624} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23626} {0} {<138>} {A Cramped Back Room} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  You slip unnoticed into the back room of the shop. It's difficult to move  around here, not so much because the room is rather small (although it is)  but because there's gold everywhere. Gold sits in chests, fills sacks and  pouches and lies in heaps in corners. Stray gold coins are scattered over the floor in a rough path to a desk and chair which has been squeezed into one  corner. The desk is surrounded by more piles of gold. A man sits at the desk  muttering to himself under his breath. One hand neatly piles gold coins into  even stacks. The other hand is busy scribbling away on pieces of paper. Several signs have been tossed to the side. He completely ignores you and  continues to work. Against one wall a staircase leads down into darkness,  some kind of basement or storage room perhaps. You take a step towards it but come too close to a sack of gold and it makes a clinking noise. The man does  not look up but an innocent looking stuffed bear lunges forward and tries to  take a chunk out of your ankle. Lingering here any longer is not such a good  idea. } {nynewoods} {} {shop} {} {1.000} {}
E {23627} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23623} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23627} {0} {<138>} {A Musty Smelling Basement} {<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>} {  You walk down the basement steps into dank smelling darkness. It is not dark  for long however. There is a spark and then a steady light from two candles  which sit alone on a dust covered table. Wisps of flame flicker in the air  around them and there is a soft noise, almost as if the candles themselves  are whispering, for there is no one else in the room. Shelves line the walls  as though they were once filled with stock, but they've been long abandoned  and are covered in dust. It seems that no one comes down to this place. The  room has an uncomfortable feeling as though you are witnessing something you  should not see. But still the candles draw your gaze and you find yourself  stepping closer instead of returning to the stairs. } {nynewoods} {} {shop} {} {1.000} {}
E {23626} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23628} {0} {<108>} {The World Between Worlds} {<108>.\/<088>} {  This is the World Between Worlds, a place often talked about in hushed  whispers but never seen... Unless of course you are dead. Yet here you stand, reasonably sure you are still amongst the living. Perhaps it is a large  place, perhaps not so big after all\; everything is in shades of grey, making  perspective nearly impossible to judge. The ground beneath your feet, the sky up above (or is it sky?), the very air around you is tinted in grey. There is no black and white here, no right and wrong, no good and evil. There is only  the neutrality of the grey landscape around you and finally the unemotional  judgement of The Wraith. Time and space do not follow normal rules here and  you walk, not sure for how long or short of a time, dimly aware of movement  around you, of others walking as well, though you can see nothing, hear  nothing, are not even sure how you know there are others. And then you've  walked to a different place or perhaps the place has come to you and you  haven't really walked at all. Floating in the middle of the grey is The  Wraith. To one side a staircase made of brilliant light rises upwards. To the other a staircase made of shadow leads below. Shades of grey mist travel  along both, having received the final judgement they will ever face. } {nynewoods} {} {tornado} {} {1.000} {}
E {23633} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23629} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23576} {shut eyes} {shut eyes} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23629} {0} {<178>} {Ascending a Celestial Staircase} {<178>~ ~<088>} {  Although the staircase seems to be made of nothing more than golden light, it is solid beneath your feet. It spirals upwards with no end in sight. Above  and below you shades are walking up the stairs as well and as they get higher you notice a curious transformation. As they walk up they become more solid,  till finally they are individuals much as they must have been at the time of  their death. Young and old, wounded and whole, in rags and rich garments,  diseased and emaciated, they head higher up the staircase. Still they climb  higher and still they change. Diseases disappear, hollow cheeks become  rounded and healthy, wounds heal, scars fade and vanish, the old stand  straight with renewed strength and the very young no longer look fearful but  laugh with joy. Finally even their clothing changes, replaced with  comfortable looking white garments, immaculately clean and fresh. Looking up  you can see the top now, see the newly revived slipping off in different  directions as they leave the last stair. } {nynewoods} {} {cloud1} {} {1.000} {}
E {23628} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23630} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23630} {0} {<178>} {Entering the Holy Heights} {<178>~ ~<088>} {  The top of the staircase empties out into a vast, sun drenched plain. Sweet,  warm breezes dance around the people, bringing with them an array of pleasant scents. Joyous shouts and laughter ring out as others rush forward, embracing those who have just reached the top, carrying them away with hugs and kisses. Wise looking creatures, perhaps angels, survey the scene, guiding those who  seem to need it, their gaze missing nothing. There is an pervading atmosphere of peace and happiness here, an encompassing feeling of safety and  satisfaction. No one who enters this place would ever want to leave nor would they ever have cause to do so. } {nynewoods} {} {cloud1} {} {1.000} {}
E {23629} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23632} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
