R {23635} {0} {<218>} {Eternal Squalor} {<218>[ ]<088>} {  Crude shelters which do nothing to keep out the cold or the heat are  scattered about here, filled to overflowing with people dressed in rags. The  stench is unbearable. A wild dog with foam flecked jowls and a crazed look  bounds into one of the huts, carrying off one of the people who utters the  start of a thin scream before his throat is ripped out. He writhes in agony  on the ground and then goes still. A minute later he crawls shakily to his  feet, his wound gone and makes his way back to the hut. Small puddles of  brackish water gather in depressions in the rocks but when people try to  soothe their parched throats and cracked lips the water turns to poison,  making them wretch and gag. Moldy pieces of bread are scattered about on the  ground but the moment someone seizes one and raises it to their lips it  disintegrates, crumbling until there is nothing left. Sobbing, moaning and  the demented laughs of those gone mad fill the air. } {nynewoods} {} {hellinside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23634} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23663} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23636} {0} {<218>} {A Torturous Path} {<218>[ ]<088>} {  A narrow, twisting, treacherous path winds its way between high walls of  jagged rocks. The ground is covered in sharp rocks and broken glass. Jets of  boiling hot steam erupt from cracks in the rocks. People in rags huddle  against the walls, moaning and yelling curses at each other. Small red-eyed  animals dart forward, barely visible in the darkness, their sharp teeth  biting into the people and causing them to cry out. There is only darkness  here. Where the flames and steam break through the rocks it is unbearably  hot, yet one step away it is shiveringly cold. Trails of black smoke obscure  the air, which smells like smoke and rot and death. Crude shelters have been  erected in breaks in the rocks. One of these burst into flames, the fire  quickly taking possession of the others as well and thin shouts of despair  can be heard as the people flee. There is a sense of hopelessness and turmoil here. } {nynewoods} {} {hellinside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23664} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23634} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23661} {0} {<178>} {A Place of Tranquility} {<178>~ ~<088>} {  A crystal clear stream meanders through a lightly wooded area, ending in a  pond, its bottom strewn with colored pebbles. Silvery fish splash about in  its depths. Water plants wave in the small ripples and a bird takes off,  skimming the surface of the water. Sunlight dapples the emerald grasses and  brightly colored flowers. Birds flit from tree branch to tree branch, their  songs mingling with the sound of the stream. Two squirrels chase each other  around a broad trunk. A chipmunk runs into his hole between two tree roots  while in the distance a rabbit raises its head, sniffing the air before  hopping off slowly. A family of ducks come into view paddling over the pond's surface. Leaning back against a large rock by the pond's edge is a man  wearing a skull mask, the first person you have seen in this place who still  wears clothes like your own instead of the white garments that all the other  souls wear. } {nynewoods} {} {cloud1} {} {1.000} {}
E {23631} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23662} {0} {<178>} {Protection and Peace} {<178>~ ~<088>} {  A sense of profound contentment greets all who enter here. All needs are  amply provided for, one's every desire the work of a thought and nothing  more. Comfortable benches sit in shady alcoves, dishes of fruit, cheese and  bread placed on tables alongside. Hammocks stretch between the trees,  blankets lie spread for a picnic beneath them. The sun shines and sweetly  scented breezes make the leaves on the trees rustle. In the background soft  music plays, its tones clear and pure. Everywhere there are people talking,  singing, dancing, eating, laughing, reading, engaging in any number of  pleasurable activities, all thoughts of toil and hardship forgotten. This is  it, the final rest, the reward that comes to those who were good. } {nynewoods} {} {cloud1} {} {1.000} {}
E {23632} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23663} {0} {<218>} {Torture and Torment} {<218>[ ]<088>} {  There is an overwhelming feeling of hatred here, warping everything in its  path. Feelings of anger and rage permeate the very air, tainting it with the  smell of blood and sweat. In the shadows people sit under twisted blackened  trees, their branches devoid of leaves. One reaches for a moldy crust of  bread but it skitters from his grasp, always remaining just beyond the tips  of his fingers. A cold wind whips tendrils of smoke through the air and a  mournful moan rises and falls in endless agony, an appropriate accompaniment  for the suffering. People moan and cry, gnashing their teeth, clawing at  their own flesh with yellowing dirty nails. Some attack others, smashing  their skulls on the sharp rocks. No matter how horrendous the injuries in a  moment they rise again, whole once more. The only thoughts here are of death  and hardship. This is it, the endless torment, the punishment that comes to  those who were bad. } {nynewoods} {} {hellinside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23635} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23664} {0} {<218>} {A Chaotic Corner} {<218>[ ]<088>} {  A black trickle of water which is choked with debris moves sluggishly along  before disappearing through a depression in the rocks. Large insects scuttle  along the ground and a snake slithers to higher ground. Jets of flame reveal  more craggy rocks and treacherous tar pools. A huge rat peers around with  blood red eyes before disappearing into a hole. From up above vultures survey the scene, their harsh screeches echoing through the air. The rocks are  studded with stunted trees their bare branches swaying in the wind. Sickly  yellowish-green moss creeps across some of the rocks while others drip with  moisture, creating dark spots of mold beneath them. In the midst of all this  stands another man, incongruously dressed in an expensive black suit. For a  moment you think he is like you... Then you see the wings protruding from his back. } {nynewoods} {} {hellinside} {} {1.000} {}
E {23636} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {23665} {0} {<228>} {The Not-So-Wild West} {<228>( *<088>} {  This area of the woods shows clear signs of being tended by the Nyne. There  are many crops growing amidst the trees. Here and there you see a tree stump  where one has been cut down to allow more light to reach the ground below. A  large pile of rocks is to one side of the path and as you continue to walk a  burly Nyne trots over, drops another earth-covered rock onto the pile and  trots away. There are a number of Nyne working the fields here and you catch  them looking at you when they don't think you are watching them. Farther  along four Nyne stand around a particularly large crop of what seems to be  wheat. The young plants are choked by weeds and look badly in need of  watering. One of the Nyne makes a gesture of disgust, saying something  angrily, and then gallops off to the north. After a moment or two the others  follow. You can continue on to the south or head to the east. Neither choice  seems more promising than the other. } {nynewoods} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {23666} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {23570} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
