R {24213} {0} {<268>} {Sea of Tranquility} {<268>. .<088>} {  A gentle breeze softly blows against your face. As you look around you see  that you are floating a few inches above the surface. Dark water is all that  this seemingly void world contains. It stretches out in all directions and  never ceases. The only illumination to the phenomenon seems to be the water  below you which glows with an inner light. The celestial bodies above are  just an ethereal memory of time. Upon closer inspection you realize that you  are on a sphere of water...it doesn't even look like you are in your own  dimension. As you stoop down to touch the water you notice that it is neither hot nor cold, but rather a lukewarm black liquid that may not even be water  at all. As you pull your hand out of the dark liquid a drop falls to the  surface, throwing soft ripples across the sea and towards the hazy horizon. } {ygg} {} {air} {} {1.000} {}
E {24186} {d} {open d;d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {24214} {0} {<238>} {Descent into Svartalfheim} {<238>/ \<088>} {  An eerie darkness shrouds this barren landscape as the light is consumed in  the hole before you. Deep in this mountain with the absence of light, only  the hearty dark elves can survive. The wind howls from within this dank  cavern. The relentless gusts chill the cold night sky. The pitch-black chasm  grasps for life to consume. An ominous feeling is emitted from the dark  grave. A thousand voices scream the evil beyond this shadowy abyss. A voice  echoes and fades into the silence from which it came. } {ygg} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
E {24215} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {24215} {128} {<238>} {Deeper into the Caverns} {<238>/ \<088>} {  The rugged path becomes steeper at this point. Still there is no sign of  light or life. Cold, onyx colored walls surround the rocky cavern floor. A  torch in the distance barely cuts the gloom and shadows. All light reaching  this point is immediately devoured by the infinite darkness. The cries of the earth are amplified by the stone of this tomb. A force beckons you deeper and a chill is sent down your spine. Further down the tunnel is blacker than coal and your conscience tells you there is a good chance you'll never return. Deeper into the heart of the earth you descend. } {ygg} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
E {24216} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {24214} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {24216} {128} {<238>} {Into the Darkest Regions} {<238>/ \<088>} {  The air here is stale and musty. Darkness veils you and the cold cavern  breeze makes you shiver. The sounds of bats are all around you. Creepy  shadows dance against the walls as the little light about you flickers. Your  hope burns out as you detect that the tunnel goes deeper into the earth. The  opaque atmosphere is nearly choking you. The rough walls scrape against you  as you stride by. The tunnel is getting shorter and narrower. The grade of  this trail is incredible. You hope that the darkness beyond doesn't swallow  you into its eternal blackness. } {ygg} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
E {24217} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {24215} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {24217} {0} {<278>} {Chamber of Night Eternal} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Your journey ends. Here lies a gigantic chamber no less that fifty feet tall  and seventy feet across. Giant pillars carved out of solid jet-black marble  support the ceiling. There is an onyx statue here in the likeness of Balder,  Hod's lost brother. A shadow shifts, then another. You realize the entire  room is alive with minions of shadows. There is no body to project these  silhouettes, just darkness. Squinting you can barely detect the outline of a  giant man. Fear sinks into you. The unknown figure sits there motionless. He  doesn't seem to notice your presence. The shadows seem to know him, embrace  him, and obey him. } {ygg} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {24216} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
