R {25769} {0} {<278>} {Inside the Gigantic Archway} {<278>. .<088>} {  Rising to a curved peak some 50 feet above you, the archway you stand in now is easily the biggest you've ever seen...  Or heard of...  Or even imagined!  Yet every inch of it is spotlessly clean, and was immaculately carved, crafted, and set.  Each stone integrates so seamlessly with the next that not even a speck of mortar is visible, and the entire archway looks almost like a natural formation.  Even the intricate carvings, spaced at even intervals approximately one foot apart, that cover the archway were done by such a master artisan that you could easily believe they were natural.  The designs seem to have no apparent pattern or significance.  They seem to be merely random swirls, loops, and assorted geometric patterns, shaped in such a way that if you stare at them for long enough, you can see a myriad of different half-formed images, which never quite come completely to the foreground.  It's eerily similar to the effect you get when looking at the clouds for a long time, and can see shapes emerging, but never quite defining themselves.  A little to the east, the dome opens up into a vastly cavernous space, so large it's hard to believe it's truly housed within a man-made building...   } {arena} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E {25770} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {25767} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25770} {0} {<278>} {Entrance to the Gladiator's Arena} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You are in a room so vast that it's beyond all possible imagining.  The only way your mind can even begin to assess your surroundings is by partitioning the room into several sections.  Your nearby surroundings, like everything else you've seen so far, were designed with loving care and master craftsmanship; yet here the similarities end.  No longer are dirt and grime removed with what appeared to have been the religious fervor of a horde of fanatically devoted priests, and a wide variety of stains are splattered on the ground and walls, the most common of which is a thick, sticky substance that appears to be blackening rust...  A sight any true warrior would know in an instant; blood.  The stones are worn in many places, so heavily trodden upon over the years that you cannot even make out a discernible path; it seems as if every inch of every stone has been walked on so often that what may have once been foot-thick granite is now so thin as to be brittle.  Everywhere you look you see people.  Every 5 to 10 feet a little cart is set up, with a man or woman hawking their wares to any who will listen.  Food vendors appear to be the most common, yet it seems as if you could buy anything your heart desired here.  Most city markets don't offer this much variety!  Guards, ushers, tourists, and of course Gladiators of every race and nation wander about here and there, talking, competing in various games of skill, or simply horsing around.  While the entire building is far too large to see, much less process in your mind, you can tell that one of the two most famous areas of this building, the fighting arena itself, is off towards the east.  Stairs leading up, and a ladder heading down through a hole in the ground offer other exits, but to destinations which you cannot quite see from here.   } {arena} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
