R {25772} {0} {<278>} {The Dueling Rings} {<278>. .<088>} {  This is quite possibly the most popular part of the Fighting Arena.  Here people may face each other in moderated one on one combat.  Traditional duels are the most common, each following the respective Accords set by their own nations or races.  Arbitrators are present to negotiate the terms of duels when the contestants cannot agree.  There are only 2 types of rings here; circular walls, wooden and 12 feet tall, surround a ring with a 100-foot diameter to make up the first.  Simple ropes define the other, circling an area roughly half that size.  Hand to hand combat is always conducted within the roped off rings, while duels of the "take 10 paces, turn, and fire" variety are held within the walled rings.   } {arena} {} {city} {pk} {1.000} {}
