R {25776} {0} {<278>} {The Group Fighting Rings} {<278>. .<088>} {  Located in a section of the arena roughly 500 feet squared are a series of "rings," of varying sizes.  Each ring is just an area defined by either a low rising wooden wall, generally about 3 feet high, a painted circle on the ground (usually black), or a much taller brick wall, perhaps 8 feet high.  Many of the rings have thematic decorations inside them, ranging from designs as simple as "protect the flag," to settings as complex as "protect the innocents, ration the food and water, and hold off the siege."  This is where Gladiator groups of almost any size can fight each other, stage fake sieges, or even fake wars.   } {arena} {} {city} {pk} {1.000} {}
