R {25777} {0} {<278>} {The Free-For-All Rings} {<278>. .<088>} {  One of the smallest sections designated for combat, this whole area is packed full of more "rings," no two quite alike, yet all relatively similar in design.  The general theme seems to be of a circle approximately 15 feet in diameter, closed off by a roughly hewn, low rising oak fence no more than a foot high.  Each ring is barren inside, save for the (now familiar) rust-colored stains soaked into the ground.  Gladiators may enter any ring here they choose, but once within a ring, they may not leave until they are the last man standing.  Strategy is vital here; Gladiators must decide not only which ring to enter, but to anticipate who may enter after them, and also to determine when is the best time to join the fray themselves.   } {arena} {} {city} {pk} {1.000} {}
