R {25778} {0} {<278>} {The Judge's Isolation Booths} {<278>. .<088>} {  About 20 men and women are visible through enormous glass walls, set in a perfect square at least 100 feet wide.  The sheer expense of so much glass would be enough to run 10 kingdoms for 100 years, yet the show of wealth does not stop there!  Behind the glass walls you can see ornately carved chairs, each a masterpiece in its own right, layered with impossibly plump cushions.  Gigantic four-poster beds, covered in thick down mattresses, and surrounded by imported privacy screens are tucked away in the far corner, and you could swear you even see some toilets apparently piped to a cesspool outside the Arena!  Three kitchens, complete with ovens, enclosed fire pits, and water piped in from a cold well, likely several miles away, complete the setting.  Completely inaccessible to the Gladiators from here, these are the judges; chosen for their expertise in combat and impeccable reputations of neutrality, they can be employed to set up any fair contest requested, arbitrate any disputes between combatants, or to judge almost anything related to combat.   } {arena} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
