R {25779} {0} {<278>} {The Chariots' Arenas} {<278>. .<088>} {  Possibly the largest single portion of the Fighting Arena is right here, divided into 6 large arenas.  The arenas are broken into 2 sets of 3.  The first set of arenas are towards the southern walls.  Adjacent to each other, each sports a spotlessly clean, paved surface of about 5000 square feet.  One in the shape of a circle, the next a square, and the third an octagon, all are surrounded by solid brick walls about 5 feet tall.  The second set of arenas takes up most of the rest of the area, starting from the north.  Each is about 10,000 square feet, but has no true shape.  Instead, the walls (also made of brick, and about 5 feet tall) follow twists, turns, and curves with no apparent pattern.  All three are also paved, but rather than providing a perfectly even surface, the paving is intentionally uneven, broken, or simply not there in many places.  The overall design appears quite formidable to operate within, yet offers many strategic possibilities to the ones who learn it well.  Between the two sets of arenas rest about 50 chariots, each one flawlessly crafted, yet quite obviously built with functionality in mind rather than beauty.   } {arena} {} {city} {pk} {1.000} {}
