R {25785} {0} {<278>} {West Entrance to the Peasants' Seating} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The entire upper level of the stadium was built to surround the Fighting Arena on the ground floor, offering views to peasants and nobles alike.  A guard rail, no more than 2 feet high, serves more as warning than protection against a fall.  The Peasant's Seating follows the northern curve of the dome, and is "guarded" by a simple wooden fence, running floor to ceiling, east to west, for the length of the dome.  A large door in the center of the eastern wall, leading to the Peasants' Seating, would be very well guarded... if the guards weren't asleep!  } {arena} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
