R {25786} {0} {<278>} {Peasants' Seating - Wooden Benches} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Rough planks have been laid out, each one raised to roughly two feet above the one in front of it, in a softly curving formation around the railing in the center of the floor to allow the peasants to watch the carnage below.  The planks do not look to have been sanded or finished at all, and quite a few peasants appear to be pulling splinters out of their behinds.  This does not seem to deteriorate the fun for them one whit, though.  The crude benches are held up by stout wooden rods below, spaced out every 10 square feet or so.  There doesn't really seem to be enough support to hold everything aloft if the stands were full, but then again, there are so many seats here, you doubt they ever fill all the way up.  The benches run up a good 150 feet into the air, 75 benches all told, each of which could probably seat 100 people comfortably, or 200 if the peasants crowded in.   } {arena} {} {inside} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25787} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
