R {25789} {0} {<278>} {East Entrance to the Nobles' Seating} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  While there are no guards or barriers to physically stop the peasants from entering, nor any rule specifically barring their admittance, it's virtually unheard of to see a peasant in this room.  It is opulently decorated, with enormous plush rugs covering every inch of the floor, and murals depicting the most famous fights in the Gladiator Arena's history covering most of the walls.  Two small basins, made of solid gold, rest in the corner of the room, holding hot and cold water.  The water is changed every half hour, and clean towels are always on hand.  Servants scurry to and fro, carrying out any request the nobles can think of.   } {arena} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
