R {25791} {0} {<278>} {West Entrance to the Nobles' Seating} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  An elaborately decorated wall to the east blocks all view of what is beyond, but everyone knows that it's the Noble's Seating.  The wall itself is covered with cloth hangings, intricately and painstakingly sewn, each showing a different picture.  Many are simply of the famous nobles and royalty who have come to the Gladiator's Arena, while others are of ceremonies held by and for royalty and nobility on special occasions.  Still others depict some of the most famous battles of the Arena's history.  In the center of the wall is an enormous oak door, carved with intricate designs and several inscriptions in a language you cannot read.  The room itself is somewhat plain, excluding the eastern wall.  The guards, fast asleep, appear to be severely neglecting their duties... but that is a common sight here.  All know what this room is and where it leads, and in all of the Arena's storied history there's never been a problem.  Many of the nobility themselves are skilled Gladiators, and your average peasant knows that they'd stand no chance against the far superior weaponry of the nobility, even if he or she had the skill required, and thus never dares to intrude.   } {arena} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
