R {25792} {0} {<278>} {Nobles' Seating - Plush Individual Chairs} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Before you is one of the most amazing sights you've ever seen.  Row after row of thickly padded chairs is spread out before you, perhaps 100 chairs across, and 50 rows deep.  Each row is lifted about 3 feet above the row in front of it, with each chair individually supported by the standard four legs; however the higher rows have legs as long as 150 feet.  The legs are extremely stout, and the higher rows are also reinforced with periodic crossbeams braced below other rows of chairs.  Each seat has a small padded platform attached to its base and protruding out about 3 feet, offering a comfortable place for the nobles to rest their feet, and each of the raised chairs can be reached by a sort of manual elevator, with a 2x2 platform attached to ropes and pulleys, and lifted or lowered by nearby staff.  All of the wood is beautifully stained, and elaborate curtains surround the entire assembly in an interweaving pattern with the wood, to create a beautiful picture.  The cushions on each chair are hand knit, and filled so thickly with down that it seems as if you could sink a full foot into them.  The walls are lined with elaborate patterns, primarily swirls and whooshes, though many designs are apparent, all done with melted gold and silver.  The sunlight sparkles off of the precious metals melted onto the walls, creating something like that a rainbow but of more (and different) colors that keeps the room well lit and completely without shadows.   } {arena} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {25793} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {25791} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25793} {0} {<278>} {Nobles' Seating - Heavily Padded Benches} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  In front of you, rising perhaps 25 stories high, is a series of thickly padded benches.  Each bench is so completely covered, from left to right, in a thickly padded cushion that you cannot even see the wood.  The cushions themselves are elaborately designed, apparently sewn by masters of their craft, and look so thick and plush that it seems if you laid down on one, you'd sink in to your nose.  The benches are each raised about 7 feet higher than the one in front of them, and that entire space is filled with a heavily padded wall, apparently to be used as a backrest.  There's staff standing nearby with what seems to be thousands of blankets and pillows, in case one of the Nobles prefers to lay down while.  The benches are supported with a series of marble pillars, each one having first been sculpted into a unique design, ranging from true statuary to simple round pillars with decorative vines wrapped about it in a lazy spiral.  The pillars are spaced at regular 3 foot intervals in every direction, leaving no doubts about the stability of this ensemble.  Every 50 feet or so is a 2x2 platform attached to ropes and pulleys and leading up through a series of trap doors inset into each bench, allowing the nobles to get to their seats with minimal effort.   } {arena} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {25789} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
