R {25794} {0} {<278>} {The Entrance to the Gauntlet} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This is the entrance to the infamous Gauntlet; the place where the best of the best go to prove their prowess in battle.  The walls are barren stone, with torches spaced evenly every 7 feet on them providing more than enough light to keep even the smallest shadow from entering.  The enormous trap door in the floor is made of stone, easily 3 feet thick, and quite obviously requires the use of all four of the attached iron rungs to lift.  The rest of the floor is a smooth gray stone, unmarred and showing only very light signs of wear.  A large sign posted on the walls provides information about the gauntlet.   } {arena} {} {inside} {safe} {1.000} {}
E {25773} {u} {open u;u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25795} {0} {<278>} {The Training Arena - Basics} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Despite being one of the plainest rooms you've seen here (or virtually anywhere), this room is gigantic.  At 250,000 square feet, the room is a perfect square, with the walls running exactly 500 feet in every direction.  There are doors on the far Eastern and Southern walls, in addition to staircase set in the center of the room heading back towards the Fighting Arena.  The staircase itself is surrounded by thick stone walls on all sides, with just a small archway at the bottom to let you out.  The vast open space of the room is mostly uninterrupted, save for a few small racks of weapons, armor, and assorted combat instruments.  Hundreds of retired Gladiators are ranged about the room, offering lessons on the basics of fighting to any who request them.   } {arena} {} {inside} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25797} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
