R {25796} {0} {<278>} {The Training Arena - Specializations} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  While much smaller than the other Training Arenas, this Arena is possibly the nicest of the three.  The walls bare some decorations (mainly engraved portraits of people whom you do not recognize, but assume are some of the more notable specialists to have trained here) and the room is very well organized.  Perhaps 250 feet to each wall, this room also creates a perfect square.  But most of the room is partitioned into much smaller subsections, and in any subsection you can find everything you need to learn the specialization trained there.  Things such as animal fighting, hand-to-hand, jousting, chariot riding, and dozens of others.  In each subsection, the equipment, trainers, and often some sparring partners are provided.  This section of the training arena is not for the weak... while there is no danger to anyone who just wanders around, there is no sympathy or letting up for those who request training in an area where they have not first mastered the basics.   } {arena} {} {inside} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25795} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25797} {0} {<278>} {The Training Arena - Weapons} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The same size as the Training Arena for Basics, the walls and floor are just as barren of decoration, but much more cluttered.  Racks of weapons line the walls, holding every kind of weapon imaginable.  Axes, staves, maces, swords, and hundreds of others, each in every variety of their own type.  Stone walls, about 1 foot high, crisscross the room in a grid, to create thousands of small areas, each about 10 feet by 10 feet.  Almost every one of these areas is in use.  Weapons specialists seem to be everywhere, training Gladiators in the intricacies of usage, and wherever they are not, men are squared off in pairs, or small groups of up to 10, doing varieties of exercises, or simply sparring.  The Gladiators are of all skill levels, and it seems as if anyone is welcome here.   } {arena} {} {inside} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25795} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25798} {0} {<148>} {A Hidden Alcove} {<148>. .<088>} {  Not much more than an oversized weapons' storage closet, this tiny alcove sports plain wooden walls, an unfinished dirt floor, and a matching ceiling that seems to be raining rocks and dust!  There's barely enough room in here for 4 grown people to stand, much less fight; yet apparently, that's what you must do.  The 3 ... men ... waiting here appear to be the source of the screams you've been hearing.  Of course, calling them "men" is not truly accurate, but as you've never seen anything like them, it's an apt enough description...   } {arena} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {25804} {d} {open d;d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25800} {128} {<278>} {The Thieves' Lair} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The small patch of quicksand you fell through appears to have been harmless, and placed there intentionally as an entrance here, to this surprisingly large room buried under the sand.  The room is easily 20 feet by 20, with ceilings at least 10 feet high.  The walls are lined with wooden planks, perfectly fitted to hold out the sand from the outside beach.  The ceiling and floor consist of more planks, and the ceiling appears to have several layers of reinforcement.  The floor is covered in dust, but whole sections are clean, as if something large had rested there for a long time and only recently been moved.  Footsteps crisscross the dust as well, more proof that the room has been used recently.  The room boasts no decoration, save for the unlit torches spaced out every five feet or so along the walls. } {arena} {} {inside} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25774} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

