R {25802} {0} {<148>} {The Gauntlet - First Challenge} {<148>. .<088>} {  You are in a small chamber, perhaps 40 feet by 20, with no apparent exits.  The walls are a smooth gray stone, and are completely unmarred.  The floor is some sort of reddish rock you've never seen before, with a rough but very solid texture.  There is no source of light in the room, nor does any light seep in from anywhere.  Off in the distance, you can hear the screams of some angry creature, but you cannot make out exactly what type of creature it is. } {arena} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}

R {25803} {0} {<148>} {The Gauntlet - Second Challenge} {<148>. .<088>} {  This chamber is much larger than the last one, perhaps 100 feet by 100.  The walls are of rough hewn earth, as if whoever dug out this chamber forgot to finish the job.  The floor is also simple earth, though it is much smoother than the walls.  There are no visible exits, and the ceiling, where you just fell through, appears completely solid.  The room is pitch black, and the screams seem to somewhat closer now.   } {arena} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {25804} {d} {open d;d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {25798} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25804} {0} {<148>} {The Gauntlet - Third Challenge} {<148>. .<088>} {  This is the largest chamber you've found in the Gauntlet so far.  The room would be rectangular, with walls of around 500 feet long by 300 feet, but the corners of the room are slightly rounded, creating a geometrical shape you cannot quite define.  The walls are made of wood, and torches are hung along them every 15 feet or so, giving the room a shadowy overcast.  Still, this is the first light you've seen in the Gauntlet that you didn't bring in yourself.  The floor is made of cobbled stones, spaced somewhat irregularly, and the grout was filled in a little too thick, so that it seeps over the edges of many of the stones.  Barely visible on the walls are slight lines which could either be cracks in the stone, or doors, though the light makes it too dim to tell.  A trap door in the floor, in the far northeast corner of the room, half covered by dirt, is visible upon closer inspection.  The screams are getting almost unbearably loud now...   } {arena} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {25805} {d} {open d;d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25805} {0} {<148>} {The Gauntlet - Fourth Challenge} {<148>. .<088>} {  You are in an enormous cavern, perhaps 100 feet in every direction, including up.  It's fortunate you were provided a ladder into this room, for this fall might have killed you.  The walls themselves seem to be made of... iron?!?  Yes, definitely iron.  The floor is simple stone, smoothly finished, and the ceiling is so far up into the gloom that you really are not sure.  A faint light seems to permeate the room, but its source is not immediately apparent.  You notice that the screams that had been so loud before now seem to be barely audible.   } {arena} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}

R {25806} {0} {<148>} {The Gauntlet - Fifth Challenge} {<148>. .<088>} {  This chamber is so small you can barely move your weapons.  At best, the room is 5 feet by 5, not enough for even a grown man to move around in.  This creates an ideal environment for the Faerie Folk to fight, which could explain why there are 4 of them preparing to attack you right now!  The walls are made of a solid black stone.  At first glance, you'd have called it granite, but there's a difference, so slight you can't quite define it, that makes you think it's another substance altogether.  The floors and ceiling are made of hard packed earth, loosely covered with boards.  The footing would be very treacherous, with gaps of varying sizes between the boards, which themselves do not seem to be secured to anything, if the room wasn't so small as to make a fall all but impossible.  The ceiling is also covered with some sort of glowing lichen, providing a faint but all-encompassing light.   } {arena} {} {underground} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25807} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25807} {0} {<148>} {The Gauntlet - Sixth Challenge} {<148>. .<088>} {  Ahhh, light!  The first truly well-lit room you've been in since you've entered the Gauntlet.  It would be an immense relief, if it wasn't for what the light showed you!  The chamber itself is of average size, perhaps 25 feet by 15, and the walls are made of a finely finished wood.  The floor and ceiling are covered with cobbled stones, perfectly carved, grouted, and fitted.  Everything looks clean and new, as if this room has seen very little use over the decades.  It all makes for a very good fighting area -- which is something you will apparently need, and quickly, since the four vicious looking animals surrounding you look as if they plan to attack immediately!   } {arena} {} {underground} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {25808} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25808} {0} {<148>} {An Audience Chamber} {<148>. .<088>} {  You've entered a gigantic chamber, with each wall being at least 200 feet long, and the ceiling apparently reaching all the way to the surface of the Earth, some 250 feet (or more) above.  Covering the walls of the chamber is one of the most amazing sights you've ever seen; what appears to be some sort of magical screens.  A few of the screens are simply black, showing nothing, while many are lit and showing what appears to be various areas of the Gladiator's Arena.  Some show assorted fights going on in the Fighting Arena, some show portions of the Training Arena, others shows some of the Peasants watching the fighting, and still others show the Gauntlet itself!  Everything you've experienced here is apparent, except for some of the Nobles' and Royals' seating areas.  Everything seems so real it's as if you could reach out and touch it!  A long wooden ladder, leading to a small iron door, almost completely dwarfed by the screens surrounding it, is set in the top of the Eastern wall.   } {arena} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}

R {25816} {0} {<278>} {Refreshment Stands} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  One of the few places in the seating areas where peasants and nobles alike must share the same space is this small concessions area.  Vendors are lined up forming a three-quarter circle, offering food and drink.  Not the high quality food of the gourmet area, though.  Here the food is a cheaper and much simpler fare, and the drinks don't seem nearly as fancy.  Nonetheless, the food smells phenomenal, and you sure don't see anybody complaining!  Nobles are always given their (standard) preferential treatment, being allowed to go first in lines, and being given 10 feet of distance by the milling peasants.  But if you're not mistaken, it seems like the peasants are actually paying a little bit less.  That could be one reason that none seem to mind letting the nobles clear out before they take their turns...   } {arena} {} {inside} {shop} {1.000} {}
E {25788} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {25789} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {25817} {0} {<148>} {In The Teeth Of The Gale} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  You stare down the teeth of a furious gale, awestruck by the fury of nature's wrath.  The wind rips through the riggings over your head, and the main mast creaks alarmingly as the wind steps up its efforts with a mighty wail.   The ship suddenly tilts in an alarming fashion, sending anything not tied down slamming across the deck and into the ocean.  A furious clanging indicates the captain is summoning the crew. } {promises} {} {waternoswim} {} {1.000} {}
