R {25920} {0} {<278>} {The Drunk Dog Inn} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Dark and smoke-filled, this tavern provides brief respite from the tumult  which surrounds it. A quick glance around leaves the distinct impression that this is not the most reputable establishment within the city's precincts. The room is large with a low roof, the lighting, dim at best, is provided by  a single wooden chandelier in the center of the ceiling. A long bar is  situated along the north wall and it is from here that this hostelry  dispenses what might loosely be termed refreshments. A sizeable hearth with  roasting spit is set into the east wall, its fire dimmed to barely glowing  embers. Alcoves little taller than a person's waist provide limited privacy  for patrons huddled within. A sparse layer of straw covers the unevenly paved stone floor. The whole room reeks of stale ale, sweat and tobacco smoke. The room grows quiet as you walk around as if they're hiding something or  perhaps want to keep something secret. Perhaps you should search for that  secret. } {drageran} {} {inside} {pk,shop} {1.000} {}
