R {28985} {0} {<178>} {Even darker Pwyll} {<178>~ ~<088>} {  It is impossible to tell whether it is day or night, because a curious black fog is smothering any light that could have existed in this room. It is possible to place a hand directly in front of the face in order to catch a fleeting glimpse of it through the swirls of darkness, but that is about all. The scent of damp dirt and tree bark reveals the fact that this is a forest of sorts. It is tough to concentrate, because sharp, scratching fingernails that must actually be tree branches keep inflicting damage to clothes and precious facial features. To the west it somehow seems even darker than this, and to the north there is just more black fog. Other directions tend to instigate the onslaught of tree branches so those would best be avoided. } {annwn} {} {mist} {} {1.000} {}
E {28984} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {28986} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {28986} {0} {<110>} {Darkest Pwyll} { } {  This is an incredibly smothering darkness. What is this place? Maybe it is a  cave. The ground feels rock hard, so unlike the natural bounce of the forest  foliage when it was underfoot. Sure enough, a cursory inspection to the left  with an inquiring hand returns the feeling of what must be smooth limestone. About five timid feet to the right is another cave wall. Unfortunately, how  far up the ceiling of this place may be is impossible to ascertain. Best to  just tread carefully so as to not end up with a stalactite smacked up against the forehead. It really is a miracle that no serious head injuries have  occurred thus far. } {annwn} {} {} {} {1.000} {}
E {28985} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {28987} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {28987} {0} {} {Darkest Pwyll} { } {  Excellent! More blackness and more cave, without an end in sight. One interesting detail about this section of the cave, is that it appears to be a juncture. A quick investigation reveals that a person can either head west, north, or east from this point. Better think quick about the best way to move, then move fast, since this is definitely not the sort of atmosphere to stop and take a siesta in. Especially considering the fact that there is some sort of fearsome howling noise echoing throughout the cave. Maybe a bat could use echolocation to figure out which way the sound is coming from, but to those creatures not possessing such a useful skill, it literally sounds like the howling is coming from all directions. The howling is gigantically loud. The howling is ethereal. Time to make a decision on a direction to take, and run! } {annwn} {} {} {} {1.000} {}
E {28988} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {28986} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {28988} {0} {<110>} {Darkest Pwyll} { } {  It is impossible that any place could exist with a darkness darker than this. Walking through here feels like stumbling around on a moonless night with  closed eyelids. Luckily, the ground is fairly smooth and flat, and so far, no sleeping creatures have been disturbed by the entry of a curious explorer. The lack of life in here makes it feel a bit like a tomb. The fact that every so often a blood-chilling howl can be heard piercing the silence adds fodder  to the mind's fire, conjuring up images of wraiths and other ghostly  apparitions. Just to the right there is a chilly draft to the air; maybe that is one of them now. Time to get out of here before sanity takes a leap off  the deep end. To go back the way most recently explored, or to carry on  forward, these are the only choices available. } {annwn} {} {} {} {1.000} {}
E {28989} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
