R {28989} {0} {<228>} {Brighter Spot} {<228>, .<088>} {  This section of Pwyll is fairly flat, aside from one distinctive landmark in the form of an oddly-shaped hill. To the north the flat meadow ends, and the foothills of Pwyll begin. All other directions are blocked off by steep cliff-faces. The cliff-face to the east does have a visible entrance to a rather dark and foreboding-looking cave. It is notable that the hill here is odd due to the fact that it is perfectly rounded off at the top, almost as if it was created by the intelligent hands of a perfectionist sculptor. } {annwn} {} {field3} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {28988} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
