R {28990} {0} {<238>} {Darker Spot} {<238>/ \<088>} {  Here begin the foothills of Pwyll. Cumulus clouds throw dramatic shadows upon these great green hills. The ground is folded in upon itself in such a way that it is reminiscent of blankets on a bed that have been left in an unmade jumble. Though if these were blankets they would be made from grass and wild grains rather than fabric. Large boulders litter the ground everywhere, making it appear as if this could be the playhouse of a baby giant. Every so often a wizened little tree grows crookedly amongst these rocks, like some sort of eccentric hermit-tree. } {annwn} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
E {28991} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {28989} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {28991} {0} {<268>} {Bright Mountains} {<268>/ \<088>} {  Climbing through this mountain range offers a spectacular view of the land below. The climb is exhausting, but the sights along the way are breathtaking. From here a person can carry on northward in order to reach some of the most colossal mountains in this range. To head south would begin a descent into the foothills of Pwyll. From this high level, it is even possible to make out a path that heads safely east, and ends up over at Pwyll's oak tree forest. Many a traveler must stop at this point in their journey to admire the waterfall that is here, cascading elegantly down through various layers of mossy plateaus. } {annwn} {} {mountain_cyan} {} {1.000} {}
E {28976} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
