R {28992} {0} {<178>} {Tree Line at Pwyll} {<178>/ \<088>} {  This point in an explorer's journey brings them near the peak of the tallest mountain in Pwyll. Reaching the jagged tip of this mountain is becoming less of a fantasy and more of a reality. It is impossible to tell what lurks on the other side the mountain, but the suspense of it causes a driving need to press onward no matter how fatigued. Looking upwards, it is obvious that after this point the altitude becomes too high for trees to be able to grow. Breathing the air is becoming difficult as well; thank goodness the crown of the mountain is near and then the journey back down will be less treacherous. The other choice, of course, is to simply head south to descend the mountain immediately. } {annwn} {} {icemount} {} {1.000} {}
