R {28993} {0} {<218>} {Pwyll Crater} {<218>/ \<088>} {  So, it is a crater that greets the brave explorer who reaches the crest of  this, the tallest mountain. Perhaps the crater is the result of a dormant  volcano. Then again, the impact of a mega meteorite could have caused such a  geographical occurrence as well. This crater measures in at least a dozen  miles across and must be hundreds of meters deep. It looks more formidable to skirt around it in order to reach the other side, than to wander down into  it. The descent into the crater really would be a steep one, and there is not much down there aside from a great dark expanse of dirt. The far side of the  crater looks too steep to climb back up, so if deciding to continue north  down the mountain, a person had best be certain they are done with their  explorations here. There is also a path from the crater that leads steeply  down to the east, and ends up at the ruins of the Pwyll marsh. The other  option is head down the southern slope of the mountain. } {annwn} {} {volcano} {} {1.000} {}
