R {29090} {0} {<148>} {Dense Forest} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  A small creek begins to run through here, which certainly is a lot easier to travel along than trying to create a path through the trees. The creek is so shallow that it is even possible to tread right through it, or in a effort to not get wet feet, hop along the stepping-stones. There is one stone in particular laying alongside the creek bed that catches the eye. It is a large stone with a hole that goes right through its center. One could hypothesize that the hole was created through the power of a stream of water jetting straight at it for many years. This must have occurred in a time when the creek ran with a lot more water than it does now. } {annwn} {} {river} {} {1.000} {}
E {29087} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29093} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
