R {29092} {0} {<148>} {Soul Trap} {<148>. .<088>} {  The air is musty and the dirt is fertile; it falls onto you in soft clumps. Worms and beetles, distraught at their sudden displacement, scurry over your  feet. The earth feels cool against your skin, almost refreshing. Hopefully  nothing falls into the hole on top of you. Maybe it would be a good idea to  get out of here quickly! } {annwn} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}

R {29093} {0} {<148>} {Dense Vegetation} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  The creek continues onward here. Above the creek the area has been decorated with twisting vines. These are very thick brown vines that look like they would take a fair bit of chopping with an ax in order to successfully break them to pieces. They twist about each other in a very creative yet messy pattern. To the north is the beginning of this small creek, and to the south it looks like the creek takes a bend and anyone traveling through can either follow the creek west, or continue to explore to the east. } {annwn} {} {river} {} {1.000} {}
E {29090} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29094} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29094} {0} {<148>} {Dense Vegetation} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  There is a small creek here that leads either to the north or to the west. Ash trees crowd around this junction like a crowd of spectators. Vines are twisting their way around the trees, though whether they trying to hug them or choke them, it is tough to say. Small bits of driftwood and a mishmash of leaves line either side of the creek. The water is moving rather quickly toward the west, and there is the distinctive loud roaring of a waterfall coming from that direction as well. } {annwn} {} {river} {} {1.000} {}
E {29096} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
