R {29095} {0} {<148>} {Dense Vegetation} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  Following the creek to the west is not very productive, since there is a steep drop-off and then an intensely loud waterfall begins. The water of the creek is so shallow that it is quite safe to stand on the rocks at the edge of the waterfall and look down. The water looks white as it falls to the ground some fifty feet below and joins up with a larger, faster moving creek. It appears as if there is merely more forest down there, with no signs of civilization evident. It is probably best to backtrack to the east in order to continue with explorations of this island. } {annwn} {} {river} {} {1.000} {}
E {29094} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29096} {0} {<228>} {Dense Foliage} {<228>( *<088>} {  The forest is really being inhospitable to anyone who wants to travel in this direction. The trees here grow so close together that there is barely a space to walk through. Further to this, there are thick vines weaving in and out of them which need to be either cut apart, climbed over, or crawled under. Talk about making slow progress. To the east it looks as if the vegetation starts to thin out a bit, whereas to the west the forest appears to be quite dark and ominous. } {annwn} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {29097} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29094} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29097} {0} {<228>} {Lighter Forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  Shafts of sunlight stream all the way to the leaf-strewn ground in this section of the forest. The leaves actually crunch underfoot, and the air is warm and dry. The trees are sparsely dispersed here, so there is ample room to take a leisurely walk through this space and enjoy the warmth of  the sun. The chipper chatter of birds is a calm background noise, and the scent of the trees is pleasant and sparks memories of warm summer days. } {annwn} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {29098} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29096} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29098} {0} {<228>} {Clearing} {<228>, .<088>} {  A small spring is the central point of this clearing. White narcissus flowers grow all around it, whereas yellow daffodils dominate the rest of the field. The daffodils are interspersed with a few noticeable types of flora including foxtails, wheat, and devil's grass. The narcissus flowers bow their heads down to the spring as if beckoning any traveler to come see what is reflected. The water of the pool stirs with not even a ripple and looks dark like the surface a slab of polished obsidian marble. Nothing mars this spring's surface, it is perfect. What would it reflect  back if a person happened to gaze inside? } {annwn} {} {field3} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {29103} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29100} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29099} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29097} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29099} {0} {<228>} {Lighter Forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  The trees of the forest are growing quite densely here, but things are kept bright by glowing globes of light that are floating through the air. Maybe they are will-o'-the-wisps, set here to guard some otherworldly treasure. Then again, maybe they are just the result of someone having fun with a magic light illusion trick. The lights shy away when a person draws near to them, so they are impossible to catch. They are still fun to gaze at, however, since they create some outstanding shadows upon the forest and really beautify the area with their colors. They reflect flickering shades of gold, red, and blue light upon the trees. } {annwn} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {29098} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29100} {0} {<228>} {Clearing} {<228>, .<088>} {  Tall wild grass grows in this clearing. It is not tall enough, however, to hide the circle of boulders that was assembled here eons ago. The boulders are so large that it must have taken a giant to move them. They look to be just the correct height to act as a comfortable seat to sit upon to enjoy dinner and stories around a campfire. To the south a field of daffodils can be seen, and to the north the trees begin to crop up again. The east and west are built up of foliage so dense that it would be too debilitating a task to attempt to travel in either of those directions. } {annwn} {} {field3} {} {1.000} {}
E {29101} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29098} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29101} {0} {<228>} {Lighter Forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  Here is a part of the forest where trees are growing in a neat circle. There is a campfire set up in the space that exists in the middle of them. Whoever planned on staying the night here made a good decision, as this is the perfect spot for a campsite. A couple of logs have been chopped into manageable sizes and set around the fire to act as seats. To the south is a clearing with tall grass and a circle of large stones, and to the west there are .... giant mushrooms.  } {annwn} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {29100} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29102} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29102} {0} {<228>} {Lighter Forest} {<228>( *<088>} {  This is an interesting section of the forest. Interspersed with the plant life here, sit a multitude of mushrooms. For some reason these mushrooms are equivalent in height to the trees around here. They are weird colors with weirder spots all over them. No, these are most certainly not the sort of mushrooms a person would want to cook up for dinner. To the east one can spy the welcoming glow of a small campfire, and in other directions there simply happens to be an impassible cliff face. Continuing eastward is really the only plausible choice. } {annwn} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
E {29101} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29103} {0} {<178>} {Lighter Forest} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  Here are the ivy covered ruins of an ancient gatehouse. A surprising amount of the original structure has withstood the test of time. Tall grass grows all around these ruins. The structure that has been left standing here is made up of small somber stones. The part of the gatehouse that still exists consists of a basic archway that looks safe enough to walk under. This gateway is connected to what must have at one point been an impressive eighteen foot tall castle wall. This wall obviously used to run all the way around the castle, but it has by this point in time become broken down in many sections. } {annwn} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {29104} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29098} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {29104} {0} {<238>} {Clearing} {<238>(<148>~<238>)<088>} {  This is where the castle courtyard must have been. There are some ruins of hollowed out buildings that could have been the castle smithy and kitchen but now they are nothing more than sunken sections of ground surrounded by piles of stones and rubble. There is also a well in the middle of the courtyard, and a number of apple trees are flourishing here despite the lack of a gardener to care for them. To the north is the old castle keep, and to the east sits a guard tower, while a gatehouse monopolizes the land to the south. } {annwn} {} {well} {} {1.000} {}
E {29113} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {29105} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
