R {30078} {0} {<278>} {Inside a dingy cell} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Dust 2 centimeters thick is caked on the cracked stone walls of this pitiful excuse for a cell.  A rusted metal bowl in the far corner serves as the toilet for the prisoners inside - thank goodness you haven't committed some horrible crime.  You see some ugly yellowish-green fungus growing on the walls\; no wonder why the prisoners don't try to clean up their cells!  You have a very dry taste in your mouth just standing in these horrific confines\; your mouth feels like it has spiders crawling around inside of it. Shivering uncontrollably, you feel like fleeing to the south, outside of this cage of terror.   } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {30077} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {30079} {0} {<278>} {Inside the jail} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The jail's hallway continues due east here, and you see several mystical orbs of light hanging on the walls.  Not only do they light up the otherwise dingy hallway, but they also serve as place markers - under each ball there is a slit in the wall, presumably a trap in case the prisoner were to escape.  You cleverly deduce that the threat of poisoned arrow is enough, for as the light flickers on the barred cell door, you do not notice any signs of attempted jailbreak.  The iron door to your north, does, however, bear the scars of disrepair, as it appears to have rusted after who knows HOW many years of exposure to the elements.  The cell lies to your north, while the center of the hallway is to the west.   } {dsr} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {30080} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
