R {30540} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mThe Hall of the Muses[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you reach the smooth stone floor of the landing, a lighted marble statue begins to come into view.  You now stand in the presence of the majestic figure of one of the Bard clan's beloved muses.  Several bards sit at the base of the effigy, some studying the great writers of the past, their noses buried in their books.  Others gaze up to the gentle face of the figure as if trying to pull a bit of inspiration from within her. Glancing around, you notice other marble figures scattered about the placid hall.  Great cathedral-like windows adorn the walls of the rounded room allowing large amounts of light to flood in, helping to light the figures that stand inbetween each of the windows.  The vaulted ceiling, along with the four giant marble pillars that reach forever upwards, gives this room a feel of great importance and reverence.  Amber-colored benches set here and there seat various bards, scholars and visitors.  The never-ending spiral staircase ascends toward the ceiling which seems so far away that none might bother to climb it, save the devoted bards. } {bard} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
