R {30544} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mAerial cloister[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Pausing to get your breath, you decide that at this point, you don't care if you see another staircase in your life. Fortunately, the architect who designed the tower seems to have anticipated this, as the chamber before you seems an ideal place to rest. You stand in a large, circular portico, the walls broken by many open gothic arches, allowing a magnificent view of the city below. The Midgaard citizens teem through the streets, tiny as ants, and if you look closely... Yes! Yes, you can see the dump from here. You're high up enough to get away from the noise of the city, and the quiet adds to the sense of calm and serenity provided by the carefully maintained potted plants here and there. Several stone benches sit between these, and many members of the guild are taking advantage of these, idly tuning instruments, contemplating their muses, or simply snoring quietly. Despite the easy access through the archways, you decide the easiest (and the safest) way back down to the ground would be via the staircase, or you may wish to explore the spires to the north and south. } {bard} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
