R {30799} {0} {<148>} {The Nile River} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  Its shining waters flowing northward, the great Nile River is the lifeblood of Egypt.  Indeed, it is the very reason that Egypt exists, and has existed for centuries.  Every year it rises to gently deposit a rich layer of silt to be farmed, and that season will soon be upon the country.  Now at its lowest, it still makes passage difficult for those traveling to the beautiful capital city, Thebes.  Thick rushes obscure the banks of the river, but now and then can be spotted people fishing, harvesting reeds, or hunting duck with throwing sticks.   } {dynasty} {} {ocean} {} {1.000} {}
