R {30802} {0} {<238>} {Royal Tombs} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  Surprise, surprise, surprise!  This is more than a hole in the ground- it's a finished passageway painstakingly carved from the stony ground.  Heiroglyphs cover the walls from the finished floor to the high ceiling, proclaiming the glorious story of Pharaoh Tuthmoses I and his dynasty.  Even though the grand hall is thick with dust, the painted symbols still gleam dully in reflected light.  One particular heiroglyph seems rather ominous; indeed, it curses those who would dare enter this sacred place for wrongdoing.   } {dynasty} {} {desert} {} {1.000} {}
