R {30807} {0} {<148>} {Further up the Nile} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  Travelling further upriver, one quickly leaves the river traffic of Thebes behind.  Skiffs and barges still make their way up and down the Nile, but now they have to carefully maneuver around the wildlife that resides more thickly here.  Looking to the south, one can see the river wend its way out of sight.  Considering that the next city is several days' journey away, there's no sense in continuing further in that direction.   } {dynasty} {} {ocean} {} {1.000} {}
E {30799} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {30808} {0} {<238>} {The Docks of Thebes} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  This set of docks is always busy during the daytime, and even at night dockhands stand ready to assist travellers.  Stone steps rise from the blue-brown water lapping at the shoreline, allowing those who arrive by boat to step easily out onto the dock.  There's also room for the larger barges to be securely tethered, goods being loaded and unloaded by ramp.   } {dynasty} {} {desert} {} {1.000} {}
