R {30814} {0} {<238>} {The Unpleasant Peasant Quarter} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  The worst of the worst.  This is where one can count on meeting up with the lowest dregs of Egypt's population.  Thieves, beggars, and murderers are common here, usually frequenting cheap beer taverns.  It's probably best to avoid any street vendors one might enounter in these filthy alleyways; not only is the food likely to be rotten, it's probably also gritty with enough sand to break teeth.  Watch out for buckets of slop being thrown from the windows!  Nobody bothers to look outside before tossing out the trash.  Unsurprisingly, the stench is almost overwhelming.   } {dynasty} {} {desert} {} {1.000} {}
E {30813} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {30815} {0} {<238>} {The Grand Plaza} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  Here the full grandeur of mighty Egypt is displayed for the benefit of both visitors to the realm and the empire's citizens.  The oblong Plaza covers more than four acres, leading to the imperial palace to the east, the premier temple of the great god Amon-ra to the north, and fantastic residences in which the high nobles of the realm reside.  Whereas the roads leading to the Plaza are simply packed dirt, here there is meticulously formed and maintained paving.  In the very center is a ring of statues depicting a dozen or so of the most important gods and goddesses of Egypt, surrounding an obelisk plated in solid platinum.  The feats and glories of Hatshepsut are inscribed thereon.   } {dynasty} {} {desert} {} {1.000} {}
