R {30818} {0} {<278>} {Hapuseneb's Private Chambers} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The private chambers of the High Priest are much more personable than the rest of the palace.  Despite a lack of enthusiasm for interior decorating, Habuseneb is nonetheless accustomed to comfort, and this room reflects that. The lion-shaped couch of pure gold is large enough to show that Hapuseneb doesn't often spend a night alone.  He delights in mental challenge, and a game of draughts, the board carved from the finest cedar, stands at ready.  Warmed wine sits on a small table in a silver goblet, hieroglyphs of praise to the gods inscribed in star sapphire.   } {dynasty} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {30817} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {30819} {0} {<238>} {The Palace Gates} {<138>~ ~<088>} {  The entrance into the royal palace is grand, a pair of tall marble pillars anchoring heavy doors of the same material.  Red sandstone walls stretch out to either side and curl around the palace in comforting protection.  The expense to install it must have been enormous, yet the rulers of Egypt didn't think twice about it.   } {dynasty} {} {desert} {} {1.000} {}
