R {30821} {0} {<138>} {The Throne Room} {<138>[ ]<088>} {  The throne room is used by the Pharaoh for any business that isn't strictly maintenance of her kingdom.  It's here that she greets foreign dignitaries, accepts the prizes of war, and the like.  The chamber is specifically designed to give an impression of power and wealth, from the golden Horus throne high on its platform to the jeweled silver used in mere torch holders.   } {dynasty} {} {palace_room} {} {1.000} {}
E {30820} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {30822} {0} {<138>} {The Royal Feasting Hall} {<138>[ ]<088>} {  Dinners at the royal palace are more of a public relations event than a small family get-together.  Nobles of the realm eat here daily, lounging around the open square full of entertainers.  The aromas of rich food vie with the scents of the luxurious lotus blossoms that decorate the room, as well as the perfumed cones of wax melting on the heads of the diners.  Roast duck, stuffed goose, dates and figs and fresh warm dark bread...  Meals are huge and irresistible, accompanied by sweet wine and beer.  By the end of the night, most of the diners will be drowsy with food, and more than a little tipsy.   } {dynasty} {} {palace_room} {} {1.000} {}
