R {31136} {0} {<228>} {[1;32mBefore the Willow Trellis[0;37m} {<228>( *<088>} {  The stone path curves as the lush orchid beds by the drifting brook give way to a carpet of bright lemon verbena and delicate gypsophilia.  Situated between two bending willow trees you see a tall wrought-iron trellis.  The pattern is a complex repetition of sacred knots and symbols.  Weaving thoughout this design, honeysuckle vines have formed a wall of lingering scent.  Here the ground has risen to shape a small grassy hill.  The soft lawn is pleasant for long rests while composing thoughts and is high enough to observe the full perimeter of the still pond.  Almost hidden beside this vantage point is a simple, shallow well.  Aged red bricks have been casually placed to direct a small tributary into the natural mossy bowl.  It has become customary for those who gather inspiration from this peaceful scene to dip an unprotected hand into the shadowed water before continuing their adventures.   } {crusaders} {} {forest} {safe} {1.000} {}
