R {31141} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mThe Temple Treasury[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A slight scent of aged metal greets you upon entering this clean, well-kept antechamber.  The walls have been constructed from large, polished grey stones and a darker, rough mortar, but the snug size and plush furnishings keep the room from feeling cold or forlorn.  Crisp parchments lie neatly rolled and stacked on one low table, offering news of trading and losses nearby and in foreign lands.  On the far side of this room stands a carved mahogany rail with an imposing iron gate just beyond.  Despite its obvious weight, the door stands fully open to allow passage for studious clerics quietly treading between the two rooms.  Their days and nights are spent assisting with the management of hopeful adventurers' transactions.  You may withdraw or deposit your gold here, but sentries of pleasant demeanor and grim countenance ensure that none shall pass beyond the rail.   } {crusaders} {} {inside} {bank,safe} {1.000} {}
E {31140} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31142} {0} {<278>} {[1;32mThe Courier's Office[0;37m} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You have arrived into a small and well lit chamber.  Hooded lanterns burn brightly on each of the four walls and a single orb of soft light pulsates warmly upon a simple oak table that is the central feature of this room.  Sitting at the table, intently leafing through a stack of official looking papers is a young cleric with stern and chiseled features that suggest he has seen much in his short lifetime.  Standing alert in the far corner of the room are several young squires who look up expectantly as you enter.  The young Crusaders are dressed in soft, snugly fitting leather leggings and jerkins.  The sturdy, brown travel boots on their feet shuffle with anticipation, ready for the off.  The Cleric looks up from his paperwork and without a word, motions your attention toward a white marble PLAQUE which adorns the southern wall of this chamber.   } {crusaders} {} {inside} {safe} {1.000} {}
