R {31747} {0} {<118>} {A Destitute Nursery} {<118>. .<088>} {  Either this room was never used or was an afterthought when the castle was  decorated, though its purpose remains relatively clear. Simple curtains of  bland cottons cascade down from their railings to the floor, dragging through the dust whenever a breeze strikes. At the center of the room rests a cradle, and a wooden rocking chair sits unused in the northeastern corner of the  area. The floors and walls are of simple and unadorned stone, their only  feature being built-in cabinets with basic (and probably expired) amenities. } {chantry} {} {redcarpet} {} {1.000} {}
