R {31749} {0} {<118>} {Lady's Fainting Chamber} {<118>. .<088>} {  In this particular room, the cold stone walls are paneled with dark and  polished wooden slats of some arcane kind. Silken sheets find themselves  draped from the edges of the room to cover the ceiling, tying in a knot at  the center of the area. One could consider this a bedroom of sorts, as a  veiled bed rests with its headrest against one wall, though a fainting couch  and other seating arrangements have been assembled around a hearth against  the eastern side of the room. South leads towards a small balcony - easily  considered to be a waste of resources considering its insignificant size -  overlooking the more 'reputable' part of Fellchantry, if one would believe  such a thing exists. } {chantry} {} {redcarpet} {} {1.000} {}
E {31745} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31750} {0} {<178>} {A Spiralling Stairwell} {<278>###<088>} {  A grand set of marble stairs with golden railings twist from below,  eventually tightening as one continues to travel upwards before reaching a  small landing with two utterly basic potted plants flanking a set of wooden  doors which lead towards the Baron's offices. These doors appear to be locked at all times, the man in charge only ever peeking past a slit within one of  the barriers before permitting entry to whomsoever bequeaths an audience with him. } {chantry} {} {castle} {} {1.000} {}
