R {31761} {0} {<248>} {Bottlebreak Alley} {<248>. .<088>} {  The alleyway terminates at this point very much in the same way that it does  to the north. Most human sounds are either sniffling, coughing or someone  losing their breakfast. The odour of rum and fish is thick in the air, most  denizens of Bottlebreak alley mostly not bothering with commerce as opposed  to the paths closer to Fellchantry Square. Much of the ground has eroded  here, causing buildings to fall into disrepair and become damaged by small  rivulets of water which seep through from the far west.  Northwards, a bend leads back to Murder Alley. } {chantry} {} {alley} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {31760} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31762} {0} {<248>} {Dead End in Bottlebreak Alley} {<248>. .<088>} {  This particular pathway comes to an end here. The alley leads up to an  unoccupied square with most buildings facing away from the alley itself,  though the odd back door may be spied where servants or tenants would empty  their chamberpots out onto the cobble underfoot. Wheels with wire along their edges are mounted from east to west, top-floor tenants pinning and rolling  (rare) laundry out to dry. Some of those textiles still drip beneath the  eternal gloom of Fellchantry. } {chantry} {} {alley} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {31760} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31763} {0} {<248>} {Treadway Alley} {<248># #<088>} {  The quaint atmosphere of Treadway Alley is tantamount here, bars and  restaurants and coffee shop owners peddling the "best seats in the house". The scent of freshly baked confectionary hangs thickly in the air and one may soon discover that beyond the face-value of Fellchantry rests an entire  community and culture unseen. Somewhat more ragged than those who settle  closer to the centre of Fellchantry, children can be seen running and  playing, much to the chargin of their elders who traffic the alleyway. } {chantry} {} {dungeon} {} {1.000} {}
E {31764} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
