R {31765} {0} {<248>} {Oberon Alley} {<248>. .<088>} {  Oberon Alley carries much of the vibrancy which one could find at the Chantry Commons - more a road than an alley, its occupants appear to take great care  in maintaining a respectable environment. Rumour on the lips of all who have  bothered to set foot here speaks of the road's name, lauded after an ancient  and obscure individual who found the secret to eternal life. It is evident in the decorations which all doors on the eastern and western flanks have on  them - every one a slightly different variant of the same thing: A wooden  carving of a wolf howling at the moon. } {chantry} {} {alley} {} {1.000} {}
E {31764} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {31767} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31766} {0} {<248>} {Monisier Alley} {<248>. .<088>} {  A small alleyway terminates here right off the eastern edge of the Chantry  Commons. The far eastern wall features a single door which no doubt leads to  someone's abode, though it is flanked by a great collection of metal artworks which glimmer in the dim Fellchantry gloom. Frequently someone with finer  dress would peruse the wares or speak to the artist responsible, often  walking away with their pockets a few coins lighter. Along the northern and  southern edges, two-storey buildings rise up and obfuscate anything beyond  them.  Westwards lies the Chantry Commons, and one can hear the signature cries of peddlers. } {chantry} {} {alley} {} {1.000} {}
E {31764} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31767} {0} {<248>} {Oberon Alley} {<248>. .<088>} {  Flags of bright color are draped wherever the occupants of this area could  find a spot, the vibrant atmosphere continuing even this far south of the  Chantry Commons. Here one can still see a multitude of howling wolf carvings  draped above neighbourhood doors. Some of the tightly packed houses feature  something which one could consider quite unique for this side of the barony,  and that is the presence of potted plants and blooming flowers.  The alley curves sharply to the west, leading towards a park. } {chantry} {} {alley} {} {1.000} {}
E {31765} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {31768} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {31768} {0} {<238>} {Oberon Nook} {<238>(<148>~<238>)<088>} {  The alleyways eventually open up into Oberon Nook, very much resembling a  park tucked away in a forgotten corner of the barony. The grasses which roll  across the area are maintained with care, the sparse scattering of trees also adding to the charm of this 'clearing' between buildings. Several benches are featured, at least one occupied at all times while children entertain  themselves in the open space under the supervision of the eternal gloomy sky  overhead.  Eastwards, one may travel back to the vibrant Oberon Alley. } {chantry} {} {well} {} {1.000} {}
