R {31971} {0} {<248>} {Another Bend in the Tunnels} {<248>% %<088>} {  This is a steep, meandering passage. It is a lot tighter to pass through than the other passages in this area, but it is still a comfortable enough size to navigate with ease. Due to the closeness of the tunnel's walls, it is easy to notice that pictoglyphs have been painted upon them. A light source picks up  paintings of hominids engaged in a whole variety of activities. This means  that this passage was cut here hundreds of years ago, and it also looks like  surface dwellers must have been down here at some point. Whether they managed to survive underground or whether they were here as slaves, would be an  entertaining story indeed. There are a few other geological points of  interest in this passage and it could prove useful to investigate them. } {uprising} {} {cave} {} {1.000} {}
