R {31975} {0} {<278>} {A Somber Walkway} {<228>,<278>|<228>`<088>} {  This nursing home in the clouds was created by the great architect Harald van Godwhine. Here is a quote from the acclaimed artist himself:        I used the grassiest grass and the treeiest trees to create a canopy      of comfort and love for my nursing home in the sky. I injected the      cotton ball clouds with Griffon's Blood in order to create a buoyant      surface for the nursing home to balance upon. After that, it was all      about adding soft textures in order to mimic the sensation of walking      on a cloud. I wanted to call the nursing home Cloud Nine, but      unfortunately that is not the name that was chosen in the end. Too      much like the name of a hotel they said. Rotters, the lot of 'em.  This architectural masterpiece has been ranked number 100 on the extensive list of Wonders of Andolor. The Cloud City of Gnomalin is ranked 99th, to Harald van Godwhine's great chagrin. He was never able to figure out how to build a structure upon the elusive material of real cloud. } {nursing} {} {smallroad} {} {1.000} {}
