R {31978} {0} {<178>} {The Reception Area} {<278>###<088>} {  The architectural team for this nursing home pondered the fact that in the  beginning, these types of facilities started out as extensions to hospitals. Therefore, to a certain extent, folks expect that a nursing home will retain  that appearance. The team also recognized that the building's entrance is  incredibly important in giving visitors that positive first impression of  what the overall facility will be like. So the designer team worked hard to  create a spacious, colorful, and inviting entrance. They wanted to imbue an  overwhelming feeling of happiness within the individual as they took their  first steps into the building. To do this, they utilized a palette of warm  color tones for several large wall murals, as well as floors crafted with a  tile mosaic finish. They added comfortable furniture to relax in, and spared  no expense on an extravagant, cathedral ceiling, made perfect with the  addition of incredible skylights. } {nursing} {} {castle} {} {1.000} {}
