R {31982} {0} {<148>} {The Sunroom} {<118>)<138>)<148>)<088>} {  Since sunlight helps to alleviate certain types of mental illness, such as  depression, the designers of this nursing home decided they would like to  create a room that would let in the maximum amount of sun possible. All of  the windows in this sunroom are made up of small panes of glass that have  been separated by wood trim. The windows are fixed in place, since wherever  they have been built, they take up the whole wall-space. The walls are  nothing more than a frame to help support the windows, and then these windows arc right into the roof. The floor here is made of hardwood that continues in from the lounge to the east. A number of pieces of classic furniture have  been proudly displayed in this room, almost too precious-looking to even sit  on! } {nursing} {} {rainbow} {} {1.000} {}
