R {31983} {0} {<268>} {A Sanitary Hallway} {<268>[ ]<088>} {  The hallways in this nursing home are wide and the floors are made of  hardwood. Wooden floors are a good choice for a nursing home since they are  stylish, and do not accumulate dirt and hidden debris in the uncontrollable  fashion that carpets are susceptible to. Every so often along the hall, there is a bench covered in soft paisley fabric that a tired soul can have a quick  rest on if their journey becomes too treacherous. Above each of these benches has been hung a painting. Each painting portrays a different view of the  countryside. Each paint stroke is visible on these paintings and extra  attention has been given to the way that the light effects the images. This  particular hallway is quite short, and only has three rooms of residents  leading off of it. If heading west, an individual will end up at the main  entrance to the building. } {nursing} {} {hallway} {} {1.000} {}
