R {32784} {0} {<278>} {Bard's Guild Hall} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A woman stonemason lifting blocks into this almost completed hall sings a  worksong as she swings her heavy load. Even when almost empty this great hall seems filled with notes just waiting to be played, spoken or sung. A poet  wanders by, mumbling his prose to himself as he walks, almost praying to some rhythmic god. Children in one corner are dressed in the rags of urchins, but  sing more sweetly than the richest man could afford, led by a cloaked bard  with a wooden baton. Other bards hurry on mysterious tasks, their steps  sounding musically on the special stone floor, each stone being tempered in a musical scale. The only door not blocked by the materials of construction  that still litter this hall, is to your south. The entrance to this guild is  to your north, leading out onto Astra road.  You also see an entrance to  some sort of performance space to your east. } {reme} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
