R {32900} {0} {<278>} {A Road through the Countryside} {<278>---<088>} {  Cottages line the road to the north and south. They are small but very tidy  and in excellent repair, judging by the fresh thatch on the roofs. Each  cottage has a brightly painted door, representing the only real difference  among them. Perhaps the farmers, after a long day of toil in the fields and a few pints of ale afterwards, use the door color as their guide to finding  home. } {firebird} {} {smallroad_ew} {} {1.000} {}
