R {33269} {0} {<278>} {Saiph} {<278>*  <088>} {  This large, bluish star's light pierces the sky like a sword.  Being very large and easy to see, it is a pity it is not a little more to the north and east, or it would replace Polaris as the North Star, marking the Major Fundamental Antipode, and be much more useful for navigation.  Some say that it was once called the Warrior Star, but this may be a misidentification given that some ancient texts said that the Warrior Star was blood red.  Others say that this star was once the sword of Tor the Lightbringer, who sealed away most of a shadow dimension in the distant past.  A few nearby remnants of that dimension are indeed nearby, but no one knows what is inside the black hole sealed a bit north from here.   } {vidblain} {} {space2} {} {1.000} {}
