R {33317} {0} {<278>} {Kitalpha} {<278>  .<088>} {  This yellow star's name has a meaning--part of a horse--which is, no doubt, a reference to its namesake, Omar Kitalpha.  As to why and which part of the horse they were thinking of when they named the star, the legend goes that Omar was a huge, oafish lout.  One day, he went out to buy a horse.  Being a large man, he should have bought a horse to accommodate his girth, but he was far too cheap and too stupid, so he bought the scrawniest old nag he could find.  Fool that he was, he then set off for a journey through the mountains, and the poor old horse's back broke.  They both fell off a cliff and died.  The star later acquired its name because, as seen from his village, it rises exactly over the cliff from which he fell.   } {vidblain} {} {space3} {} {1.000} {}
