R {33399} {0} {<278>} {Zacuto} {<278>*  <088>} {  This star, the Astrologer's Star, is known for its role in the development of the astrolabe.  Due to its peculiar precession, it helped astrologers perform the precise calculations required to map out the motions of the stars through the heavens, and thus eventually to construct the tables required to use the astrolabe for much of anything useful.  And so even today, its clear white light in the northeastern part of the sky is a beacon to all who would study the stars.   } {vidblain} {} {space2} {} {1.000} {}
