R {34391} {0} {<278>} {Office of Employment} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You are standing in the employment office.  The room is well-maintained and well-organized, but filled with tension.  Job applicants sit at the tables set in rows and against the walls, filling out the apparently endless forms needed to get through the door for interviews.  Helpful little gnomish assistants move about the room answering questions, administering various tests and directing applicants to the next step of the process.   } {gnomalin} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {34389} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {34392} {0} {<278>} {Office of the Mayor} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  You walk into a room that is decorated with style.  Plush carpeting, wood-paneled walls, painted ceiling, chairs, and tables furnish the room.  A receptionist commands the small desk at the side of the room.  She looks up at your entrance and asks how she can help you.  The Mayor's secretary flits in occasionally, checking with the receptionist to make sure everyone is on the appointment list.  A huge desk dominates the center of the room, but is currently vacant.  Papers are piled all over the desk, and a pair of glasses rests against a steaming drink.  A plaque sits on the desk stating "Mayor".  } {gnomalin} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
