R {34615} {128} {<248>} {Lair of Prince Tumek} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  You have come face to face with the formidable figure of one of the Sahuagin princes.  He is surrounded by several guards and more of the same sharks that you fought in the alcove.  It is not luxurious quarters that this prince resides in.  The walls are more of the rough, cold dark stone that makes up the rest of the stronghold.  They glow softly with a bioluminescence that is emitted from small sea bacteria.  Behind him hangs a skull of shark, with his large jaws open as if the long dead animal is reaching to devour you.  On one side of the room is a carved, stone table.  Some bloodied, barbaric daggers lay alongside a bowl that looks to be filled with body parts of unfortunate prisoners.  A rack of tridents and spears hangs on the wall on the one side of him.  You send a quick prayer to your deity as you prepare to meet this foe who is now staring coldly at you.   } {sahuagin} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
