R {35105} {0} {<228>} {A Forest of Maple and Elm} {<228>( *<088>} {  Away from the savage cliff-face, the woods are vibrant and strong.  Great maples reach skyward, sharing space with the massive branches of elms. Beneath them grow small bushes, through which you can see the scantest of paths, great flagstones that have crackled and crumbled with age.  From the trees you can hear birdsongs.  A continual back-and-forth, the song comes in all directions, the birds flying tree to tree, occasionally landing in the bushes in search of food.  Near the cliffs, the ground is rocky and hard, and the vegetation stops, replaced by a dull, brown moss that chokes out all other life. } {ketu} {} {forest} {} {1.000} {}
