R {35114} {0} {<228>} {The Great Plains} {<228>, `<088>} {  This is the confluence of an endless prairie and the northern woods and hills.  The ash and alder peter out gradually, giving way to the strawgrass of the plains.  Scattered about the earth are large rocks, perhaps the remnants of boulders.  Around you the air is hot and humid.  Away from the shade of the forest, the sun radiates its heat freely, unhindered by the protective arms of the trees. } {ketu} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
