R {35127} {0} {<238>} {The Valley of Shale} {<238>^ ^<088>} {  The precarious hillside gives way to a rock-strewn valley, its appearance one of a long-dried up river.  It continues for some way until it meets a steep slope, and the grade and sharp stones combine to form an impassable barrier. The sun above catches something in the rocks, and at the right angle, you can see a dull glitter from the shale.  Throughout the valley, you see cracks and crevasses begin to form, some a few inches in size, while some stretch several metres. } {ketu} {} {rocks} {} {1.000} {}
