R {35138} {0} {<238>} {The Canyon Ring} {<238>^ ^<088>} {  The path curves here.  You are in the north-western corner of the canyon ring, the gigantic rock casting a shadow directly south of you.  The earth here seems a bit less rocky than elsewhere.  You see more dirt than rocks, each step more even, and less precarious.  The wind constantly twists and turns about the central rock, and when it reaches you, it kicks up small clouds of dust, thin little twisters that rise high enough to get into your mouth, leaving a gritty, dirty feel. } {ketu} {} {rocks} {} {1.000} {}
