R {35441} {0} {<148>} {A Root Hair} {<148>. .<088>} {  A small, hairy root branches from the main roots here, seeking purchase in  the diseased soil that surrounds it. This root seems slightly healthier than  the others surrounding you, but still emits a slight odor of malice and death as you peer into its dark shadows. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35433} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35442} {0} {<148>} {A Wilting Root Hair} {<148>. .<088>} {  The root around you hums in anticipation, although you're not sure what the  excitement is representing. The root around you certainly offers no hint, as  it seems to be wilting, more than likely from a lack of water or other  liquid. The source of that lack can be found north and east of here, but the  end result is a hair root having a major bad hair day. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35436} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35443} {0} {<148>} {A Hidden Root Hair} {<148>. .<088>} {  This root hair is very hard to see, probably due to the blindingly bright  light shining from the moss and fungus growing on the walls. Oddly enough,  this moss seems to be very dry, as is the rest of the root here. No moisture  makes it past the light and the fierce heat emanating from the walls. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35436} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35444} {0} {<148>} {A Clingy Root Hair} {<148>. .<088>} {  This root hair is apparently where all the dead critters in the roots go to  die, or whatever. Or perhaps this is where they're re-animated. Moldy bodies, body parts, and other putrid bits of flesh cling to the walls in this root  hair, some of them actually still moving or waving gently in the breeze. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35435} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35445} {0} {<148>} {The Cork Root} {<148>. .<088>} {  The walls here seem to be made of a slimy, mold-ridden cork. Despite its  mouldering condition, the cork still seems to absorb every sound produced in  the room, casting everything here in a bizarre and unnatural silence. Even  your footsteps and shouts are muted, leaving you in what feels like an  enclosed shell of evil. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35437} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35446} {0} {<148>} {The Vascular Root} {<148>. .<088>} {  The darkness here seems total, while all around you a whispering sound can be heard. It's not in any language you recognize - you're not sure, in fact,  that it IS a language. However, it teases at the edge of your understanding,  bringing to mind images of slimy, creepy dead things which still crawl  through the earth, lusting after blood. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35437} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35447} {0} {<148>} {Hairy Root} {<148>. .<088>} {  Tendrils of root curl inward as you step off the primary arterial root,  seeming to seek out your flesh and blood. The hairs twist around as you  approach them, their sharp, jagged edges resembling broken teeth, and the  rusty color of their long vines seeming to be stained with dried and ancient  blood. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35431} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35448} {0} {<148>} {Primary Controlling Root} {<148>. .<088>} {  The roots here are an odd combination of hair roots and a massive, corked  root that spirals upwards through the diseased soil. Odd lights and fairy  symbols are embedded throughout the spiralled cork, offering no insight on  what it might be used for, or why it's here. However, even getting near it  causes a painful shuddering through the roots and upwards into the tree,  making you cautious about actually touching it. } {tol} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35433} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35449} {0} {<278>} {Your Fuaigh} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  At last you have overcome your fears and emotions by entering your Fuaigh. Now you are worthy to don the Black Robe of a Denali, of Aiighialla. } {empire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}

