R {35596} {0} {<148>} {The Mansion Of Burrows} {<148>. .<088>} {  This burrow is the largest you have seen and based upon its size and  opulence, must belong to a very important rabbit family. The walls are  panelled with wood, giving the home a feeling of being above ground, rather  than an underground burrow. The walls are painted in a subtle earth tone with light brown trim along the border. A table stands in the middle of the room,  and upon it is a vase filled with carrot fronds. A doorway to the north leads to another section of the main level, and a stairway leads upwards to the  sleeping quarters. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
