R {35597} {0} {<148>} {A Civilian Burrow} {<148>. .<088>} {  The burrow is dusty from having been vacant for quite a while. Cobwebs hang  in the corners and the furniture is covered with linen. The potted plants,  starved of water, have died. Whoever lived here perhaps intended to return,  but for some unknown reason has been delayed or worse, has met with a tragic end. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35595} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35598} {0} {<148>} {A Messy Burrow} {<148>. .<088>} {  Toys are strung everywhere making walking almost impossible. Kits can be  heard hopping through the burrow yelling at the top of their lungs. A kitten  is shivering in the corner, apparently traumatized from the kits. The  furniture has been turned upside down and the cabinet doors of the kitchen  stand ajar with packages of vegetables opened and strewn about. Feathers  float through the air as pillows are being swung ferociously through the air. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35595} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35599} {0} {<148>} {A Busy Burrow} {<148>. .<088>} {  Although the burrow is small in size, it is tidy. Every stick of furniture is neatly placed in perfect symmetry. Toys and books are stored in polished wood bookcases, and where there is a bare wall, drawings by the kits of the family are tacked with love. A dining table stands in the middle of the room and it  is set for a dinner of vegetable medley. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35595} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35600} {0} {<148>} {Guard Station} {<148>. .<088>} {  The guard station is a small office-like burrow. A desk covered in paperwork  is set against the east wall and a row of filing cabinets lines the west  wall. Open drawers reveal numerous files that have names and numbers written  upon them. Water drips from a crack in the ceiling, but a wooden bucket is  perfectly positioned to collect the water. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35593} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35601} {0} {<278>} {Inside A Large Tepee} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This is one of the larger tepees in the campground. It is clear that several  of the rebels live in this one tepee. However, it is hard to tell if it is a  family or just individuals sharing their living quarters. The walls are bare  on the inside, undecorated unlike the outside of the tepee. There are five  beds in this tepee varying in size, but even with that information, it is  hard to tell who resides here. } {terramire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {35623} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35602} {0} {<148>} {An Underground Playground} {<148>. .<088>} {  The playground is huge, and continues far to the west and north. Equipment  has been constructed by the slaves to give the kits something to do during  the time of preparation for war. Most parents assign their slave to watch  their children and keep them safe. Many of the kits take this opportunity to  taunt and tease their slave, unaware how dangerous this could turn out, given that some slaves might prove disloyal in the end. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4501} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {35603} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35603} {0} {<148>} {A Playing Field} {<148>. .<088>} {  The field is covered with sand carried in by the slaves of the military. This serves as a safe surface upon which the kits can play and rough-house. Screams of laughter fill the air. War, it seems, is the farthest thing from  the kits' minds. Only when they return home, after a day of play, are they  reminded of conflict and worry in the faces of their parents. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35602} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35604} {0} {<148>} {Veggies 'R Us} {<148>. .<088>} {  The smell of freshly harvested vegetables fills the air. Bushels full of  produce are placed neatly about the shop. The vegetables are brought in from  the military gardens and although they are local, they cost more than they  should. The military overcharge the merchants and they, in turn, raise their  prices to make a profit. } {terramire} {} {underground} {shop} {1.000} {}
E {35616} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35605} {0} {<148>} {A Back Alley} {<148>. .<088>} {  Very little light reaches in to this narrow alley. What little there is,  casts shadows that seem to move of their own will. Cannisters of trash lie  knocked over, their contents strewn across the tunnel floor. The alley feels  dangerous, and few rabbits would enter here, unless they are up to no good. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35616} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35606} {0} {<148>} {A Garden} {<148>. .<088>} {  It seems very out of the ordinary for a garden to be growing underground  without sunlight! However, there is a strong magical presence that radiates  light and heat for the plants and vegetables. The plants and vegetables are  very healthy and some are even ready for picking. They serve as one of the  main resources of food for the military. Many rows have been neatly sown and  the harvest is about to take place. Very few rabbits are allowed here. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4524} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {35607} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35607} {0} {<148>} {A Garden} {<148>. .<088>} {  Each plant in the garden appears to be in the peak of health. The soil is  well tilled and weeded, and it remains damp from the last watering. Vegetables grow in neat rows and are tended to by the slave of the military. They are picked and taken to the kitchen for preparation as soon at the first sign of ripeness. No vegetable or fruit is allowed to over-ripen and be  wasted. The rabbits all enjoy the fresh garden vegetables but few have seen  the garden. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35606} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35608} {0} {<148>} {A Hallway} {<148>. .<088>} {  The hallway is bare except for doors that lead to the officer's sleeping  quarters. None of the officers have to share a room, however, it isn't  uncommon for one of the officers to bring home a date. They aren't required  by the army to share a room, but nothing prohibits it either. The room to the west is uncommon, but does exist.The official part of the quarters is  off-limits to anyone who is not an officer. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
