R {35610} {0} {<148>} {Officer's Quarters} {<148>. .<088>} {  Although no one is here, several torches burn away lighting the room. The  room is warm, even though most places seem rather cool in the rock tunnels of this place. Many pictures and paintings hang upon the wall. The rabbit who  lives here definitely appreciates art. There is a cabinet to the west with an open door. That is the only thing that seems out of place in this place. However, it does appear to be a man only place, as no womanly touches have  been placed upon the quarters. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35609} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35611} {0} {<148>} {Officer's Quarters} {<148>. .<088>} {  The room is very dark and a single light seems hardly efficient to make  things out clearly. A small desk is to the south of the room, next to a large piece of furniture that must be the bed. Along the northern wall, the small  amount of light causes a sparkling in the wall as the light reflects upon the minerals in the rock which the room was carved from. The earth gives way to  rock in various places of the tunnels in the earth, which makes some place  colder than others. The room seems very unimportant really, just an average  bedroom. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35609} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35612} {0} {<148>} {A Shared Officer Burrow} {<148>. .<088>} {  Two officers share this burrow, although there is an empty burrow available. They enjoy each other's company and moving belongings to another burrow seems like a daunting task after a hard day's work. However, it would be simple  enough to bring a slave in to do it. They can run an army, yet not come up  with this simple solution. Both rabbits have thrown their uniforms upon the  floor and the sound of both of them snoring and snorting rings through the  air and can almost definitely be heard in the rest of the officer's quarters. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35608} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35613} {0} {<148>} {Soldier's Sleeping Quarters} {<148>. .<088>} {  Depressions line the ground instead of beds. The soldiers line each  depression with blankets in hopes to keep warm and have a softer place to  sleep. Like drones, the soldiers are pushed too far and they tend to be on  their last leg of sanity. Right where the army wants them. New recruits dream of home and wish very much that they wouldn't have joined the army with an  impending war. A soft sob rings through the room, although no rabbit speaks,  each recruit knows how the other feels. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4521} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35614} {0} {<148>} {Soldier's Sleeping Quarters} {<148>. .<088>} {  Depressions line the ground instead of beds. Each depression is lined neatly  with blankets. None of the empty ones appear to have been slept on in days. The torches never go out making dreams almost impossible for the overworked  soldiers. No one speaks loud, hoping not to disturb the other soldiers. A  large row of lockers line the east wall, a makeshift storage unit for the  soldiers. The lockers are subject to search at any time from an officer. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4521} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35615} {0} {<278>} {The Family Community Center} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Family oriented activities are held here in this burrow on a bi-weekly basis. The army sponsors the events in order to bring a sense of community to the  new housing project. This tactic works quite well as it brings the kits and  their parents out of their homes to mingle with other new residents. Several  picnic tables are set up near a stone grill for community cookouts, and there are markings on the floor of the cavern that suggest the area is used  regularly for rabbitball. } {terramire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {35594} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35616} {0} {<148>} {An Underground Market} {<148>. .<088>} {  Market burrows line the tunnel. Although the area is well-lit, thieves and  pickpockets thrive in this section of Terramire. Shoppers glance over their  shoulders constantly, checking their shadows. There is a narrow ally to the  east, but common sense tells one to avoid it. One cannot tell if a murderer  or cut-throat lurks in such a place. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
