R {35617} {0} {<278>} {A Family Tepee} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Toys are scattered about the tepee. From the looks of this place, the mother has been very busy with out of control children instead of cleaning. The  teepee is a disaster area. The dirty dishes are on the table, exactly as they were left this morning after breakfast. Four plates and a small bowl with  utensils... a family of five it seems. Two of the kitchen chairs have since  been knocked over and a plant has been knocked over as well. } {terramire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {35626} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35618} {0} {<278>} {A Nicely Kept Tepee} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Everything is in its place in this tepee. It appears to belong to only two  minions, as there is a single double bed and a table with two chairs. Paints  and a paintbrush are on a stool near the wall of the tepee, where an  unfinished painting is drying. } {terramire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {35629} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35619} {0} {<278>} {The Equipment Tepee} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This is one of the largest tepees in the camp. Equipment has been stockpiled  in this structure, in preparation for war. There are shields, breastplates,  bracers, boots and leggings. Each piece of armor is handcrafted and put  through strenous testing to ensure that the minions are at least as well  armed as their foes. The date approaches and soon, all of this equipment will be stained with blood. } {terramire} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {35628} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35620} {0} {<148>} {Beyond The Wall} {<148>. .<088>} {} {terramire} {} {underground} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {35621} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35621} {0} {<148>} {The Light At The End Of The Tunnel} {<148>. .<088>} {  You see a light in the distance to the north. It is strange that none of the  troops of Fort Terramire know this place exists. Someone has to know, but  who? The smell of mold pervades the air and slimy looking slugs slide along  the ground, undisturbed by your presence. Jagged rocks peek out from the  earth at intervals as you walk towards a distant light. One slip and no  telling what will happen. Glowing red eyes stare out of the darkness and the  light seems further away now. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35622} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {35620} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35622} {0} {<148>} {The Enemy Campground} {<148>. .<088>} {  These tunnels are the work of undead minions of Dorisaine, sworn enemy of  Fort Terramire. While the military leadership of Terramire concerns itself  with dreams of supremacy over other parts of the world, this small group of  minions have only one thing in mind - the take over of Terramire. They dug  their tunnels deep - very deep into the earth, leaving no evidence behind of  their existence. It would not be at all surprising to find minions walking  along the streets of Fort Terramire, under the very noses of those they wish  to destroy. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
