R {35627} {0} {<148>} {The Cookin' Place} {<148>. .<088>} {  Cast iron pots hang over fire pits and women stand over them, preparing the  communal meal for the village. To the east is an underground garden of root  vegetables. There is a lack of natural light in the village and as a result,  hallowed lights are hung at intervals over the garden to help encourage  growth. Tables have been set for the meal, first seating being for the men,  second for the children and last for the women. But since the women tend to  pick and taste at the pots and vegetables as they cook, they are generally  quite full even before the men get seated. A back tunnel leads out of the  village, but it is hidden and those coming and leaving are very careful not  to be seen. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E { 4537} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {35625} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {35628} {0} {<148>} {Near A Hut} {<148>. .<088>} {  The hut to the east is larger than any of the tepees found to the west and  north. A pulsating sense of evil emanates from the hut and every once in  awhile, maniacal laughter can be heard coming from within. The minions seem  not to notice the disturbance. However, it is hard not to notice. It is the  laughter of someone or something who is truly insane. The dirt path continues to the south and to the west. } {terramire} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {35630} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
