R {36510} {0} {<228>} {A shady spot in the plains} {<228>, `<088>} {  The branches from the large grove of trees to the south extend outward even  to this point. The shade is welcome after so much time in the open and it  appears that even the animals of the plains feel the same. Many tracks of  small scurrying animals dot the landscape here, most seeming to lead off  toward the south west. The reason becomes clear as you stop to listen; the  sounds of murmuring water come from that direction. You can hear the soft  chirping of birds high over head in the branches of the trees, and to the  south you can see the thick trunks of the trees. The sounds of people also  come from the south and it becomes clear that the camp of the roaming nomads is someplace close. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
