R {37031} {0} {<248>} {Stillness} {<248>~ ~<088>} {  The water has finally stopped moving, and you feel weightless in a cavernous  space of indeterminable size. You resolve to seek the surface and begin  swimming upwards. Something bumps into your leg and you spin around, but it  is far too dark to see what it was. While you rise red lights *pop* into  existence all around you, what could they be? They're getting bigger, and you try to swim faster, a sinking feeling in your stomach tells you to flee, but  there's no escape!! } {livingmine} {} {underwater} {} {1.000} {}
E {37028} {swim up} {swim up} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37032} {0} {<148>} {A T-junction} {<148>. .<088>} {  Closer than ever, you can discern the roar is coming from the east. There is  some comfort in knowing where the source is, but not too much. The freshly  hewn tunnel continues to the north as well, maybe that direction is safer. Then again, maybe exploring here was not worth the risk at all. } {livingmine} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
