R {37144} {0} {<218>} {Before a Monolithic Bridge} {<218>/ \<088>} {  You stand before the most awesome sight you have ever seen! Twin stone spires protrude impossibly high up into the mountain, encased in neatly bored  circles. The spires appear to have intricate carvings covering their entire  surfaces, but the stone enclosures make it difficult to be sure. The bridge  itself is easily wide enough for three wagons to cross side-by-side, and  appears sturdy enough to hold an entire army. At least 400 feet long, it's  built entirely out of a material you've never seen before. A faint red-green  glow radiates from the floor of the bridge, slightly disorienting you and  creating an eerie mist that obscures the moving shapes beyond. Although  flames enshroud almost everything, you can see a small corridor between the  flames heading east over the bridge. } {inferno} {} {volcano} {} {1.000} {}
