R {37240} {0} {<218>} {Above the Faultline} {<218>/ \<088>} {  As you near the bottom of the stairwell, you're presented with an awesome sight: the faultline causing the shaking appears to be right below you.  A monolithic bridge, spanning several hundred feet, stretches over what may well be a bottomless fissure.  Fire saturates everything, igniting at will yet needing no fuel.  Staring at the bridge you notice dim shapes moving about in somewhat repetitive patterns and, despite the heat, you feel an icy chill run down your spine...   } {inferno} {} {volcano} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {37130} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37239} {u} {u} {16} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37300} {0} {<238>} {The Pass} {<238>/ \<088>} {  At the southwestern edge of the Halo Mountains lies the entrance to Dusk  Valley.  The pass is fifteen feet wide and half a mile long.  Cliffs on both  sides shoot up hundreds of feet.  The wind at the entrance of the pass screams  through.  Small boulders and rocks continuously fall from above and explode  upon impacting the ground.  The ground is made up of rock, dust, sand, and  crushed up bones.  Near the end the pass where the cliffs end the ground  transitions to a rich farmable soil.   } {duskvalley} {} {mountain} {} {1.000} {}
