E {37906} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37911} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37911} {0} {<228>} {A sandy spot on the river bank} {<228>, `<088>} {  The vegetation gives way here to a sandy bank.  The sand is cool and damp,  with small river stones scattered over its surface.  The river curves  slightly to the north and, out on the water near the bend in the river, you see a small swirl of water.  Silt and sand are pushed toward the bank by that swirl, before the river continues on to the east.  To the north, you  can see more grass and, farther to the northwest, you can just begin to  make out foothills and purple peaks far in the distance.  } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37910} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37907} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37912} {0} {<148>} {Along the river bank} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  The river continues to the west, here, after its slight bend to the  southeast. It appears that its source is someplace in the far off mountains. The water is moving swiftly by on the southern edge of the plains, while to  the north, east, and west the prairie stretches out before you. The openness  of this place is becoming monotonous, and it seems as if these plains will  never end. } {nulan} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}
E {37907} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37915} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37913} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37913} {0} {<228>} {On the river bank near the foothills} {<228>, `<088>} {   The river twists and turns to the south as the cool breeze, coming off  the water, smells of mud and fish.  Insects buzz around you here and the  shrill calls of birds echo across the prairie.  To the west, you see the  beginnings of some foothills, marking the western edge of the plains,  while, to the north, the prairie stretches out before you.   } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37912} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37916} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37914} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37914} {0} {<228>} {Entering the low foothills} {<228>. ^<088>} {   The river falls away to the south, here, as you begin to climb into the foothills.  The mountains are closer, now, and there is a sense of danger  in this area.  The grass underfoot is shorter than out on the grasslands  but it is still lush and green.  Small clusters of flowers break the  otherwise green carpet of the ground and, here and there, a few small trees stretch their wavering limbs toward the sky.  To the north, you can travel  along the foothills while the river provides the boundary to the south.   Further west, the foothills give way to the steep slopes of a mountain range.   } {nulan} {} {hills} {} {1.000} {}
E {37913} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37917} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37915} {0} {<228>} {In tall grass} {<228>, `<088>} {  The grass here is quite tall, over three feet in height. It waves gently in  the soft breezes which perpetually blow over these plains. White clouds race  across the sky, their fanciful shapes seeming to dance to the music of the  breezes. Chirping birds dot the sky, their eyes alert for the abundant food  that thrives in this rich land. To the west, the ground rises to foothills  which mark the boundary of the grasslands and, farther to the west, you can  make out the snowcapped peaks and tree covered slopes of a mountain range. To the north, the grasslands continue. You catch a hint of mud in the breeze  from the south. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37903} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37922} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
