E {37916} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37916} {0} {<228>} {A slight rise} {<228>, `<088>} {    The land begins a slow rise to the north and west here.  Continuing, in either direction, will take you into the range of foothills.  Clusters of flowers dot the landscape and the thick carpet of grass isn't as tall here  as it is to the east.  The openness of this place is beginning to make you  feel just a bit exposed and the looming mountain peaks, far to the west,  look much too foreboding to enter.  The sounds of insects are everywhere and  small birds race the puffy clouds moving overhead.  An eagle's scream echoes, in the distance, and you know that it has ended the existence of something in the world of the living.  South and east, the grassland continues and,  scanning the horizon, you think you can see a herd of animals, though at  this distance, it is difficult to make out what kind.  } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37915} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37923} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
