R {37927} {0} {<228>} {Walking through well cropped grass} {<228>, `<088>} {  The grass here is much shorter than in other places on the prairie. There are many hoof prints scattered over this section of the grasslands, and it isn't  difficult to imagine what animals might have used this spot for food. It  seems as if this is also a commonly used spot for people to rest during long  journeys across the grasslands, at least the comfortable looking haystack  would suggest as much. A cluster of trees is visible to the northwest, which  seems out of place in this expanse of open grassland. Near the trees, a herd  of wild cattle can be seen grazing. To the west, you can see a small stream,  and to the northwest, the plume of smoke is more pronounced. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37926} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
