R {37930} {0} {<228>} {A gentle rise} {<228>, `<088>} {    The land begins to rise here toward the low range of foothills to the west. A small section of the foothills extends to the south and, all around, are  clumps of wildflowers and small shrubs.  The mountains, to the far west, look  quite high and, the closer you get, the more ominous they seem to become.   The sounds of small grassland creatures seem to fade from your ears, somewhat, as you near the low foothills but you can still see birds flying high overhead. A large eagle wings its way off to the west, probably toward its nest high on  one of the mountaintops.   } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37929} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37939} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
