R {37939} {0} {<228>} {Near the foothills} {<228>, `<088>} {    The grasslands rise slowly toward the low range of foothills here. The  grass is very long, just over four feet in height. The sounds of insects and  scuttling creatures can be heard during lulls in the gentle breezes which  make the grass stir restlessly. The sky seems alive with dancing clouds and, far in the distance, the hunting call of a bird of prey echoes over the  prairie.  There is a grove of large trees to the north and east and a plume  of smoke can be seen rising from its center. You can hear thundering hooves  and, occasionally, you catch glimpses of herds of cattle and men on horseback  out on the plains. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37938} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
