R {37940} {0} {<228>} {In the western foothills} {<228>. ^<088>} {    The plant life is a bit thicker here than on most of the prairie.  Small, scrubby bushes dot the landscape and wildflowers and clover carpet the  ground.  This is a relatively gentle section of the foothills.  The ground  is fairly level and very few large rocks are in sight.  The high peaks of  the mountains rear up to the west and a cliff prohibits any further passage in that direction.  To the north, you see flat grassland, though the cliff  turns at this point and you see the chain of foothills continuing farther  to the north and west. To the south, the foothills become somewhat  treacherous and, of course, to the east, the plains stretch back toward the horizon. } {nulan} {} {hills} {} {1.000} {}
E {37939} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37931} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37941} {0} {<228>} {Out on the plains} {<228>, `<088>} {  The grasslands seem alive with wildlife. Small chitters and yips come from  the ground, hidden in the tall grasses of the plains. Errant breezes set the  grass to swaying, and wild flowers to nodding in time with its sighing song. Far to the west, you can make out a grove of trees, and the sounds of running hooves drift to you from the west, as well. To the north and south the plains continue. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {36507} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
