R {37943} {0} {<228>} {A shady spot on the plains} {<228>, `<088>} {  The branches of the large trees stretch out to cover this area of the plains. Small plants shelter under the green branches, and the breezes which seem to  always blow are cooler here than in the open grasslands. Large, thick roots  burrow deep into the ground, their exposed surfaces providing hiding places  for the smaller wild life on the prairie. To the west, the large trunks of  the trees spread out, seeming to enclose something, which you can't quite  make out at this distance. To the north and south, you see more grassland,  and to the far north, you think you can just make out the eaves of a forest. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37942} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {36509} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
