R {37945} {0} {<148>} {A shady spot on the stream} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  To the north and east, the stream runs under the branches of the large grove  of trees. The water is cool and clear and many of its inhabitants swim past,  seeming to revel in the cool shade. Overhead, the sounds of squabbling and  chirping birds fill the air and a few twigs drop from the branches of the  towering trees. To the east, you can see the outer trunks of the grove of  trees and the sounds of playing children and bawling cattle are very  noticeable. The smells from a cook fire drift to you from the south, as well, and you're sure that you can smell roasted venison and beef. Not too far off  to the west, you can see the low range of foothills that mark the western  boundary of this grassland and, far to the north, another visible boundary is just in view, a forest that seems to stretch off to the east and west. } {nulan} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}
E {37944} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37954} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
