R {37947} {0} {<228>} {Out on the prairie} {<228>, `<088>} {    The soft grass and clover here look cool and inviting.  The open sky  stretches off to the north and south and, to the west, the mountains seem to reach into the sky.  To the far east, there is shade to be found under a large grove of trees.  Right here, however, the carpet of vegetation is cool and soft.  The ground is flat and, with the exception of a couple of  openings into a prairie dog's burrow, uninterrupted.  To the southwest, a rockslide blocks part of your view and a stark cliff rises next to the jumble of boulders.  To the west, however, the foothills continue, and continuing west will eventually allow you to climb into the rugged hills.  To the north, you can just make out the eaves of a large forest.   } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37946} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
