R {37956} {0} {<228>} {Near the foothills} {<228>, `<088>} {  The grass here is very tall.  The foothills directly to the west rise out of the grasses, with small stunted trees on their slopes.  The ground on the foothills is a bit more rocky than on the grasslands, though there is still plenty of greenery on their slopes.  Here, the ground is not as flat as it is farther east.  It rises toward the western foothills, and small dips and ruts are treacherous when unseen in the tall vegetation.  The sounds of insects filter up through the tall grasses, as well as those of the small wild rodents which scurry through the grasses on their daily business.  From here, you can travel north into the winding foothills, and you can just see a dark forest in that direction, a physical boundary to this flat land.  To the west, the foothills followed by the imposing range of mountains loom up presenting another obvious physical boundary to the plains.  To the south and east, the large grove of trees stands, and a herd of wild cattle race toward it, the thundering of their hooves vibrating through the ground.  The presence of the wild looking nomads is felt, as well, their eyes seeming to always be on you, and you catch sight of a few, ranging out on the flanks of the wild cattle, seeming to herd and guard the beasts from attack by natural predators and from the more intelligent predators who only wish to deal in hides and fresh meat.   } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37955} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37965} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37947} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
