R {37958} {0} {<228>} {A turn in the foothills} {<228>, `<088>} {    The foothills turn a bit here, bending to the east as they wander across  the western edge of the plains. The stark mountains, to the west, loom high  above the flat, open land.  Occasionally, an eagle flies high overhead on  its way to a nest far up on the cliffs and peaks of the mountains. The  ground here is rugged, rocks and small holes and ravines waiting to injure  the unwary passerby.  A few scrubby bushes and twisted saplings reach upward toward the sky and the ground is thick with high grasses and clover.  All  around, is the feeling of danger and the sense of being watched.  To the  east, the plains stretch out before you and, to the northeast, a forest  looms up as a boundary to the grasslands. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {37957} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37949} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37959} {0} {<228>} {In tall grass} {<228>, `<088>} {  The grass waves gently in the breezes which blow across the plains.  Tall and thick, it hides the ground from sight, but the sounds of insects and small animals come clearly from the hidden recesses of the earth.  Overhead, the clouds dance and shift with the air currents, and the sounds of hunting predators echo across the open grassland.  In the distance, herds of large animals gallop across the plains, and occasionally you catch sight of a Nulan'Boar tribesman on horseback, or a woman moving easily through the plains.  To the southwest the large grove of trees stands alone, looking very out of place in the vast open stretches of green, and to the north, the eaves of a large forest are visible.   } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
E {36507} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {37960} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {37960} {0} {<228>} {Out on the plains} {<228>, `<088>} {  The plains seem to stretch on for miles. The soft grass underfoot looks to be growing back and you guess that, at one time, this was a popular grazing spot for the many herds of animals that call this flat land home. Far to the west  you can make out a low range of winding foothills, and to the north, a line  of trees which lead into a dark forest. The grasslands stretch out far to the south, and to the south and west, the grove of trees stands out like a  beacon. } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
