R {37993} {0} {<228>} {A large cook fire} {<228>, `<088>} {  As you move into the firelight, it becomes apparent that this is the source of all the smoke and smells of cooking.  The large fire is surrounded by men and women turning spits, kneading dough, and cutting meats.  It appears that all the cooking for the entire camp is done at this one large fire.  Spits are loaded with roasting haunches of deer and cow.  Several flat rocks serve as an oven where large, flat pieces of dough become some sort of bread, and there are even a few glowing kettles positioned very close to the fire, steaming and bubbling.  From the smells coming from one of these you guess that the herbs and nuts that some of the women of the tribe bring in are becoming a stew or soup of some sort.  The fire itself does not use much wood.  It seems to utilize more readily available fuel sources, such as dried dung from the herds of animals, and dried grasses.  There are a few chunks of wood scattered among the other sources of fuel, but they are not the most important part of the fire's makeup.  From here, you can travel west into a scattering of tents, or north, deeper into the camp of the Nulan'Boar.   } {nulan} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
