R {38181} {0} {<278>} {The Great Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The great room stands two-hundred feet long and wide, and one-hundred twenty-five feet tall.  The floor at the center of the room is sanded oak planks in a crosshatch pattern.  Marble tiles encompass the wood and stretch to the edges of the room.  A tower rises up above the ceiling nearly fifty feet, and light shines down through its small windows.  Twelve-foot tall portraits of ancient Eldars rest along the walls.  Two rows of armor statues run north to south.  Each statue is placed about every fifteen feet, and there is about forty feet between the two rows.  A few leather couches are staggered around the room with coffee tables set in front of each.  In the exact center of the room is a handcrafted mahogany table with four chairs.  Set up on the table is a small hammer and a leather restraint.  Carved into the mahogany table are rules to the barbaric game of knuckles.   } {afterglow} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
