R {38219} {0} {<248>} {The Cave} {<248>% %<088>} {  The carved-out cave is about two-thousand feet long, five-hundred feet wide, and two-hundred feet tall.  Pathways of different widths have been constructed out of oak directly on top of the stone floor.  A countless number of five-foot wide support beams have been anchored into the ground and rise up to the roof of the cave.  The cave has been sectioned off according to where certain minerals and rocks are found.  Along the  walls of the cave there is evidence of quartzite, granite, limestone, sandstone, coal, gold, diamond, malachite, silver, amber, and several  shades of marble.  Large drops of collected humidity splash down from  the ceiling into small pools.  One of the walls has some writing on it that could be read. } {afterglow} {} {cave} {} {1.000} {}
