R {39654} {0} {<148>} {Exploring the Deep Ocean} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  The sea floor is not devoid of life. Somehow, in this absence of sunlight,  life manages to thrive. Clusters of sponges take up most of the prime real  estate here. These sponges grow like pillars, jutting out of the ground as  fuzzy, orange fingers of a giant. Some of these hand-like sponges have seven  fingers while others have only four. Primitive civilizations might have  considered these to be the hands of gods. } {oceanpark} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}
