R {39764} {0} {<148>} {Challenging Waters} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  After a sharp, considerable drop, the water of the river is white and  frothing. Just when you manage to successfully navigate past a rock, suddenly there is a new rock to worry about. The kayak is getting thrown around like a cat's play toy, and it feels like a small miracle that it is still  right-side-up. Droplets of water rocket through the air and target your  entire body, occluding your vision. } {oceanpark} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}

R {39765} {0} {<148>} {Hazardous Waves} {<148>~ ~<088>} {} {oceanpark} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}

R {39766} {0} {<148>} {Dangerous Rapids} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  Endless whitewater, gigantic waves, humongous rocks, and gut-wrenching drops  characterize this section of the river. The kayak is getting bashed around  severely, causing a great fear to arise that it might get broken. It is such  an intense feeling, to have nature throw the kayak around and exhibit its  unharnessed power. Maybe it's crazy to let nature take control of you like  this, but you feel so much more alive than ever before! } {oceanpark} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}

R {39767} {0} {<148>} {Suicidal Rapids} {<148>~ ~<088>} {  Death is the most likely outcome of such a suicidal venture as this. Rocks  are absolutely everywhere, and the water is inescapable, dousing your entire  body with every inch of movement. There is no safe way to get through this. You already have the skills necessary to navigate through dangerous water,  but what you really need now is a whole lot of luck! And what is that sound  under the crashing of the waves, is it singing? Who would be singing in the  midst of all this turmoil? } {oceanpark} {} {waterswim} {} {1.000} {}

R {39768} {0} {<228>} {Mini Moon Island} {<228>* *<088>} {  Mini Moon Island is the smallest of the Crescent Moon Islands, so that is of  course, how it obtained its name. It is hardly more than a tiny strip of land with a few hardy palm trees that have claimed it as their own. Visitors to  the area have cherished this island as a favorite picnicking spot, but it is  rare for an individual to stay here longer than a couple of hours, since  there is really nothing to do here, aside from enjoy the spectacular view of  the ocean. } {oceanpark} {} {jungle} {} {1.000} {}

