R {40246} {0} {<228>} {An Overgrown Path} {<228>, `<088>} {    The ivy fields to the west blend into a line of brown thorn bushes which have overtaken the pathway. Shredded bits of clothing hang off the razor sharp  thorns and they wave in the breeze. Travelers have stomped across the thick  weeds to try and reclaim the route. Just beyond the line of thorn bushes to  the east stands an ancient hundred-foot tall mausoleum which has been  completely swallowed up by a thick overgrowth of curly ivy. The large oak  door to the building has a strange twisted lock, and directly next to the  door is a small hole just big enough for a small animal to probably fit  though. Underneath the lock on the ground is a small pile of millet  seed shells. Swarms of mosquitoes gather near the ivy along the marble  block walls in the thick humid air. A murder of crows leers down from  a peak on the roof with their black beady eyes. } {shadowsend} {} {field} {} {1.000} {}
