R {40292} {0} {<238>} {The Grove} {<238>( *<088>} {  Piles of various wood-types have been stacked in rows according to their  species and when they were cut down. The skinniest branches and twigs have  been neatly stacked for use as kindling. The mid-sized tree trunks have been  cut into two-foot sections for use in stoking large fires. The most  impressive piles contain eight-foot long planks that have been cut into  two-inch slabs and stacked twenty-feet high. Between each row of lumber  narrow boards allow air to flow and dry them out. } {shadowsend} {} {dead_forest} {} {1.000} {}
