R {40401} {0} {<278>} {The Commodity Trading Floor} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Bustling activity swirls around the commodity trading floor, and the  cacophony of eager, professional voices reaches a level that might almost be  called loud. A higgledy-piggledy network of implicit agreements, traditional  arrangements, and personal favors permeates the negotiations taking place. Traders, representing the landed aristocracy of surrounding countryside  estates, mill about and drive their bargains with implacable determination. Their principal buyer -- the bank itself -- plans to reap great profits  through reselling these commodities to far-flung dukes and princes with whom  they have secured exclusive trade agreements by making expedient offers of  credit. The boisterous atmosphere contrasts sharply with the other rooms of  the bank, in which business proceeds in a more muted, august fashion. The  foyer of the bank can be seen to the south. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40400} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40402} {0} {<238>} {The Office of the Magister} {<238>[ ]<088>} {  A richly appointed office glows with an amber light that reflects off the  luminous wood surfaces of the walls and a sturdy, generously proportioned  desk. The surface of the desk is kept fastidiously neat and the pyramidal  metronome that sits atop it fills the room with the regular beats of its  happy ticking. Two gilt-framed oil paintings, done by old masters, depict the early morning tableau of a picturesque cityscape with breathtaking realism. Overall the office seems to exude an aura of casual power, as if matters of  great import are routinely conducted within it. A massive vault door to the  north serves as an imposing and powerful deterrent to would-be thieves, and  the accounting room opens up to the south. } {stuff} {} {office} {} {1.000} {}
