R {40403} {0} {<278>} {The Accounting Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Three rows of long tables take up most of the space in the center of this  room, and locked glass cabinets crammed full of large, musty ledger books  line the walls. Young men perch on uncomfortable stools set before the  tables, and remain almost inhumanly still for hours at a time while hunched  over their work. The rarely-broken silence seems to amplify even the  slightest sounds: a tentative cough, the creaking of a stool, the rustling of a stiff page being turned all seem unduly loud. Every so often, a clerk will  stand up, retrieve another tattered ledger from the cabinets, and set it on  his desk with a loud thud that sends dust motes swirling into the air. A  slight crack in one of the windows evidences a futile attempt to ameliorate  the stuffiness of the room. The light of the room spills into the bank's  foyer to the west, and into the Magister's office to the north. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
