R {40405} {0} {<278>} {A Room of Ritual} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Arcane apparatuses, ranging in size from a small cube that could be held in  one hand to a slender rod several feet long, reside in several niches set  into the sides of this circular room. The arcane engines are composed of an  unsettling combination of slick, modern materials and things that look like  they date back thousands of years. The silver-grey slate tiles on the floor  flicker with smoky patterns only visible out of the corner of one's eye, and  darker spots on the floor uncomfortably suggest bloodstains. The putrid,  decaying smell of wet leaves or old cheese hanging over the room must be  impossible to cleanse: it remains despite signs of a recent scrubbing. Suspended in the center of the room, four long chains ending in manacles  dangle down from the ceiling and appear to be designed to hold somebody  immobile in the air above a low, flat table. A spiral staircase winding  around the side of the room leads up and on three sides of the room there are doors perfectly flush with the curved walls. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
