R {40407} {0} {<278>} {The Arcane Oculist's Workshop} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  An arcane oculist's workshop, this room is designed to meet all the  requirements for making the lenses and prisms that are capable of detecting  shadows of death. At least one step in the process seems to require bathing  one side of the glass in the light of the three moons. A hole in the ceiling  allows a pale shaft of the moons' light into the room, which is then  separated out by a complicated arrangement of mirrors into a three streams of black, white, and grey, which are focused again onto one side of the glass. The opposite side of glass is bathed in the darkness cast by a magically  inverted candelabrum. Other procedures utilize the workbenches covered in  delicate instruments, powders of fine metal shavings, wires of silvery metal, a torch with a green flame, and a bronze hammer to check etheric vibrations. The room is doused in a the smell of acid that cuts sharply into flesh. Several instruments tremble dangerously due to the powerful energies being  manipulated in the main chamber to the south. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40406} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40408} {0} {<278>} {The Seeing Pool} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  In the center of this quiet, removed room is a triangular pool of water, the  surface of which is perfectly flush with the floor, and that seems to have a  limitless depth. The water speaks with a whispering echo of the voice of the  ocean, and must have been created with a combination of magic and muscle to  help the scryers see more clearly. Other focusing agents include crystals  hanging from the ceiling which refract and diffract the dim light in the  room, casting complicated patterns on the walls. The room also evidences an  interest in sketches and memory games in which one has to remember the  objects placed in view for a short time. These games are designed to train  the eye as the scryers scoff at the notion that seeing things unseen requires the neglect of everyday sight. The imprints of futures are read in the  minute, usually overlooked details found in the surface of the water or the  patterns of light on the wall, visible only to a trained eye. Overall, a  meditative calm envelopes the room that is quite unlike the charged energy of the main chamber that can be felt from the east. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40406} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40409} {0} {<278>} {The Chambers of the Shadow Catchers} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A collegial, fraternal atmosphere pervades this large common room: it seems  that almost everyone in the room is well known to each other. The space itself is slightly disorganized and has evidently seen the customary wear and tear  that comes with ample use. Designed to serve several purposes, much of the  furniture is easily moveable to suit a ceremonial gathering, public  discussion, or informal work space. Given the innocuous bookcases along one  wall, unremarkable tables and chairs, and productive bustle everything at  first glance seems surprisingly domestic. Yet beneath the veneer of everyday  activity, there are hints of something else: at least one clump of people  have gathered close together with heads bowed and have affected nonchalant  glances around the room to see if anyone is listening. The chambers of the  shadow catchers continue to the east and west, while the entrance is farther  to the south. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
