R {40410} {0} {<278>} {The Shadow-Silk Farm} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  In a small wing off to the side of the main common room, a much odder  assortment of objects find a cob-webbed resting place. Most bizarre, an  enormous glass case occupies much of the space, and within it hundreds of  spiders the size of a man's palm are supplied with insect-like prey and  gently induced to build web after web. Special charms -- the result of long  and frustrating experiments -- have been laid over the spider farm to prevent the territorial creatures from trying to eat each other alive. Once a day,  the spiders are put to sleep and the webs are harvested into tangled gobs. The strands are then spun along spinning wheels and twisted to produce usable thread which is stored in great spools. Shadows are stretched and drawn and  pulled and wrapped and spun in much the same way, although spinning shadow is done on a wheel made entirely of a silvery metal. The weavers who work with  the thread wear the same silvery-metal as thimbles on every finger enabling  them to work with the impossibly slippery material. To the east lies the main room of the shadow catchers' chambers. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40409} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40411} {0} {<278>} {The Aerial Rehearsal Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This wing of the chambers has a floor that is curiously spongy or springy as  if a bog had somehow found itself underneath the stone tiles on the ground. Bodies are flying through the air and leaping, twisting, and turning before  they descend back to the ground. They cross impossibly long distances with  the grace of dancers walking on clouds with dazzling precision and incredible speed. The dance becomes even more complex when nets start flying through the air, in a intricate game of tag that happens at lightening quick speed. It  seems that the magic used in capturing shadows of death comes as much from a  ritual binding dance as the weavings in the net. This room opens into the  largest room of the chambers of the shadow catchers to the west. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40409} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40412} {0} {<278>} {The Chambers of the Shadow Bringers} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A vaguely chivalrous attitude prevails in the large common room, the focus of which is a giant circular fireplace surrounded by four curved benches. An  extensive accumulation of a wide variety of knives and exotic blades is  displayed with pride, and it seems likely most occupants in the room could  supply detailed histories of the weapons. The centerpiece of the collection  is a cache where the last shadow knives known to exist in the entire world  are stored. Underneath the air of normalcy that every Umbrifus is at pains to display there is an undercurrent of low murmurs that have teeth set on edge. There are never less than three highly alert Umbrifi appearing to loiter  casually next to the case of shadow knives. The chambers continue with  smaller rooms to the north and east. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40414} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
