R {40413} {0} {<278>} {The School of Deathly Shadows} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Resembling a classroom more than anything else, this space contains a group of benches oriented toward one side of the room, where posters and drawings of the anatomy of three or four different species have been pinned up.  On each poster, crucial attention has been paid to locating the exact places in the body where a person's shadow of death becomes attached.  Next to these posters are various notes explaining the advantages and disadvantages to using each species as a target.  An unmistakable sickly smell of preservatives wafts through the air.  Several long, hermetically sealed boxes that look large enough to contain fresh cadavers are stacked in a corner.  In addition to teaching the crucial lore of shadows of death, the curriculum taught here also engages in philosophical reflection on whether ends can justify means.  To the south lies the main room of the chambers.   } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40412} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40414} {0} {<278>} {The Sparring Chamber} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This room is furnished far more sparsely than anything else in the chambers. Built as a sparring chamber, it consists only of an almost entirely bare  floor. A shielded platform at one end provides a safe vantage point for  watching the combatants. The room is used as an essential part of the Umbrifi training regimen to develop dexterity, quickness, and strength in using a  knife. For not only must one find and severe the spot where a shadow of death attaches, but these warriors must be able to bring a victim to death's  embrace in the first place. And most people do not wait idly for this to  happen. Wooden knives, weighted inside with lead, are used in most sparring  matches to prevent more serious injuries. The Umbrifi also utilize this space to stay physically fit, practicing a type of shadow boxing with swords called floryshe. Adjoining the room to the west is the main common room. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40412} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40415} {0} {<278>} {The Room at the Top of the Stairs} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This small room seems to have been outfitted to serve as an impromptu interview location: a table rests here with two chairs sitting on opposite sides.  The long tasseled rope of a bell-pull hangs from the ceiling intended to summon somebody from the forge without the visitor crossing into their sacrosanct domain.  The whole set-up is a concession wrung from the instinctive guarded secrecy by the practical necessity of cooperation.  To the south is the entrance to the shadow forge and a curving spiral of stairs descends along the circumference of the room down to the room of ritual below.  The stone stairs have been markedly worn down in the middle from the scuffle of a thousand footsteps.   } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
