R {40417} {0} {<278>} {The Shadow Forge} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Two silvery-metallic anvils, one a good deal larger than the other, form the center of the busy activity in this room.  After making the shadows of death malleable in the mysterious fire, smiths lay the material on the anvils.  Then they tap instructions with a small hammer to the strikers who swing massive twenty pound hammers where directed.  Intense ringing overwhelms the room as blow after blow is struck and metal meets shadow with dramatic force.  A shimmering bubble of magical enchantment envelops the air close to the anvil, and the smiths carefully keep their work pieces within the bubble whenever possible.  Several hammers, all made from the same silvery-metallic substance of the anvils, hang on one of the walls.  Smoke billows into the room from the great hearth of the forge to the west, and eruptions of turbulent black liquid can be seen to the east.  Farther north is the entrance to the forge.   } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
