R {40418} {0} {<278>} {The Shadow Forge} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  In this corner of the forge a fiercely crackling fire spews forth voluminous  quantities of smoke. The hood crowning the hearth evidences some effort to  vent the smoke but most of it winds up in the room anyway. The truly  disconcerting part of the fire is the color of the flames -- they are an  eerie shade of grey. Perhaps stranger still is the fact that the fire gives  off absolutely no heat. A shimmering bubble of enchantments surrounds the  hearth to keep impurities out of the shadow stuff as it twists and writhes in the flames. Despite the exhaustive efforts of the assistant pumping the  bellows, the fire burns no hotter. The bellows in fact is poorly situated in  relation to the fire, which seems strange. The room expands to the east where two anvils and many hammers are kept. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40417} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {40419} {0} {<278>} {The Shadow Forge} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Liquid, the blackest black of night, fills a trough that lines the edge of  this room, and it swirls with currents that -- if possible -- are even darker still. From time to time, silver streaks flash across the trough, forking and branching like a spectacular display of lightning. The surface of the liquid  is everywhere uneven, roiling and rolling like the ocean during the approach  of a storm. Hissing, sizzling noise erupts from the liquid each time a piece  of something recently shadow-forged is dipped in by a smith's assistant  wielding silvery-metallic tongs. It sounds for all the world as if something  burning hot had been quenched despite the lack of any perceptible heat. The  room continues to the west, where the mighty clanging on the forge's great  anvils is almost deafening. } {stuff} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {40417} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

