R {42138} {0} {<278>} {A Lip over the Hole} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This bit of a ledge evolves into an even narrower ledge to the north, or  carries onward in a similar fashion to the south. Uniquely, this section of  the ledge also juts outward to the east, as a lip of limestone that extends  out to the middle of this cavern's great pit. This is the only point in this  huge, circular chamber where the floor extends out from the ledge that  follows the wall. The slab of rock that sticks outward is like a long stone  plank, built so that an individual can walk to its end, and upon ignoring all signals of danger, jump into the pit. Perhaps this is where the cyclopses  send disobedient slaves to their doom. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
