R {42145} {128} {<278>} {A Sleeping Dormitory} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This section of the dormitory is a lot like the last. Each space is occupied  by a wood-framed bed, and each bed is covered with several animal pelts. To  the far south there is a hearth, and the only other sources of light are  torches on that reside on the far western side of the room. Therefore, this  section of the chamber is riddled with shadows that grow and fade and are  again reborn as flames from the hearth flicker and tease the walls and floor  with their light. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {42144} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {42146} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {42146} {128} {<278>} {A Sleeping Dormitory} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  Since cyclopses would need far larger beds than the ones in this room, this  must be where they keep their slaves. This section of cave has not been  modified as extensively as the section in the corridor. The floor has been  covered in moss so that it is soft to walk on, and there is a modest hearth  in the south-eastern corner. This room is mainly for sleeping. Two dozen beds have been set up throughout this dormitory. Each bed is made from an oak  frame, with legs, a headboard, a foot-board, a mattress, and a pillow. Several animal pelts cover each bed, since it must be awfully cold sleeping  in this dank chamber. There are a couple of dressers standing along the  western wall, and these have enchanted lanterns sitting upon them. These  lanterns are the only light sources in the room, aside from the hearth. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
