R {42148} {0} {<278>} {An Enchanter's Room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The walls, ceiling, and floor of this room are lined with smooth, grey  stones; exactly like the corridor to the west. The room is small,  rectangular, and terrifically cluttered. It looks like this room has been set up for an enchanter. At the center of the room is a tall table, the perfect  height to stand at while creating potions. The wall to the east contains  shelves that have been stuffed full of books and scrolls. The northern wall  is flanked by a counter that has been stocked with empty vials and a myriad  of ingredients in bags, jars, and other strange-looking containers. The  southern wall contains a rack that carries items similar to those upon the  counter to the north. Dozens of candles are being used to keep this room lit. They don't seem to be enchanted, since they are dripping wax all over the  table where they have been placed. There are red candles, white candles, and  black candles. The room smells of old parchment, something like vinegar, and  candle wax. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {42142} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {42149} {0} {<278>} {A Small Forge} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This chamber is not large, and it is not elaborate either. The walls and  floors have been lined with smooth grey stones, like the corridor to the  east, and the room's shape is practically a perfect cube. There are no  enchanted lights in this room, so it must be largely unused. The chamber was  obviously at some point used as a forge, but it looks to have more recently  become a sort of storage area. In the middle of the room, there is a wrought  iron anvil that has several crates piled on top of it. The far wall of the  chamber has also been piled up high with crates. Looking inside of them  yields nothing of great interest. Many crates are empty, but a few contain  smelly animal pelts, clay mugs, and clay pitchers. There is an  industrial-looking hearth that takes up the entire northern side of the room. The hearth is cold and empty, a sign that it definitely has not been used in  some time. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {42142} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {42150} {0} {<248>} {A Cyclops Pit} {<248>% %<088>} {  After a nasty fall, anyone who decides to enter this pit will find themselves landing on a soft pile of cyclops carcasses. Yes, it is disgusting, but the  cyclopses do not seem to mind. They lounge in this pit like happy walruses,  and are undisturbed by the scent of their rotting kin. Of course it is  impossible to remain undetected in this pit, it's like putting a spotlight on oneself. This is where the cyclopses eat, sleep, and fight. The entrance to  the pit is just a very tiny pinpoint of light from way down here, and the pit itself is pitch black. } {uprising} {} {cave} {pk} {1.000} {}
E {42138} {climb out} {climb out} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {42151} {0} {<178>} {Entering the City Proper} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  This is the city proper. To the south reside the remains of the city gates,  which are now little more than a massive mess of splinters and rubble. The  city proper has not fared much better. The only bit of it that is still  entirely intact is the durable black limestone of the cobblestone road. Several statues have been eradicated here, as well as an entire guardhouse. There must have been some powerful magic used in order to tear everything  into such pieces. It looks as if a tornado touched down here. A very angry  tornado. Curiously, the bodies of the statues are practically disintegrated,  but their heads remain toppled about on the ground, staring blankly, and  looking every bit as if they are completely befuddled by their current state. } {uprising} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
