R {42156} {0} {<278>} {Entrance to the Temple of the Night} {<278>. .<088>} {  In order to reach the entrance to the most important building in the dark elf city, the Temple of the Night, there is a path that heads up a cluster of stalagmites that have grown together into a strange, gnarly pattern. The path twists up, and up, and up, through the middle of a massive cavern. How is it that these stalagmites grew to be so tall, and how lucky were the dark elves to find a cavern so large? One very likely possibility is that the dark elves used their magic to create this cavern and all that is within it. Near the top of the mass of stalagmites, is the temple entrance. At this point the stalagmites have somehow managed to wrap themselves around the temple's set of double doors. It is tough to discern exactly what is going on, because the doors are a glossy black, and the stalagmites are also black. This setting is the stuff of nightmares. To make things more confusing, will-o'-the-wisps dance across the scene every so often, further impeding the ability to discern what is going on by occluding vision with their bright flash of light. The path is made of shiny, slippery, obsidian stones, and the temple door is flanked with imposing statues depicting the handmaidens of the great goddess of the dark elves. Their goddess is simply known as the Dark Lady, since invoking her true name is said to bring with it her wrath. The handmaidens are serpentine, with elven torsos and heads. They wear armor that has been built from the skulls of the Dark Lady's enemies. The lower halves of their bodies are like the bodies of snakes, and they also have dragon-like wings on their backs. Their faces are drawn back in snarls, daring the uninvited to open the temple door. } {uprising} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
