R {43351} {0} {<238>} {Jailor's tent} {<238>[ ]<088>} {  Stepping into the tent has the same effect as stepping into the camp from  the forest; the sounds from the camp are still clearly heard, however the  breeze from the forest can be felt. A desk stands in the center of the tent,  neatly ordered stacks of paper atop. A lone piece of paper lies by itself on  the desk, and appears to be a prisoner manifest. Armor and weapons line the  walls, along with various torture devices. What kind of tent is this? } {siege} {} {hut} {} {1.000} {}
E {43350} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43352} {0} {<238>} {A dangling cage} {<238># #<088>} {  Swaying dangerously in the forest breeze, this cage dangles from a large tree close to the camp. An insane amount of clanking and cursing comes from a  small clay building to the east. The cursing sounds like something other than a kobold, however. There is a surprising lack of magical energy in the cage,  despite being surrounded with some of the eldar's best soldiers. } {siege} {} {cabin} {} {1.000} {}
E {43350} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43353} {0} {<238>} {A dangling cage} {<238># #<088>} {  This cage is more in the forest than it is in the camp. It dangles  precariously from a giant tree, at the mercy of the environment. The sounds  from the camp are dulled by the distance; however the eerie quiet from the  white tent to the south is unnerving. Considering how many magical creatures  are in and around the cage, there is a surprising lack of magical energy  here. } {siege} {} {cabin} {} {1.000} {}
E {43350} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43782} {0} {<178>} {A Collapsed Section of the City Wall} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  All around the dark elf city there is an obsidian stone wall. In many places, the wall's stones have been built up against natural cave walls, simply for  decorative purposes. In others, the city wall has been built in order to cut  off entry from an open tunnel, so these sections of wall serve a greater  purpose. This tunnel once contained one of the more important sections of the city wall, but it has been pummeled into oblivion. Bits of the wall rest in  crumbled piles all over the ground. A tent has been set up where the wall  once stood, in an attempt to block the greater part to this tunnel's  entrance, as well as to serve as a handy place for guards to sleep. Many  guards have been ordered to keep the city's perimeter secure, but they won't  be spending very much time resting in the tent. The guards are constantly on  call, and have orders to obtain no more than a minimal amount of sleep in  these dangerous times. The tent's entry flap has been left invitingly open. } {uprising} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {42158} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43783} {enter tent} {enter tent} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43783} {0} {<278>} {A Military Tent} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This is a rectangular tent, with extra-high walls, and therefore a peak that  is even higher. The tent is spacious enough to stand up in, causing it to be  quite comfortable for its temporary use as living quarters. Once inside, it  is noticeable that this tent contains two door-flaps, one facing the dark elf city, and the other facing away from it. Three poles hold up the entire  contraption. One stands upright, and the other two secure the tent  horizontally at its top. There is a stove hole located at what could be  considered the back of the tent, but the stove is not in use at the moment. The base of the tent is lined with canvas and bedrolls cover it. The bedrolls line the wall to the north and the wall to the south, so that there is an  aisle through the tent's center, for walking unimpeded. The whole scene is  very neat and orderly, exactly as one would expect from persons operating  under rules of strict discipline, as these dark elves surely are. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {43784} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43782} {exit tent} {exit tent} {0} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43784} {0} {<278>} {A Military Tent} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This section of the tent is similar to the last, but the entry flap to the  east has been secured shut, whereas the entry flap to the west still stands  invitingly open. Bedrolls have been laid out in a neat row, their heads  planted against both the northern and the southern walls of the tent. The  tent is so tidy that it appears as if no one has ever slept in it. The walls  are made of a dark grey canvas, and everything is just a bit damp due to the  moist atmosphere of the cave. } {uprising} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {43783} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43785} {0} {<178>} {A Collapsed Roadway} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  To the east the city still burns uncontrollably. The flames are massive and  the direction is blocked off with toppled rock, fallen stalactites, and  toppled stalagmites. This mess extends itself nearly to the roof of the cave, but there are gaps in between the bits of debris where one can see the fiery  flames as they burn. The smoke in the air is thick enough here to summon a  cough with almost every breath. Therefore, walking in a sort of crouch in an  attempt to evade some of the smoke, and to actually be able to see where one  is going, seems most wise. Since the road to the east is impassible, any  travelers are basically forced to head back to the west from here. There is  so much rubble on the ground that it is difficult to pick a spot to step, so  traveling is slow going. } {uprising} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {42155} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43786} {0} {<178>} {A Burned-Out Forge} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  The disastrous city fire did not spare this small forge, but it looks like  the dark elves have been in here recently, possibly even this very day. It  seems that they don't have time at the moment to tear down the burned-out  building and build from scratch, but they do have need of a forge. Therefore, they have made this room useful. The hearth that serves as the  forge is happily crackling away in the far right-hand corner, the smoke being filtered out through a mysterious chimney that must lead to some unused  cavern above the dark elf city. A freshly painted sign stands beside the  forge with useful instructions for novice blacksmiths. Since the room's walls are made from stone, the damage to the overall structure of the building has  been minimal. The items inside of it, however, must have been a different  story, since the ones here now all appear to be brand new. A stout square  anvil stands near the hearth, with a hammer leaning against its side. A  trough of clear water sits close to the door. The wall opposite the hearth is accompanied by a tall wooden table that has an empty weapons rack, bellows,  and pliers sitting on top of it. } {uprising} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {42155} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43787} {0} {<278>} {A Residential Road} {<278>. .<088>} {  This is the section of the dark elf city where its most highly regarded  members of the community usually reside. The houses that surround the road  were at one time the largest, and most exquisite in the entire city. Now they are but shadows of what they once were. It is evident that the dwellings were once beautiful, judging by the wondrous stonework that now litters the  roadway. The stones that are visible here on the ground in the midst of the  rubble, have been uniquely carved, or polished. Many of the stones are black, or dark grey, but there are some that are emerald, ruby, or amethyst in  color. While the houses in this section of the street have been pretty much  leveled to the ground, the ones further to the west still stand on either  side of the street, so they could be interesting to explore. To the east can  be found the remnants of what was once the dark elves' marketplace. } {uprising} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E {42154} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43788} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43788} {0} {<278>} {A Residential Road} {<278>. .<088>} {  This has the look of the end of the city. The road to the west has been  blocked off by a wall of obsidian stone that stands at least fifteen feet  high. And indeed, unlike other sections of wall in the city, this one does  still stand. The disaster that wracked this city seems to have had less of an impact on this particular corner of it. To the east, the residential  buildings have been basically destroyed, but the houses to the north and  south of this corner, are still standing. They are burned out husks of what  they once were, but at least they can still be recognized as buildings. The  buildings almost match each other when examining their exteriors. They have  both been made to look like castles, with tall stone walls including a sort  of keep as well as turrets. It looks like there may have been a neatly  sculpted, underground version of a lawn in front of each building before the  fire, but now the ground is burnt to smithereens. Stone steps lead up to the  front door of the main building on either side of the street. The front doors are even still intact, so it might be worth exploring. } {uprising} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E {43787} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43789} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
