R {43789} {0} {<178>} {A Burned Out House} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  Upon entering the building, it is obvious that its interior isn't as  interesting as was hoped. The front door almost doesn't even open, because  the ceiling of the building has collapsed in on itself. Anything that was  inside has either been badly burned to unrecognizable bits, or has been  smashed or crushed by objects that fell while the building burned. The smell  of the ashes is strong and the air is crisp and harsh to breathe in. The only point of interest left in here, is a stained-glass window on the eastern side of the building. While some of it must have exploded in the heat, there are  still a few broken pieces that sit within the window frame. The pieces are  crimson red in color, as if they are attempting to convey the suffering that  went on in here. } {uprising} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {43788} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43790} {0} {<178>} {A Burned Out House} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  This building's interior did not survive the fire's wrath. It isn't  particularly interesting to look at, either. Piles of rubble lie about the  room. A set of stone stairs leads up to nothing at all, because the second  floor of the building caved in at some point. It's amazing to think that this building would have recently contained one of the wealthiest dark elf  families in the city. Now it looks like any other abandoned, burned-out  building. Aside from the acrid scent of smoke that hangs in the air, this  building could have been abandoned like this for years, considering the way  it looks. } {uprising} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {43788} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43791} {0} {<268>} {Northern Edge of the Dais} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  The dais is the most beautiful part of this temple. Enchanted motes of light  rain down endlessly like stardust and cause a kaleidoscope of color to play  over the statues and other decorations that are on the dais. The dais has a  surface made from red marble, causing it to look as though it has been spread with the blood of sacrificial victims. Fresh-looking black flower petals have been scattered all over it, and this portion of the dais features three  larger-than-life, cast bronze statues. The statues depict three of the dark  elves' most treasured demigoddesses. On the left sits the demigoddess of  fortune, wearing a wealth of jewels. To the right stands the demigoddess of  fame, perched upon a pile of skulls and grinning menacingly. In the center  stands the demigoddess of time, who has been depicted as if she is getting  ready to smash a sundial with a hammer. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43792} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43794} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43792} {0} {<268>} {Approaching the Dais} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  To the west is the temple's dais. Since everything in this temple seems to be magnified in size, the dais is raised so high, that from ground level in this hall, an individual can not even see what the dais floor looks like. This  makes sense, since dark elves tend to use levitation to engage in all of  their activities. In case an individual is not utilizing the power of  levitation, there is a spiraling staircase made from a tree that leads up to  the floor of the dais. Interesting that the dark elves have used plants and  trees in this temple, whereas outside in the cave tunnels, they tend to only  use stalagmites. It is almost like the dark elves are secretly paying homage  to their ancestors who lived above ground. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43793} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43791} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43793} {0} {<268>} {A Hallway in the Temple} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  As an individual travels deeper into the temple, it becomes easier to see  what is going on inside of it. It's as if the black mist has completed a full inspection, made a decision that whatever tests that have been run, have been passed, and as a result, retreated down to the ankles of the curious  explorer. There are sculptures made from black marble; cast bronze  sculptures; and sculptures that have been made out of more unusual materials, like tree trunks and unknown types of rock that glow blue or red. Strange  large plants grow in the room, emerging right from the floor and twisting  around the temple's black stone columns. Somehow, these plants manage to not  crack the black marble floor. What can be seen of the room's great black  stone columns from beneath these enveloping plants, is covered with  glittering black and white diamonds that have been fixed to the columns in  enchanting swirly patterns. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43795} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43792} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43794} {0} {<268>} {At the Pulpit} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  The center of the dais features a statue honoring the Dark Lady. Since the  Dark Lady does not like to hear her name spoken by mortals, or for them to  depict her in her true form, the dark elves have created a sculpture of her  as she likes to appear to mortals when she is feeling especially mischievous. At these times the Dark Lady enjoys taking on the form of a grotesque-looking monster, and subsequently scaring all of those who have been disloyal to her. This is a monster with nothing more than an elven skull for a head, an undead dragon's body and wings, and a gigantic scorpion tail, complete with a  venomous stinger. This statue is at least fifteen feet tall, and has been  created from white marble; in stark contrast with its dark surroundings, and  therefore the focal point of the room. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43791} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43796} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43795} {0} {<118>} {Inside the Temple of the Night} {<118>[ ]<088>} {  This is no normal temple. Stepping into the Temple of the Night is like entering into a different type of reality. It is dark as night, and a sound like whispering seems to come from every direction. Sometimes the whispers get so close to the ears that it seems as if whatever is making the sound is hovering right beside them. The shadowy mist that began to make itself known at the temple entrance is even thicker in here. When it is so thick that it is difficult to see, a strong floral scent arises, then the mist always seems to dissipate a bit, but the smell is overwhelming enough to cause dizziness. The floors in the temple are black marble, and echo a loud clacking noise with each step an individual takes, since the temple hall is so massive. Whenever the black fog clears enough to be able to look around, it is still difficult to see, since it is so dark. There is a faint light emitting from a source high above, however. Upon looking upwards to investigate, it is revealed that some sort of enchantment has been added to the temple to make it appear as if there are tiny points of light lurking up high in the temple's rafters, like stars. The swirls of mist move away to reveal statues that depict gruesome-looking creatures, and other expensive adornments to the temple, then quickly hide them again, teasing the onlooker. } {uprising} {} {bloodyroom} {} {1.000} {}
E {42156} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43793} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43798} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43796} {0} {<268>} {Southern Edge of the Dais} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  This section of the dais is similar to the other sections, in that the floor  is made from crimson marble, mimicking the look of the blood of sacrificial  victims. A six foot long slab of obelisk stone has been placed near the wall  to the west; this being a spot where, undoubtedly, sacrificial victims must  make a regular appearance. Upon the wall to the north, a triptych of  paintings has been mounted. It details the religious history of the dark  elves, from when they were first saved by the Dark Lady, to the first time  that she interceded in a major battle that the dark elves were losing, to  more recently, when she appeared to the dark elves, to bring them new hope. The dais is dark, but enchanted motes of light fall from an invisible source, descending until they land upon an object, whereupon they burst into  nothingness. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43797} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43794} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43797} {0} {<268>} {Approaching the Dais} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  The temple's dais looms to the west. In order to reach it, there is a twisted tree that winds its way over to the dais's surface, with a set of stairs that have been meticulously carved into it. The great trunk grows right out of  the temple's black marble floor, looking every bit as if this is a normal  occurrence. The tree trunk leads up to the dais, which has been made entirely out of red marble. Around the tree trunk, drape curtains of blue moss, like  spiderwebs. The temple is cool, but not as damp at the outside tunnels, so in that respect, more comfortable. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43798} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43796} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43798} {0} {<268>} {A Hallway in the Temple} {<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>} {  At this point in the temple, black mist swirls about the wary traveler's  ankles. Perhaps the mist serves as some sort of security device, since it  seems to completely dissipate to the west. This section of the temple is  filled with organic adornments. Many beautiful potted plants have been placed on slabs of black marble, at varying levels. These plants are all so exotic,  that they are completely unidentifiable to the uneducated eye. The bulk of  these plants look a lot like a rainbow of water lilies that sit in dirt  rather than water, and the others seem to be varieties of mushrooms that all  glow in the dark. Some of these mushrooms are as large as trees and ooze a  sticky white substance. The wall behind the plants is covered with a soft  blue moss, and the floor is made from black marble. } {uprising} {} {temple} {} {1.000} {}
E {43795} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {43797} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {43800} {128} {<248>} {Beyond Dark Curiosity} {<248>[ ]<088>} {  Huge wooden doors, withered with age, stand to the north. There is nothing  but darkness to the south. An unsettling dread descends upon you over the  idea of proceeding forward. Small candles line the walls, each of them not  properly illuminating any of the surroundings. The candles seem to have a  small detail within their flames, but it will only make sense upon closer  inspection. } {crynn} {} {chessblack} {} {1.000} {}
