R {44529} {0} {<248>} {Approaching the City} {<248>% %<088>} {  This bit of tunnel is as dark, damp, and cold as the section of tunnel before it. Why anyone would want to perpetually subject themselves to this sort of  environment seems ridiculous, but there are tales of the dark elves'  banishment from the surface lands of Andolor, so maybe life underground is  their only choice. They do seem to flourish down here; it is said that a  single dark elf can survive for centuries. Freakish sculptural reliefs leap  out from the walls of this tunnel. There are monstrous, dragon-like  creatures, with mouths wide open, attempting to devour dark elf warriors. In  the same scene, dark elf priestesses have been sculpted. They are  manipulating golems that seem to be successfully holding back the onslaught  of these dragon-like creatures. What makes the scene so grotesque, are the  dead bodies and random body parts that litter the ground in the scene, that  have been rendered with a frightening sort of realism. } {uprising} {} {cave} {} {1.000} {}
