R {44568} {0} {<248>} {A Gentle Turn in the Tunnel} {<248>% %<088>} {  This tunnel is cold and damp, but upon its walls grow thousands of  multicolored crystals. These crystals are far from average, because they glow in the darkness. There are hundreds of blue, yellow, green, orange, purple,  and red crystals. It is almost as bright as daylight in this tunnel, and as a result, it feels safer than the other tunnels in the area. Creatures that  live underground prefer the cover of darkness, as light can be cruel to eyes  accustomed to peering through pitch black caves. Also, those who use darkness as their ally when hunting, are at a severe disadvantage in a tunnel such as  this. These crystals must have been added by some sort of eclectic sorcerer. It is a pity that there was no hint left behind to figure out how they ended  up here. There are a few other interesting geological formations in this  tunnel, and it may prove interesting to investigate them. } {uprising} {} {cave} {} {1.000} {}
E {44567} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
