R {44572} {0} {<248>} {A Widening Tunnel} {<248>% %<088>} {  The tunnel begins to widen out a bit here. Strange holes exist in the tunnel  walls. They look a bit like the holes in an anthill, only on a larger scale. However, if this is the case, they must have been made by an ant of at least  five feet in length. Or possibly by a gigantic worm. The holes are so  perfectly round, the image of a humungous worm almost seems logical. That  really does bring the tickle of a memory, something about enormous worms  living underground. Would such a worm eat more than just dirt, is the most  worrisome question. Aside from the network of round holes in the wall, there  are several geological formations of interest in this tunnel. Perhaps it  would be a good idea to investigate them. } {uprising} {} {cave} {} {1.000} {}
