R {44573} {0} {<248>} {A Slight Turn in the Cave} {<248>% %<088>} {  At this point, the path takes a turn to the west, continuing in a gently  sloping decline. Walking through this tunnel is a bit complicated, because  cumbersome, bushy growths of calcite emerge in a tangle from the floor,  looking a bit like coral reefs. The largest bush in the cave is about 6 feet  tall, and there are dozens of others that have attained a similar height. At  least they allow a traveler some cover, but of course they make great hiding  places for predators, as well. There are several other interesting geological formations in this cave, maybe it could prove useful to investigate them. } {uprising} {} {cave} {bank} {1.000} {}
