R {45673} {0} {<238>} {Clark Park, At Least It Used to Be} {<238>, `<088>} {  Bent and twisted metal is contorted and scorched as it acts as a makeshift  lightning rod. It must have been from the time before that monstrous tower  was built. It is easy to imagine that this used to be a children's  playground. There are empty patches of land where picnic tables might have  been. Tar paper shingles lie in various piles, proving that there might have  been a roofed pavilion here at one point. What is here now is a statue, a run down chipped statue. The plaque beneath it is somehow still here and not part of the tower structure. } {fury} {} {dead_field} {} {1.000} {}
E {45672} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {45674} {0} {<278>} {Approaching Fury City} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you continue forward along the crudely overgrown road, you see what's left of Fury City just ahead of you. Tufts of weed grass grow out of every crack  in the road. An albino deer spots you and runs off towards the small patches  of wooded areas outside of the town. A crack of thunder startles you as you  look up at the sky and take another good look at the tower ahead of you. It  seems like it might have been an actual building of maybe five or six floors. The rest of the tower looks like it is made of pieces of all of the other  buildings dangerously fitted together reaching towards the red sky. } {fury} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
E {45675} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
