R {45681} {0} {<178>} {Spices In The Air} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  Crossing the carved teak threshold, you notice a low wooden platform crowded  with worn leather jutis-some cracked, others dusted from travel. A household  of many guests, perhaps. The floor is covered with a faded woolen durrie, its dyes dulled by years of footsteps. Opposite the shoe stand, a bamboo rack  leans against the mud wall, draped with soft, fraying pashmina shawls. To  your right, the scent of cumin and mustard seed drifts from a clay chulha. A  brass spice box sits nearby, filled with turmeric, chilies, and garam masala. The cookfire glows gently. At the far end, beneath a carved niche, rests a  sagging charpoy-ready for a weary guest to recline and share stories by  lamplight. } {fury} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {45676} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
