R {45682} {0} {<178>} {Nirvana it is Not} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  A broad charpoy dominates the chamber, its woven frame wide enough for a  small family, layered with fine cotton sheets and embroidered blankets. Overhead, a jagged opening in the thatched ceiling admits a pale shaft of  light-strangely colorless amid the rooms ruddy hues. Against the lone  standing wall rests a carved teak armoire, its doors slightly ajar, revealing folded kimkhwabs in soft pastel tones. Scattered across the earthen floor are wooden toys and clay figurines, some teetering near gaping holes that reveal  the level below. The air feels brittle here. Perhaps it is wise not to  linger. } {fury} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {45681} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {45683} {0} {<278>} {The Rude Way} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you turn the corner, you are met with more destruction, more things broken and battered. You are beginning to think that more than just the storm  wrecked this place, with derelict buildings to the left and right of the  worn-out road. One missing brick is threatening to trip you. You do notice  that between two wrecked buildings, there is an alleyway to the east. North  and south, the road continues. } {fury} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
