R {45686} {0} {<178>} {Traditional Values} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  After entering the doorway, you begin to take in the entire room. Just like  everyone else in this forsaken place, everything is in a state of decay. The  walls are lined with ceremonial candles wherever there isn't a hole allowing  in the elements of the storm. On the west wall, a table with a box seems to  be empty of the coins it is intended to capture. There is a modest  kitchenette to the east, a small table in between holds two religious books. The occupants behave as if there is nothing wrong with their slowly crumbling home. } {fury} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {45685} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {45687} {0} {<178>} {Tornado Alley} {<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>} {  Entering into this home, you find everything somehow in more chaos than  anywhere else. Everything that is still in some kind of working fashion is  wide open. All the dishes are smashed on the floor. The carpet is bunched up  against the far wall with a small end table. Whoever lives here has no regard for keeping things neat and tidy. The one thing that is intact is an old  chair, but other than destroying it, there isn't much you can do to it. } {fury} {} {ruins} {} {1.000} {}
E {45684} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {45688} {0} {<278>} {Hero's Way} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This section of the city, this dilapidated road, is named for you, or someone like you. You can even make out a half-hanging street sign saying "Hero's  Way" with celebratory bordering, signifying that this was an honor bestowed  on someone from another time. The sky continues to flash red with an  accompanying rumble as the storm continues to rage on. The tower looms ever  higher to the east, inaccessible from here. To the west is another one of  those semi-intact buildings. The Way continues to the north. } {fury} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
