R {46068} {0} {<148>} {The Symbol of the Forgotten} {<148>. .<088>} {  The ceiling of this temple is really quite elegant. The room's columns  actually continue right into it like structural ribs. The ceiling is vaulted, and pointed arches have been created wherever the ribbed vaulting meets at  its center between each set of columns. The overall shape is a lot like that  of a spider's web. } {dungeon} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {46067} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {46065} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {46069} {0} {<148>} {The Symbol of the Forgotten} {<148>. .<088>} {  Looking toward the far west of this section of the temple and above its  golden altar, there is a giant stained-glass window that fits neatly in the  space just under the pointed arch. Though this is the space where in a  cathedral one would normally find a rose window, instead the minotaurs have  made their window look like a giant eye. The iris of the eye is blood red and strong white, red, green, purple and blue segments also exist within it. The  window is somehow backlit, though it is impossible to tell how from this  vantage point. } {dungeon} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {46070} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {46061} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {46070} {0} {<148>} {The Symbol of the Forgotten} {<148>. .<088>} {  Looking out from this part of the temple, it is easy to see how the room's  seating has been set up. From west to east, wooden benches have been placed  into two long rows. The benches all face the golden altar that sits against  the eastern wall of the room, and they stop about 10 feet away from it. Each  bench is made from oak and has been polished to a soft sheen. } {dungeon} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {46062} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {46069} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {46071} {0} {<148>} {The Symbol of the Forgotten} {<148>. .<088>} {  Stairs lead up to the golden altar that fills this end of the room. It is  framed by two low-hanging chandeliers. The altar itself is long and  rectangular. Both on top of the altar and behind it, there are many statues  of winged creatures. From far away they look like angels, but upon closer  examination they reveal themselves to have grotesque features. } {dungeon} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
E {46072} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {46062} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {46072} {0} {<148>} {The Symbol of the Forgotten} {<148>. .<088>} {  This golden altar is extremely ornate. In its front and center, staring out  at whoever might be sitting in the congregation, is a giant golden eye. On  top of the altar, many golden candles have been lit and they shed their soft  light upon a painting that hangs just overtop of the altar. The painting  shows the ghostly-looking image of someone who is not of this world. The  image creates such abject terror in any onlooker that it has the power to  send chills through their body and briefly paralyze them.    * A giant golden eye is the focal point of this altar.  } {dungeon} {} {underground} {} {1.000} {}
