R {46963} {0} {<238>} {A dried up river} {<238>^ ^<088>} {  This river has long since dried up and all that is left now are the smooth  stones of the riverbed. Driftwood lies scattered along the length of the  river and in fact, grasses and young plants are growing in the less stony  parts. The river was relatively shallow and as such the dried up bed is very  easy to cross. There seems no point in following the river's course as it  seems to go on north and south for as far as the eye can see. The best way out is to climb out of the ravine. } {tanra} {} {rocks} {} {1.000} {}
