R {47018} {0} {<278>} {Beginning of marble path} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A wide, immaculately laid marble path stretches north from this place toward  a shining palace. Along the path, beautiful green fields and flower patches  grow in gardens bordering both the east and west. The occasional child  scampers across the path to his or her delight, chasing flower petals and  butterflies on the breeze. The palace itself is a shining white structure  framed by a large dome and hand-carved statues of singers, musicians, and  dancers inlaid upon each of its corners and edges. Above this walkway stands  a 15 foot marble archway, to the exact proportions of the crumbled archway in the ruins, had it still been intact. And in fact, the palace ahead is to the  exact proportion of the remaining base stones left standing in the ruins. At  the center of the tiles on this spot, a plaque bears an inscription. } {songpalace} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
