R {47019} {0} {<228>} {A quiet grove} {<228>. ^<088>} {  This clearing has likely sat here for ages, hidden from above by tree roots,  mud, moss, and rock. The foliage creates a natural dome-like structure under  which some old fallen logs have been arranged in a circle around a firepit. The fire itself is quite unnatural in shape and nature - it glows a hot blue  and is in the shape of a tuning fork. When approached, the fire changes form  into a cryptic message. It appears to be the one untouched relic of the great structure that once stood east of here. } {songpalace} {} {field2} {} {1.000} {}
E {47016} {e} {open e;e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47020} {0} {<278>} {Path through the gardens} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  This portion of the gardens imbues a sense of tranquility. Faint music can be heard from the Palace to the north when a production is underway, and the  fountain to the north gives a sense of flow and peace. To the west is the  Garden of Duke Nhoukym, and to the east is the Garden of Lady Maltesa. } {songpalace} {} {road} {} {1.000} {}
