R {47530} {0} {<278>} {West wing} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  There are many doors along the hallway of the west wing of the manor. One  wooden door to the north is slightly ajar and a wisp of smoke emerges from  the room within, carrying with it the scent of tobacco. There is a large set  of double doors in the south wall that catches your attention and is probably worth a closer look. At the far end of the hallway is a single door that has  carvings of roses in the panelling. Large chandeliers light up the wing with  hundreds of candles, which are never allowed to burn out. Small tables  adorned with vases and figurines are placed between the doors along the walls. Paintings and tapestries adorn the walls above the small tables and their artwork. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
