R {47535} {0} {<278>} {Dining room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The dining room is quite extravagant, with a long table capable of seating  thirty dinner guests, as the centre of attraction. The wall panelling is dark brown, which has recently been polished. The windows are slightly open which  lets in a gentle breeze that barely rustles the curtains. A very large  portrait hangs over the fireplace on the west wall and vases of flowers are  sitting on pedestals between the windows. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {47538} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47536} {0} {<278>} {Ballroom} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The ballroom is quite large, with long frosted glass windows along the walls. Outside the windows some white swans are swimming on a pond which is  surrounded by tulips. Looking up at the ceiling of the ballroom, you can see  some floating chandeliers drifting slowly along, which twinkle like starlight in the evening. There is a raised platform to one side of the room where  musicians gather during events to provide the music for dancing. Potted  plants and colourful flowers decorate the small niches along the walls,  adding vibrancy to the room. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {47538} {w} {open w;w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47537} {0} {<278>} {Trophy room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  As you walk into this room you see a group of animals ready to attack. Along  one wall are animal heads mounted on plaques and displayed as prized kills. In one corner is a statue of full plate mail armour with a sword and a shield hung on the wall behind it. On the wall beside the door are shelves with  various trophies from archery and sword fighting competitions. There are two  comfortable chairs by the window with a small table between them. On the  table is a decanter filled with brandy and two crystal goblets. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {47538} {n} {open n;n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47538} {0} {<278>} {East wing} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The east wing of the manor has many doors along its length. To the north,  halfway along the hallway, double doors with glass panels show the room  within. A little further along is a door in the south wall with a large iron  lock. Considering the wealth on display in the manor, there must be treasured items within. At the far end of the east wing are highly ornate double doors  with frosted glass panelling. There are many niches in the walls, which  display antiques from all over Andolor. Vases of flowers are seated on highly polished wooden pedestals, and tapestries and paintings adorn the walls along the entire length of the hallway. Large chandeliers light up the wing with  hundreds of candles. } {aardington} {Key in desk at 47533} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
