R {47548} {0} {<278>} {Guest room} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A large, comfortable bed has been freshly made up and a couple of vases of  flowers adorn the dresser, their delicate perfume filling the room. A pair of matching travel bags sits next to the bed, ready to be unpacked into the  dresser that rests against the wall. A fire crackles in the fireplace,  warming the room comfortably for the new guest. Through the windows you can  see a well-manicured hedge maze next to a grove of apple trees. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {47546} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47549} {0} {<278>} {Bathroom} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  A large marble bathtub is the dominant feature in this room. It is big enough to easily accommodate the mightiest of men with room to spare. The floor is  made of marble as are the washbasins near the windows, which have a wonderful view over the kitchen gardens to the north. Brass towel racks hold thick,  fluffy white towels which are cleaned every day. A large hamper sits beside  the towel racks for all the used towels. A cupboard houses a pump which is  used to both fill and empty the water from the tub and basins. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
E {47539} {s} {open s;s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47550} {0} {<278>} {Attic} {<278>[ ]<088>} {  The attic is dimly lit with only small windows to let in the light during the day. It is a very long and large room, as it spans over a good portion of the manor proper. Old wardrobes hold clothes which are centuries old and are  quite fragile. Trunks and chests contain all manner of treasures and junk  which have long since been forgotten. White cloths, now grey with dust, cover disused pieces of furniture. Spider webs cling to boxes and rat droppings  litter the floor. The attic continues to the east and a set of wooden stairs  lead back down to the store room. } {aardington} {} {inside} {} {1.000} {}
