R {47578} {0} {<238>} {The hayloft} {<238># #<088>} {  This is a large hayloft where most of the hay is stored. Off to one side  there is some bedding where the stable hands sleep at night, so they can take turns to keep a watchful eye on the Earl's prized pets. From this vantage  point you can see into every stall, all of which are filled with fresh hay. The smell of the animals is rather cloying up here as the stables are kept  heated for the comfort of the animals. } {aardington} {} {cabin} {} {1.000} {}
E {47577} {d} {d} {32} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47579} {0} {<238>} {The carriage house} {<238># #<088>} {  Inside this building there are wagons and carts of different sizes that have  all sorts of uses, from carting hay to transporting the Earl and his family  when he leaves the grounds of the estate. A large, long wooden trestle table  occupies a space off to one side and acts as a work bench. The table is  covered with tools and supplies to keep the estates' transport in excellent  condition. There are harnesses and leather straps hanging on racks, freshly  oiled and waiting to be put to use. } {aardington} {} {cabin} {pk} {1.000} {}
