R {47584} {0} {<178>} {A beautiful garden} {<168>*<158>*<138>*<088>} {  This beautiful garden is very well tended by loving hands. Wild daffodils  grow along the rocky garden edge, their bright yellow petals, with the  trumpet-like centre piece, a delight to the local bees and butterflies. A  bush, with long stems covered in hundreds of tiny purple flowers, sits to the rear of the garden. The variety of plants and the colours of the flowers are  quite wondrous. There are some wooden benches placed at intervals on the  green grass and against the wall of the temple, giving you an opportunity to  sit in the sun and enjoy the sensory delights of the garden. } {aardington} {} {flowers1} {} {1.000} {}
E {47583} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {47585} {0} {<178>} {A beautiful garden} {<168>*<158>*<138>*<088>} {  There is a small, bubbling spring, amongst the many flowering plants, that  tinkles quietly. River stones have been brought in to make the spring more of a feature in the garden, as well as giving water to the plants. The stones  have also formed a shallow bowl, which the birds like to ruffle their  feathers in. Some insects have taken advantage of the water, laying their  eggs in the calmer areas. Flowering shrubs offer food and shelter to the  local wildlife as well as decorating the garden with their unique flowers. } {aardington} {} {flowers1} {} {1.000} {}
