R {47586} {0} {<178>} {A beautiful garden} {<168>*<158>*<138>*<088>} {  There are some of the most beautiful roses you have ever seen in this part of the garden. Each rose bush has a different colour and type of rose, so each  one is distinctly unique. Under each rose bush is a bronze plaque, attached  to a mottled grey marble stone. On each plaque is a name, a few words, a  birth and death date. The rose bushes make up a semi-circle at the end of the white stone path, which is edged with a low, green leafy hedge. While it is  encouraged to look and reflect upon these stones, you are not invited to take a closer look. } {aardington} {} {flowers1} {} {1.000} {}
