R {50635} {0} {<278>} {Western Temple Road} {<278>. .<088>} {  The exteriors of the dark elves' stalagmite structures are tastefully  decorated with precious stones. Since black is the most prized color of dark  elves, the buildings are mainly decorated with black diamonds and beads of  shimmering black tourmaline. These gemstones are for more than just  decorative purposes, however. The dark elves know of ways to store protective magical spells inside of them. The gemstones act as wards around the  buildings that they protect, calling up earth golems and expelling poisonous  attacks if an intruder happens to try to enter the stalagmite tower. The  interiors of these towers must look just as exotic and beautiful as their  exteriors, but it would be a suicidal maneuver to attempt to enter one. } {uprising} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E {42154} {n} {n} {1} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {42153} {s} {s} {4} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {50636} {0} {<278>} {Northern Temple Road} {<278>. .<088>} {  This is a continuation of where the dark elves' trading market once stood. Several upended carts lie sprawled along the road, making traveling through  here a tiresome adventure. It looks like one of the carts must have been  selling clothing, because torn up bits of cloth litter the roadway, along  with the bits of wood and metal. Any clothes that made it through the  disaster unscathed have definitely been snatched up by now by greedy hands. The streets are so quiet, it is almost eery. Imagining how full of life this  street must have been before disaster struck this city, is a bit saddening. Burned-out husks of buildings stand, partially collapsed, to the north and  the south. To the east and west, extend the remains of the dark elves'  marketplace. } {uprising} {} {city} {} {1.000} {}
E {42155} {e} {e} {2} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}
E {42154} {w} {w} {8} {0} {} {1.000} {} {0.00}

R {50639} {0} {<118>} {In the Dark Lady's Realm} {<118>. .<088>} {  What you are now standing on appears to be a gigantic slab of black marble  that is floating in the middle of black space. This stone surface continues  onward to the north, but drops off sharply to the south. There isn't a hint  of ground below the drop-off, so jumping off the edge would be a bad idea. To the north, there is a wisp of a dark figure standing at what must be a  tall, white throne. Any other direction just leads to an edge of the marble  slab, so the only sensible way to travel is to the north. But if that figure  is the Dark Lady, how will she treat you when you meet her? She must have  been the one who summoned you here, so you'd better take a deep breath, and  move to meet her. } {uprising} {} {redcarpet} {} {1.000} {}
