R {55582} {0} {<118>} {An Intriguing Foyer} {<118>[ ]<088>} {  The first thought that crosses your mind is "WOW, what a dump." For what  should've been this home's first impression, it has not set a great one. The  hardwood floorboards are half rotted, decayed, and frankly, in some cases,  missing entirely. As you focus on each step, making sure you don't end up in  the basement, you smash your head on what's left of the chandelier. Crying  out in pain, you close your eyes tight, yelling out obscenities. When you  open your eyes you spin around. Now there is no chandelier\; well, there  is, but it is back up on the ceiling. Intact, it cascades a brilliant  flickering light from its crystals, illuminating the foyer. There is an  influx of activity as servants move to and fro, heading towards the kitchen  to the west and the halls to the east. The walls are in pristine condition  with beautiful works of art hanging upon them. As you continue to look around taking in the room, one of the servants walks right through you. The moment  their ethereal form is no longer blocking your vision, the foyer is back  to being crap. You can see the den ahead though, for some reason you feel as  if you cannot progress towards it. Perhaps the hall to the east would be more accepting of exploration. You nearly trip as you forget to check if the floor is still under you. As you regain your footing, you watch as a purple and  green spider the size of a mouse crawls over and climbs up the leg of a  beautiful woman and settles on the back of her knuckles. Behind her is a  large man in a black hoodie. While setting the spider down on a dusty shelf,  she says, "Welcome to the House of Krazees, Welcome Home.".  } {manor3} {} {bloodyroom} {safe} {1.000} {}
